ments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T19:59:12Z","email":"116077423+AbdullahHAK@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Abdullah"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T19:59:12Z","email":"116077423+AbdullahHAK@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Abdullah"},"message":"Redesign visual language to match hynts.in''s premium SaaS look\n\nRebuilds the theme around what actually makes hynts read as premium\n(inspected their live CSS/markup directly, not guessed): a neutral\nnear-black/white base rather than a color-tinted one, with a single\npurple accent used sparingly - a gradient-text headline word, buttons,\nactive states - instead of saturating every surface. Adds Lexend\n(their primary UI font), a real landing-page hero on the homepage\n(status badge, big headline, subtext, pill CTA scrolling to #jobs),\nand a consistent radius/shadow token scale (--radius-sm/lg/xl,\n--shadow-sm/md/lg/glow) applied across every card and button for a\ncohesive soft-shadow, rounded-corner feel instead of the flatter,\nmore uniform styling from the previous pass.\n\nAlso fixes a real mobile overflow bug caught by actually screenshotting\nthe pages headlessly: .hero-badge is an inline-flex element whose text\nruns become separate anonymous flex items, so the default\nflex-wrap:nowrap let it grow past the viewport on narrow screens\ninstead of wrapping. Fixed with flex-wrap:wrap + max-width:100%, plus\noverflow-x:hidden on body as a defensive backstop.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2f2b20e7b71f93f83750b755c9a7af24e9a2b111","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AbdullahHAK/jobless/git/trees/2f2b20e7b71f93f83750b755c9a7af24e9a2b111"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AbdullahHAK/jobless/git/commits/9ee4114f6edea71af6b44e98f1fceac681e4c210","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116077423?v=4","events_u