nts_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Obed-Ababio/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Obed-Ababio/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Obed-Ababio/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Obed-Ababio/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Obed-Ababio","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Obed-Ababio/sankofa-ehr/commits/eb484c4cde2bf96b499938e812dd57d0d012cd22/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T02:55:10Z","email":"ababioobed98@gmail.com","name":"Obed Ababio"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T02:55:10Z","email":"ababioobed98@gmail.com","name":"Obed Ababio"},"message":"fix(security): close FHIR R4 privilege bypass — upgrade fhir2 to 2.5.1 (CVE-2025-46823)\n\nThe refapp-bundled fhir2 2.0.0 does not always enforce OpenMRS privileges\n(GHSA-g5vq-w8v2-4x9j, critical): Front Desk, denied clinical reads on REST,\ncould still read Observations via /ws/fhir2/R4. The distro build now swaps\nin fhir2 2.5.1 (patched 2.x line for platform 2.4.1+; core here is 2.6.4)\nthe same way it swaps Initializer.\n\nVerified live: frontdesk denied FHIR Observation/Encounter (\"Privileges\nrequired\") while keeping FHIR Patient lookup; clinician unaffected. The\ndenial surfaces as HTTP 500 + OperationOutcome rather than 403 — no leak,\ntracked as an upstream nicety.\n\nroles.spec.ts: test.fixme becomes a real assertion pinning the denial so a\nbase-distro bump can''t reintroduce the vulnerable version. Two users in one\nPlaywright test need separate request contexts — the shared fixture''s cookie\njar replays the first user''s JSESSIONID, which OpenMRS prefers over Basic\nauth. Suite green: 12 passed, 0 fixme.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UYShKeRjPgU5eCMCQ6FMYP","tree":{"sha":"b31e4c5be0669351605bbcbfcbd07debee539375","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Obed-Ababio/sankofa-ehr/git/trees/b31e4