/users/FullStackChef/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FullStackChef","id":28607748,"login":"FullStackChef","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4NjA3NzQ4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commits/8f8181ccaeb9cf14c48f65c68bb889a62f9a8113/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-02T08:34:19Z","email":"brett@fieldstate.io","name":"Brett Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-02T08:34:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor(c4-ui): fold canvas-c4 into c4-ui — one shared engine, one C4 surface (ADR I) (#129)\n\nOwner ruling: the studio surface is what enterprise consumes — an\nintermediate C4-semantics package with a single sibling consumer is\nindirection without a customer. canvas-c4 (never published) is deleted;\nits projection, card chrome, C4CanvasHost, layout composition, styles,\nand all 65 tests move into c4-ui/src/c4/ via git mv, and c4-ui''s index\nexports the full C4 API. @workspec/canvas remains the one shared engine\npackage from the extraction.\n\nZero behavior change, proven: all 12 parity goldens byte-untouched;\ncompiled styles.css structurally identical (49/49 theme vars, .c4-el\nrules byte-equal, drops are duplicates from the old standalone compile);\nexport surface conserved name-by-name (33 values + 20 types); test\ntitles conserved 201->199 via audit consolidation with union\nenforcement (net tightening — spec-defaults re-export lost its\nexemption). release.yml drops to 9 bootstrap names; RELEASING.md\ndangling-tarball note re-verified by real packs. ADR B superseded by\nADR I; S6 spike doc gains a consumption-model correction preamble.\n\nAdversarially reviewed (fold-completeness + docs/release lenses):\nzero blocking findings. Gates: c4-ui 199, canvas 170, c4-layout 20\n(golden intact), c4-studio 127, site 41 + build, mf-host smoke,\nparity 12/12, root build/typecheck/test exit 0.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"04a1acd29528ba1c44202ac6f17d2b92a7ecb0aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/git/trees/04a1acd29528ba1c44202ac6f17d2b92a7ecb0aa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/git/commits/8f8181ccaeb9cf14c48f65c68bb889a62f9a8113","verification":{"payload":"tree 04a1acd29528ba1c44202ac6f17d2b92a7ecb0aa\nparent adee75247d1de9be5409a91ae4dfc624bb99d858\nauthor Brett Smith <brett@fieldstate.io> 1785659659 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785659659 +1200\n\nrefactor(c4-ui): fold canvas-c4 into c4-ui — one shared engine, one C4 surface (ADR I) (#129)\n\nOwner ruling: the studio surface is what enterprise consumes — an\nintermediate C4-semantics package with a single sibling consumer is\nindirection without a customer. canvas-c4 (never published) is deleted;\nits projection, card chrome, C4CanvasHost, layout composition, styles,\nand all 65 tests move into c4-ui/src/c4/ via git mv, and c4-ui''s index\nexports the full C4 API. @workspec/canvas remains the one shared engine\npackage from the extraction.\n\nZero behavior change, proven: all 12 parity goldens byte-untouched;\ncompiled styles.css structurally identical (49/49 theme vars, .c4-el\nrules byte-equal, drops are duplicates from the old standalone compile);\nexport surface conserved name-by-name (33 values + 20 types); test\ntitles conserved 201->199 via audit consolidation with union\nenforcement (net tightening — spec-defaults re-export lost its\nexemption). release.yml drops to 9 bootstrap names; RELEASING.md\ndangling-tarball note re-verified by real packs. ADR B superseded by\nADR I; S6 spike doc gains a consumption-model correction preamble.\n\nAdversarially reviewed (fold-completeness + docs/release lenses):\nzero blocking findings. Gates: c4-ui 199, canvas 170, c4-layout 20\n(golden intact), c4-studio 127, site 41 + build, mf-host smoke,\nparity 12/12, root build/typecheck/test exit 0.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqbwELCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAcFgQAAgvDfjCK4OScl/9G4oJPY7A\n9E1yXx5HhLmyYKScHom+Coz0+/A6DscPS0qsuwsml04UW5QsV88g9hgbTdOA/MKT\nOA4OCITlxJwoNe9/8B7akxsa/lJcnEKv+xqJbEZaistOaEyU2rZ3bIv3jCcBQ7mm\nHUiDBQguK6KfqdMcDKhv6x0MuJ89jgpEK2LVtJmGtPwZuE8nriozgCsXyL1dycwo\nBKCiOaeDvWkoEU/21evWzvk/fC49hpH/btThrS0m37dtC0Kl9CywAm2U6+x1emZt\nKFHTs7p13It0/mDJziXCjpE6uJUxQYdFw7xeKUX9yvyX71oKOeaAs+P1aMUwXBdG\nST4DZ6AiVmSlJlc9VrJknio3+9h0xN2DlXycO4aR/2gTYooenMx402iVTPyknIYJ\niFEL/vzA7XMCoZcXWGiQuNl5gBywcUEHtFneBsio/PcSeVrkSYNdDQuUrlaw8DlC\ndKpN6kmaBQ76iC4kJ6Ah3mY1qyOSWmIwsYSJ1c37KaTAjlSLanCGH53VtmfPNP4h\neJBKaJIL6R9mghjpx6LLeIwhYG4teQPwsHRqwt8iH5uLax3cD7nCTkCracIY7hrY\nB9P7Mi5bRbCi2zCRvIAotY+fGcGKwCQwVukzpllFcX9cRAwbJnZJXZLH31McT6FS\nlco8SZgvBKoI+HPCNAzk\n=VJyY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-02T08:34:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commit/8f8181ccaeb9cf14c48f65c68bb889a62f9a8113","node_id":"C_kwDOTPvB8toAKDhmODE4MWNjYWViOWNmMTRjNDhmNjVjNjhiYjg4OWE2MmY5YTgxMTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commit/adee75247d1de9be5409a91ae4dfc624bb99d858","sha":"adee75247d1de9be5409a91ae4dfc624bb99d858","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commits/adee75247d1de9be5409a91ae4dfc624bb99d858"}],"sha":"8f8181ccaeb9cf14c48f65c68bb889a62f9a8113","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commits/8f8181ccaeb9cf14c48f65c68bb889a62f9a8113"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28607748?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FullStackChef","id":28607748,"login":"FullStackChef","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4NjA3NzQ4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commits/adee75247d1de9be5409a91ae4dfc624bb99d858/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-02T05:19:35Z","email":"brett@fieldstate.io","name":"Brett Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-02T05:19:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(canvas)!: canvas family — enterprise canvas as shared OSS packages + C4 studio parity (#128)\n\n* docs(canvas): D0 — record extraction decisions A–H + sequencing as ADRs (#123)\n\nNine markdown ADRs under docs/canvas/decisions/ following the tech-spec §6\nformat rule (prose ADR branch — constraint-driven calls, no graded cost\ncomparison). Content sourced from epic #116.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(canvas): S1 — @workspec/canvas engine core (store factory, hooks, utils) (#117)\n\nPorts the enterprise canvas engine core into a new OSS package:\n- zustand v5 vanilla-store factory + <CanvasProvider>; useCanvasStore(selector)\n  keeps the exact enterprise call signature (contract-tested two-instance isolation)\n- types split (enterprise-only fields excluded), open Shape model groundwork\n- Canvas with self-measured viewport seam (zero window/document globals,\n  enforced by a source-scan test); camera/pointer/keyboard wiring in an\n  inner component beneath the viewport provider\n- hooks: camera, pointer-events (instance tool registry), keyboard,\n  hover (instance-scoped), text-editing, image-input\n- utils: geometry, transforms, history, hit-test (consolidated, z-order\n  pinned by tests), align-distribute, fractional-index, ids, lens,\n  sticky-defaults, containers (kindOfShape -> injected kindResolver)\n- persistence opt-in via persistenceKey (default off), zod-gated load\n- strictness pilot (store + SelectTool): ~5 mechanical fixes/100 LOC, no\n  behavioral rewrites\n\nAdversarially reviewed (3 lenses + skeptic verification): 2 blocking\nfindings fixed with mutation-verified tests (viewport provider wiring,\nhit-test ordering); zod gate, dispose(), and flaky-conditional test\nholes closed. S2 debt logged on #118.\n\n89 tests green; build/typecheck/lint clean on node 22.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(canvas): S2 — shapes, tools, chrome, open registry, token audit (#118)\n\nPorts the enterprise interaction + rendering surface into @workspec/canvas:\n- open ShapeModule registry with six opt-in ShapeUtil capabilities replacing\n  enterprise hard-coded per-type lists (selfRendersSelection, isConnectable,\n  connectorKey, isGroupContainer, containerTitle, isContextMenuSurface)\n- shapes: sticky family (both lens faces, promote/demote, content blocks,\n  media notes), text, draw (RDP + Chaikin), image, and the full connector\n  family — orthogonal router ported verbatim (committed route snapshot:\n  fans incl. dy-dominant, reversed directions, self-loop, detours, clamping)\n- tools: hand/draw/text/sticky/connector/place + registerWhiteboard()\n- chrome: Shape, ShapeLayer (container-rect culling), SelectionLayer\n  (capability-driven), Background, MarqueeBox, ZoomControls, Minimap\n  (injected kind colors), ContextMenu (host-bridged), Toolbar + vendored\n  tooltip/kbd; <Canvas> renders the enterprise default stack when childless\n- keyboard scoping API: shortcutScope window|root|none (window = enterprise\n  parity; root = focus-scoped for multi-canvas; space-pan clears on blur)\n- CSS: canvas keyframes, .c4-conn derivation with literal +22% dark lift,\n  enterprise #64748b fallback via documented local token\n- token-audit test: every var(--*) read resolves from @workspec/design or\n  the documented exemption files; zero color literals elsewhere\n- all six S1-review debt items resolved (ledgered on #118)\n\nAdversarially reviewed (3 lenses, 8 mutation probes) + fix round: router\nsnapshot gaps (fan-redirect, dx<0, self-loop) pinned with mutation\nevidence; pointer-hook contracts completed; CSS fallback drift declared.\n\n152 tests green; build/typecheck/lint clean on node 22.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(canvas): S3 — @workspec/canvas-c4 C4 layer + capability-driven routing (#119)\n\nNew @workspec/canvas-c4 package — C4 semantics as a layer on the canvas:\n- buildC4Shapes: verbatim port of the enterprise projection (lens\n  partition, lane-offset/fan precompute, z-banding, boundary bbox math,\n  meta.ephemeral protocol, fitCamera 1x cap) over studio ResolvedDiagram;\n  validationErrors/artifactRefId/elementSlug carried via the C4NodeMeta\n  protocol; meta.dimmed kept as a host-settable spotlight hook (matches\n  enterprise history: set in 14c4b5c9, removed in d783789e)\n- c4node/c4boundary chrome byte-matched to enterprise (accent borders,\n  eyebrow/title/description metrics, DRAFT chip at Tailwind-v4-correct\n  4px radius, rework halo, watermark, cylinder/hexagon silhouettes),\n  pinned by source-literal chrome-metrics tests until the S4 parity\n  harness takes over\n- C4CanvasHost extends CanvasHost: full 12-method enterprise bridge,\n  all optional, optimistic-local-first fallback contract-tested\n- decision-A composition: elk positions via injectable C4LayoutFn\n  (elkC4Layout default over @workspec/c4-layout); node dims imported\n  from c4-layout so renderer/layout drift is impossible; .layout edge\n  waypoints advisory\n- style reconciliation: spec-defaults.ts canonical here (c4-ui copy\n  retires in S4); .c4-el derivation on shared --el-tint-* tokens,\n  dark-theme literals source-pinned\n\n@workspec/canvas: routing membership now capability-driven\n(routedEdges/isRouteObstacle with legacy name-set fallback, route\nsnapshot byte-identical) + S2-debt tests (connector label-edit commits,\nsticky promote/demote, minimap kind colors) + EdgeLabelEditor escape fix.\n\nAdversarially reviewed (3 lenses, 10 mutation probes, skeptic\nverification: 4 confirmed blockers fixed with mutation evidence, 1\nfalse blocker refuted). canvas-c4: 59 tests; canvas: 167 tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(c4-ui)!: S4 — facade swap onto canvas/canvas-c4, renderSvg on shared geometry, parity harness (#120)\n\n@workspec/c4-ui recomposed on @workspec/canvas + @workspec/canvas-c4,\nexternally props-compatible (28 contract tests preserved through the real\nengine pointer pipeline). Facade tool keeps the shipped interaction\ncontract (background drag pans; drag-to-pin never activates); a11y wrapper\nadds screen-reader click activation; selection controlled by\nselectedNodeId; drag-commit rides serializeForWrite with the lens-merge\ncontract now mutation-pinned. C4Explorer unchanged except label-aware\nspacing wiring. spec-defaults retired to canvas-c4 re-export; one\ncomposed stylesheet. MF remote react singleton widened to ^18.3||^19.\n\nrenderSvg: edges via the shared orthogonal router (face-aligned inline\narrowheads, lane fan-out, detours); all colors resolved to literals\n(standalone SVGs contain zero var() reads); CodeQL js/html-constructed-\nfrom-input #1-#3 sinks sanitized with hostile-input regressions.\n\nLayout: label-aware layer spacing at the composition seam\n(labelAwareLayerSpacing = enterprise ranksep formula) via additive\nc4-layout layerSpacing option — defaults untouched, golden layout\nsnapshot byte-identical. Projection respects pinned node sizes (edges\nanchor on the actual card face). Pinned-size + label-clearance +\nlens-merge contracts all mutation-verified.\n\napps/parity (private): Playwright golden harness — 12 committed goldens\n(cards/edges/boundary/system-context/container-lens/grid x light+dark,\nhover/selection/drafted/reworking states seeded), deterministic fonts,\nstale-dist guard, out of root test recursion (darwin-local lane; CI\nstory ledgered on #121). Comparison sheet vs enterprise references\ndelivered; references are April-era, port tracks enterprise HEAD chrome.\n\nBREAKING (alpha): stretch preserveAspectRatio model replaced by the\nenterprise camera (no distortion, zoom 0.1-4); see c4-ui CHANGELOG.\n\nAdversarially reviewed (3 lenses, 12 mutation probes, 10 agents): 6\nblockers fixed with mutation evidence. Family gates: canvas 170,\ncanvas-c4 65, c4-layout 20, c4-ui 135, c4-studio 127; mf-host smoke +\nparity 12/12 green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(canvas): S6 — enterprise re-adoption spike report + draft diff (#122)\n\nVerdict: enterprise adopts @workspec/canvas + @workspec/canvas-c4 without\nforking — zero required package changes, three recommended (filed as a\nfollow-up issue). All 18 external useCanvasStore sites survive an 89-line\nsingleton shim; every enterprise shape re-registers with zero capability\ngaps; the 12-method bridge maps 1:1 onto C4CanvasHost; sync/atlas contract\nsurface verified matching. Adoption shrinks the enterprise canvas\n(-735/+510). Node-kind ledger answered: six kinds need spec-default\nentries; participant is dead data. Estimated effort ~1-1.5 dev-weeks,\ngated on the S5 publish. Static verification only (packages unpublished).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(release): S5 — publish prep, site wire-up, docs, audit hardening (#121)\n\n- release.yml: canvas + canvas-c4 inserted in dependency order; defuses two\n  pre-existing landmines by also wiring mcp-core (every *-studio deps it;\n  absent from the registry — next tag would have published uninstallable\n  studios) and the seven topology-* packages. RELEASING.md family table +\n  not-yet-bootstrapped callout (10 names) + bootstrap-and-tag-in-one-\n  sitting warning.\n- c4 family staged at 0.1.0-alpha.6 (c4-layout layerSpacing + c4-model\n  CodeQL fix are load-bearing for the recomposed c4-ui); canvas +\n  canvas-c4 at 0.1.0-alpha.1.\n- apps/site: c4-* flipped to workspace devDeps per the cost/pages.yml\n  precedent (LOUD_NOTICE + tsconfig references + drift-log entry 20\n  retire runbook); /c4/demo renders the recomposed stack.\n- Parity local-only lane: root pnpm run parity(:update), README section,\n  CI guard comments (darwin-only goldens).\n- Token-audit hardening: full CSS Color 4 named-colour set + background\n  shorthand in canvas; complete scan mirrored into canvas-c4; sticky\n  cross-product derived from StickyColor. shared-modules invariant\n  strengthened to call-site verification.\n- READMEs completed to the normative contracts (CanvasHost 7-method,\n  capabilities incl. routing, meta protocol split, camera model);\n  c4-ui styles.css dead SVG-era rules pruned.\n\nAdversarially reviewed (release-correctness + gates lenses): zero\nblocking; array order, 10-name bootstrap list, tarball dep rewriting,\nand site deploy independently verified. Full monorepo build/typecheck/\ntest green on node 22.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"44f7a9a425fec7d983cdfee93f239a0f3b848cd8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/git/trees/44f7a9a425fec7d983cdfee93f239a0f3b848cd8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/git/commits/adee75247d1de9be5409a91ae4dfc624bb99d858","verification":{"payload":"tree 44f7a9a425fec7d983cdfee93f239a0f3b848cd8\nparent 541e561c9a12df7352c738f097c19377db808b99\nauthor Brett Smith <brett@fieldstate.io> 1785647975 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785647975 +1200\n\nfeat(canvas)!: canvas family — enterprise canvas as shared OSS packages + C4 studio parity (#128)\n\n* docs(canvas): D0 — record extraction decisions A–H + sequencing as ADRs (#123)\n\nNine markdown ADRs under docs/canvas/decisions/ following the tech-spec §6\nformat rule (prose ADR branch — constraint-driven calls, no graded cost\ncomparison). Content sourced from epic #116.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(canvas): S1 — @workspec/canvas engine core (store factory, hooks, utils) (#117)\n\nPorts the enterprise canvas engine core into a new OSS package:\n- zustand v5 vanilla-store factory + <CanvasProvider>; useCanvasStore(selector)\n  keeps the exact enterprise call signature (contract-tested two-instance isolation)\n- types split (enterprise-only fields excluded), open Shape model groundwork\n- Canvas with self-measured viewport seam (zero window/document globals,\n  enforced by a source-scan test); camera/pointer/keyboard wiring in an\n  inner component beneath the viewport provider\n- hooks: camera, pointer-events (instance tool registry), keyboard,\n  hover (instance-scoped), text-editing, image-input\n- utils: geometry, transforms, history, hit-test (consolidated, z-order\n  pinned by tests), align-distribute, fractional-index, ids, lens,\n  sticky-defaults, containers (kindOfShape -> injected kindResolver)\n- persistence opt-in via persistenceKey (default off), zod-gated load\n- strictness pilot (store + SelectTool): ~5 mechanical fixes/100 LOC, no\n  behavioral rewrites\n\nAdversarially reviewed (3 lenses + skeptic verification): 2 blocking\nfindings fixed with mutation-verified tests (viewport provider wiring,\nhit-test ordering); zod gate, dispose(), and flaky-conditional test\nholes closed. S2 debt logged on #118.\n\n89 tests green; build/typecheck/lint clean on node 22.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(canvas): S2 — shapes, tools, chrome, open registry, token audit (#118)\n\nPorts the enterprise interaction + rendering surface into @workspec/canvas:\n- open ShapeModule registry with six opt-in ShapeUtil capabilities replacing\n  enterprise hard-coded per-type lists (selfRendersSelection, isConnectable,\n  connectorKey, isGroupContainer, containerTitle, isContextMenuSurface)\n- shapes: sticky family (both lens faces, promote/demote, content blocks,\n  media notes), text, draw (RDP + Chaikin), image, and the full connector\n  family — orthogonal router ported verbatim (committed route snapshot:\n  fans incl. dy-dominant, reversed directions, self-loop, detours, clamping)\n- tools: hand/draw/text/sticky/connector/place + registerWhiteboard()\n- chrome: Shape, ShapeLayer (container-rect culling), SelectionLayer\n  (capability-driven), Background, MarqueeBox, ZoomControls, Minimap\n  (injected kind colors), ContextMenu (host-bridged), Toolbar + vendored\n  tooltip/kbd; <Canvas> renders the enterprise default stack when childless\n- keyboard scoping API: shortcutScope window|root|none (window = enterprise\n  parity; root = focus-scoped for multi-canvas; space-pan clears on blur)\n- CSS: canvas keyframes, .c4-conn derivation with literal +22% dark lift,\n  enterprise #64748b fallback via documented local token\n- token-audit test: every var(--*) read resolves from @workspec/design or\n  the documented exemption files; zero color literals elsewhere\n- all six S1-review debt items resolved (ledgered on #118)\n\nAdversarially reviewed (3 lenses, 8 mutation probes) + fix round: router\nsnapshot gaps (fan-redirect, dx<0, self-loop) pinned with mutation\nevidence; pointer-hook contracts completed; CSS fallback drift declared.\n\n152 tests green; build/typecheck/lint clean on node 22.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(canvas): S3 — @workspec/canvas-c4 C4 layer + capability-driven routing (#119)\n\nNew @workspec/canvas-c4 package — C4 semantics as a layer on the canvas:\n- buildC4Shapes: verbatim port of the enterprise projection (lens\n  partition, lane-offset/fan precompute, z-banding, boundary bbox math,\n  meta.ephemeral protocol, fitCamera 1x cap) over studio ResolvedDiagram;\n  validationErrors/artifactRefId/elementSlug carried via the C4NodeMeta\n  protocol; meta.dimmed kept as a host-settable spotlight hook (matches\n  enterprise history: set in 14c4b5c9, removed in d783789e)\n- c4node/c4boundary chrome byte-matched to enterprise (accent borders,\n  eyebrow/title/description metrics, DRAFT chip at Tailwind-v4-correct\n  4px radius, rework halo, watermark, cylinder/hexagon silhouettes),\n  pinned by source-literal chrome-metrics tests until the S4 parity\n  harness takes over\n- C4CanvasHost extends CanvasHost: full 12-method enterprise bridge,\n  all optional, optimistic-local-first fallback contract-tested\n- decision-A composition: elk positions via injectable C4LayoutFn\n  (elkC4Layout default over @workspec/c4-layout); node dims imported\n  from c4-layout so renderer/layout drift is impossible; .layout edge\n  waypoints advisory\n- style reconciliation: spec-defaults.ts canonical here (c4-ui copy\n  retires in S4); .c4-el derivation on shared --el-tint-* tokens,\n  dark-theme literals source-pinned\n\n@workspec/canvas: routing membership now capability-driven\n(routedEdges/isRouteObstacle with legacy name-set fallback, route\nsnapshot byte-identical) + S2-debt tests (connector label-edit commits,\nsticky promote/demote, minimap kind colors) + EdgeLabelEditor escape fix.\n\nAdversarially reviewed (3 lenses, 10 mutation probes, skeptic\nverification: 4 confirmed blockers fixed with mutation evidence, 1\nfalse blocker refuted). canvas-c4: 59 tests; canvas: 167 tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(c4-ui)!: S4 — facade swap onto canvas/canvas-c4, renderSvg on shared geometry, parity harness (#120)\n\n@workspec/c4-ui recomposed on @workspec/canvas + @workspec/canvas-c4,\nexternally props-compatible (28 contract tests preserved through the real\nengine pointer pipeline). Facade tool keeps the shipped interaction\ncontract (background drag pans; drag-to-pin never activates); a11y wrapper\nadds screen-reader click activation; selection controlled by\nselectedNodeId; drag-commit rides serializeForWrite with the lens-merge\ncontract now mutation-pinned. C4Explorer unchanged except label-aware\nspacing wiring. spec-defaults retired to canvas-c4 re-export; one\ncomposed stylesheet. MF remote react singleton widened to ^18.3||^19.\n\nrenderSvg: edges via the shared orthogonal router (face-aligned inline\narrowheads, lane fan-out, detours); all colors resolved to literals\n(standalone SVGs contain zero var() reads); CodeQL js/html-constructed-\nfrom-input #1-#3 sinks sanitized with hostile-input regressions.\n\nLayout: label-aware layer spacing at the composition seam\n(labelAwareLayerSpacing = enterprise ranksep formula) via additive\nc4-layout layerSpacing option — defaults untouched, golden layout\nsnapshot byte-identical. Projection respects pinned node sizes (edges\nanchor on the actual card face). Pinned-size + label-clearance +\nlens-merge contracts all mutation-verified.\n\napps/parity (private): Playwright golden harness — 12 committed goldens\n(cards/edges/boundary/system-context/container-lens/grid x light+dark,\nhover/selection/drafted/reworking states seeded), deterministic fonts,\nstale-dist guard, out of root test recursion (darwin-local lane; CI\nstory ledgered on #121). Comparison sheet vs enterprise references\ndelivered; references are April-era, port tracks enterprise HEAD chrome.\n\nBREAKING (alpha): stretch preserveAspectRatio model replaced by the\nenterprise camera (no distortion, zoom 0.1-4); see c4-ui CHANGELOG.\n\nAdversarially reviewed (3 lenses, 12 mutation probes, 10 agents): 6\nblockers fixed with mutation evidence. Family gates: canvas 170,\ncanvas-c4 65, c4-layout 20, c4-ui 135, c4-studio 127; mf-host smoke +\nparity 12/12 green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(canvas): S6 — enterprise re-adoption spike report + draft diff (#122)\n\nVerdict: enterprise adopts @workspec/canvas + @workspec/canvas-c4 without\nforking — zero required package changes, three recommended (filed as a\nfollow-up issue). All 18 external useCanvasStore sites survive an 89-line\nsingleton shim; every enterprise shape re-registers with zero capability\ngaps; the 12-method bridge maps 1:1 onto C4CanvasHost; sync/atlas contract\nsurface verified matching. Adoption shrinks the enterprise canvas\n(-735/+510). Node-kind ledger answered: six kinds need spec-default\nentries; participant is dead data. Estimated effort ~1-1.5 dev-weeks,\ngated on the S5 publish. Static verification only (packages unpublished).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(release): S5 — publish prep, site wire-up, docs, audit hardening (#121)\n\n- release.yml: canvas + canvas-c4 inserted in dependency order; defuses two\n  pre-existing landmines by also wiring mcp-core (every *-studio deps it;\n  absent from the registry — next tag would have published uninstallable\n  studios) and the seven topology-* packages. RELEASING.md family table +\n  not-yet-bootstrapped callout (10 names) + bootstrap-and-tag-in-one-\n  sitting warning.\n- c4 family staged at 0.1.0-alpha.6 (c4-layout layerSpacing + c4-model\n  CodeQL fix are load-bearing for the recomposed c4-ui); canvas +\n  canvas-c4 at 0.1.0-alpha.1.\n- apps/site: c4-* flipped to workspace devDeps per the cost/pages.yml\n  precedent (LOUD_NOTICE + tsconfig references + drift-log entry 20\n  retire runbook); /c4/demo renders the recomposed stack.\n- Parity local-only lane: root pnpm run parity(:update), README section,\n  CI guard comments (darwin-only goldens).\n- Token-audit hardening: full CSS Color 4 named-colour set + background\n  shorthand in canvas; complete scan mirrored into canvas-c4; sticky\n  cross-product derived from StickyColor. shared-modules invariant\n  strengthened to call-site verification.\n- READMEs completed to the normative contracts (CanvasHost 7-method,\n  capabilities incl. routing, meta protocol split, camera model);\n  c4-ui styles.css dead SVG-era rules pruned.\n\nAdversarially reviewed (release-correctness + gates lenses): zero\nblocking; array order, 10-name bootstrap list, tarball dep rewriting,\nand site deploy independently verified. Full monorepo build/typecheck/\ntest green on node 22.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqbtNnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgrUQAB8o+3luFONh9cgp6R5ts1lG\nXTLN9PDVOCVJi68sYKfVpqdkZGo23WhrzG250v48nsDMVrg4HS/to/1a4Z1cyGaN\nvlMU6xX5AROsa+3JAwZboJcIudSEuoUllqWVuXO6dZCUy23B5VGhIobe54JeIDvB\nNEnotMqOW9dHnFT+748t/5oyQVJ/NRdoLgEr9+/vPUnSdh8B1W1V45xLmYrYumbX\nau/A32olzu7uhfxBiB8RJLXjADtXX+a1Ato1/MejyvP5CBKILvBj1UZwAPlmf7RF\nQ4EshGGs8hz96gZMSPFpfYcwvCjLjUidBkW6NR4ztuoVnobs1DGgvb+W2vUQ6KPM\nylDFcLvz2FSMY+KfzdHNBhujL35Mb9SvkmjFy7xAMmaIAMmyZSkBOo6FKu72a7NK\nlz2K02ZWA+Acgmz3SvJM9DqFPfSXsKDFOMSyQY6MLUoZjH70UI7cBWU4Egpn/CY6\noWPyBgQoe6X+YR9rAEToWKw0p3gTN2vpYZ9yRN4h2SdBEaWabGvwI4NOn5ShTLUH\nYEHvpMhDyF2ABA3yqWfYNUwExCgRU9MJkVfx7qlOxkg3CtmRFko/BubKrE8aWERm\nc9QH2uCS8sinUzSrQ73O0tXIAVE3zok9ndVerBvl1g6W01hIDt2gbui1oxuFuXra\nmllgYqEFE1M+8862Rqkc\n=K0cQ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-02T05:19:36Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commit/adee75247d1de9be5409a91ae4dfc624bb99d858","node_id":"C_kwDOTPvB8toAKGFkZWU3NTI0N2QxZGU5YmU1NDA5YTkxYWU0ZGZjNjI0YmI5OWQ4NTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commit/541e561c9a12df7352c738f097c19377db808b99","sha":"541e561c9a12df7352c738f097c19377db808b99","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commits/541e561c9a12df7352c738f097c19377db808b99"}],"sha":"adee75247d1de9be5409a91ae4dfc624bb99d858","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commits/adee75247d1de9be5409a91ae4dfc624bb99d858"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28607748?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FullStackChef","id":28607748,"login":"FullStackChef","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4NjA3NzQ4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commits/541e561c9a12df7352c738f097c19377db808b99/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-26T03:47:49Z","email":"brett@fieldstate.io","name":"Brett Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-26T03:47:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(topology)!: per-env resource overrides on Resource.spec.overrides (S1, #104) (#115)\n\nBREAKING: Environment.spec.overrides is removed; per-environment\nresource overrides now live on the resource itself —\nResource.spec.overrides keyed by environment id. Legacy files fail\nloud: a dedicated legacy-environment-overrides ERROR (validate exit 1,\nMCP write refused, studio PUT refused) names the field, file/line, and\nthe new home — no silent stripping (review caught zod''s non-strict\nparse silently evaporating v0 overrides AND deleting them on write\nround-trips).\n\n- overridable set: config (shallow top-level merge), cost\n  (field-by-field), resourceGroup, network; identity fields\n  (name/kind/type/provider), presence, realizes, links, source are not\n  overridable\n- merge semantics documented precisely: null sets-but-never-removes;\n  placement refs non-nullable (no per-env unplacement); nested config\n  objects replace wholesale (golden-tested)\n- both override-key integrity rules are MODEL diagnostics (no schema\n  cascade): override-environment-not-present +\n  dangling-override-environment-ref, identical key positions, messages\n  lead with the fix (\"remove this override key\")\n- override resourceGroup/network VALUES are dangling-checked like base\n  placement refs (review proved a phantom RG could absorb $490/mo in\n  cost rollups behind a green validate)\n- resolve() returns the merged view; recon/cost/ui/lens consume\n  resolved values unchanged — cost required zero changes (goldens\n  byte-identical to main, migration is behavior-preserving)\n- example demo migrated; contract docs (resolved-topology.types.ts,\n  schema/model READMEs, json-schema regen) updated to the true\n  semantics\n\nRationale for Resource-side placement: the family''s variance idiom is\ncolocated-with-the-owner (connections[].environments,\nResource.spec.environments, decision lines'' per-env qty/amount maps);\none resource file tells its whole cross-env story, and dual mechanisms\n(v0 shipped an Environment-side deep-merge variant) would compete.\n\n402 tests green across 7 suites; revert-checked: legacy check,\npresence diagnostic, dangling-override-placement check, shallow merge.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1592e9f6c29401df5f47034f15ecd6ff101d0eb7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/git/trees/1592e9f6c29401df5f47034f15ecd6ff101d0eb7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/git/commits/541e561c9a12df7352c738f097c19377db808b99","verification":{"payload":"tree 1592e9f6c29401df5f47034f15ecd6ff101d0eb7\nparent 8d9cf4c1652560296ffd820312aacf7825c03434\nauthor Brett Smith <brett@fieldstate.io> 1785037669 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785037669 +1200\n\nfeat(topology)!: per-env resource overrides on Resource.spec.overrides (S1, #104) (#115)\n\nBREAKING: Environment.spec.overrides is removed; per-environment\nresource overrides now live on the resource itself —\nResource.spec.overrides keyed by environment id. Legacy files fail\nloud: a dedicated legacy-environment-overrides ERROR (validate exit 1,\nMCP write refused, studio PUT refused) names the field, file/line, and\nthe new home — no silent stripping (review caught zod''s non-strict\nparse silently evaporating v0 overrides AND deleting them on write\nround-trips).\n\n- overridable set: config (shallow top-level merge), cost\n  (field-by-field), resourceGroup, network; identity fields\n  (name/kind/type/provider), presence, realizes, links, source are not\n  overridable\n- merge semantics documented precisely: null sets-but-never-removes;\n  placement refs non-nullable (no per-env unplacement); nested config\n  objects replace wholesale (golden-tested)\n- both override-key integrity rules are MODEL diagnostics (no schema\n  cascade): override-environment-not-present +\n  dangling-override-environment-ref, identical key positions, messages\n  lead with the fix (\"remove this override key\")\n- override resourceGroup/network VALUES are dangling-checked like base\n  placement refs (review proved a phantom RG could absorb $490/mo in\n  cost rollups behind a green validate)\n- resolve() returns the merged view; recon/cost/ui/lens consume\n  resolved values unchanged — cost required zero changes (goldens\n  byte-identical to main, migration is behavior-preserving)\n- example demo migrated; contract docs (resolved-topology.types.ts,\n  schema/model READMEs, json-schema regen) updated to the true\n  semantics\n\nRationale for Resource-side placement: the family''s variance idiom is\ncolocated-with-the-owner (connections[].environments,\nResource.spec.environments, decision lines'' per-env qty/amount maps);\none resource file tells its whole cross-env story, and dual mechanisms\n(v0 shipped an Environment-side deep-merge variant) would compete.\n\n402 tests green across 7 suites; revert-checked: legacy check,\npresence diagnostic, dangling-override-placement check, shallow merge.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZYNlCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyDcQAGG+isSkmM8w1gaejXJlpgOW\nvzdtaKWcg9A98wYY+NieqeGScMkXsdof+zoOBxefY/6UeheYDMznk7Frii8+kRG5\nsHNpZ4ooPTnrUMcE4IsNghFw6wkvl73/nA5pGJXYHX40IvlzJjJ/deGtYsCz1qiq\nTKlduEJB0c3aVXJ794HDRAm/me3Kn878bUwqb8oVnoybXOjH7bzHUZWQvh9NnQYY\nNta7ogTCOq4b8Ti4iwkUxd0wifeXj5zkhCWkL3ZkXo1RL1a08lycRNOgUtI0eGZk\nENO+gcwQqOBaNivT0JLViZy/xaRpUuYkj3y3KqRlnjZbvZztI13GGAzGpax+r7vc\nnBP1MOAKx0ae0Z9sSSPctEYMaXQIK4rA9saZqZGquHvXgk4tiWdfMYf0YbBuxV9h\nZrO2ewkECfSi62xuvnA1RfCcnWY01trMvRVenegnscBDGvvSta6xxfWYK2jfKVeY\n8fakgm/h1FS+LkLjAuoi+H8AIkaDZktHXu87BDQFYxrEz4Kw0KnqZoaFnTzILFlG\nhQ7jd3uFvEStbC7hdpKkvNz7qbYUPRnCItlTZRkv6Vas3w7ATjbCq1HGhH8OU/mf\ntIB3XYFpAZMD0+qSpylHvUQRsXC2WUojxiu4udwPj81cz+EEsApMFAfTnUnjPISb\nHTZPQ+xWTydx2Wq2hqQS\n=452t\n-----END P