ithub.com/users/FullStackChef/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FullStackChef","id":28607748,"login":"FullStackChef","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4NjA3NzQ4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commits/8d9cf4c1652560296ffd820312aacf7825c03434/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-26T03:32:28Z","email":"brett@fieldstate.io","name":"Brett Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-26T03:32:28Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(topology): aspire import adapter — apphost graph to derived state (S2a, #105) (#114)\n\nNew `aspire` adapter in @workspec/topology-adapters consuming the\nworkspec-graph/v1 apphost dump (aspire-hosting A1 contract): graph JSON\nin, derived Resource artifacts + connections out. Load-bearing for S2\nplacement and S4 brownfield recon.\n\n- kind/type/provider mapping with longest-prefix matching; curated\n  azure table (storage/search/sql-database/app-insights/log-analytics/\n  identity/redis-cache/redis-enterprise), postgres/redis families,\n  compute fallback; SQL Server deliberately unmapped (only the database\n  maps — mirrors the terraform/bicep precedent; review caught the\n  conflation against the real Aspire.Hosting.Azure.Sql assembly)\n- queue family (rabbitmq/kafka/nats) skip-with-warning: no queue\n  ResourceKind in v0 schema — documented gap\n- first adapter to derive CONNECTIONS: env/args/connection-string\n  references -> primary edges; wait edges excluded (ordering, not\n  dataflow); closes the v0 \"adapters don''t derive connectivity\" gap for\n  the aspire path — miswired detection now works end-to-end (tested)\n- CLI: import writes/prunes a fixed-slug derived-connections.yaml under\n  .topology-actual/<env>/; re-import staleness verified (terraform\n  re-import removes it; \"captured empty\" retained as connections: [])\n- loadDerivedTopology now fails loud on MULTIPLE observed-topology\n  files in one env dir (MultipleObservedTopologiesError naming every\n  offender — mirrors the authored side''s \"no single topology found\"),\n  surfaced as 422/isError/CLI error across all serving paths\n- reserved-slug guard: an imported resource slugifying to\n  \"derived-connections\" is excluded with an error diagnostic\n\nadapters 159/159, studio 111/111; typecheck/lint clean; revert-checked\n(SQL split, multi-file guard, connection emission, collision guard).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ab8c81541fc9054ec0989e73b497cd3d7b134fca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/git/trees/ab8c81541fc9054ec0989e73b497cd3d7b134fca"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/git/commits/8d9cf4c1652560296ffd820312aacf7825c03434","verification":{"payload":"tree ab8c81541fc9054ec0989e73b497cd3d7b134fca\nparent c89d13c3153b287c19a0e729b42755a42b6151ee\nauthor Brett Smith <brett@fieldstate.io> 1785036748 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785036748 +1200\n\nfeat(topology): aspire import adapter — apphost graph to derived state (S2a, #105) (#114)\n\nNew `aspire` adapter in @workspec/topology-adapters consuming the\nworkspec-graph/v1 apphost dump (aspire-hosting A1 contract): graph JSON\nin, derived Resource artifacts + connections out. Load-bearing for S2\nplacement and S4 brownfield recon.\n\n- kind/type/provider mapping with longest-prefix matching; curated\n  azure table (storage/search/sql-database/app-insights/log-analytics/\n  identity/redis-cache/redis-enterprise), postgres/redis families,\n  compute fallback; SQL Server deliberately unmapped (only the database\n  maps — mirrors the terraform/bicep precedent; review caught the\n  conflation against the real Aspire.Hosting.Azure.Sql assembly)\n- queue family (rabbitmq/kafka/nats) skip-with-warning: no queue\n  ResourceKind in v0 schema — documented gap\n- first adapter to derive CONNECTIONS: env/args/connection-string\n  references -> primary edges; wait edges excluded (ordering, not\n  dataflow); closes the v0 \"adapters don''t derive connectivity\" gap for\n  the aspire path — miswired detection now works end-to-end (tested)\n- CLI: import writes/prunes a fixed-slug derived-connections.yaml under\n  .topology-actual/<env>/; re-import staleness verified (terraform\n  re-import removes it; \"captured empty\" retained as connections: [])\n- loadDerivedTopology now fails loud on MULTIPLE observed-topology\n  files in one env dir (MultipleObservedTopologiesError naming every\n  offender — mirrors the authored side''s \"no single topology found\"),\n  surfaced as 422/isError/CLI error across all serving paths\n- reserved-slug guard: an imported resource slugifying to\n  \"derived-connections\" is excluded with an error diagnostic\n\nadapters 159/159, studio 111/111; typecheck/lint clean; revert-checked\n(SQL split, multi-file guard, connection emission, collision guard).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZX/MCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOIsQADBabIb/HJoGf1NlPIsXwh/z\nAJc5i5s7dHXbPYuG67ORJ8iHdrUnVPhydZBNBdo5nKI7xZCw6wj3z8flC9jvaYeY\nx1Rcu4kMfsl+v05Kz6wfrimeCuf1XuUZHsn7eKbd1sYPe/EboDJuj5sbqLnsPGu5\nTT9is4hF/xvvqS3VqTsVh/1JFcrBH6LYrhQBQR105FKSu+IRoT6brmVJ44oE1AAv\nlAa7Ts9NbCrEaZTL25ew8K0WNGGIzkOI4Yrqxw+v+gs3G2eWCT79r2VM/Ab+tiJX\n2S1r6r/YDFJhlcOJSF0yiqjxo3wXih65YieaQj+He4qAnKDBXZRfulVEvLdb/P/R\nk8g5tRbVcy3r4Ak6mMhkS+8iACQlKnFCnLv3ZiF3TPyTfDCmzDMw/IdWA8/BdPc