s://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28607748?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FullStackChef","id":28607748,"login":"FullStackChef","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4NjA3NzQ4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commits/c89d13c3153b287c19a0e729b42755a42b6151ee/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-25T21:56:53Z","email":"brett@fieldstate.io","name":"Brett Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-25T21:56:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(topology): S0 publishing-provider spike findings + branch decision (#113)\n\nS0 (#103) answered the v0.1 branch question empirically against Aspire\n13.4.6 with real `aspire publish` runs: cross-package interposition\nworks (a WorkSpec-owned pipeline step''s mutations land in stock\nDocker Compose and Azure Bicep output), and every probed infra-shell\nconcept — SKU, per-resource resource-group placement, alien\nvnet/subnet constructs — survives the stock providers at step time.\nPer the frozen decision procedure: enrichment branch.\n\n- docs/topology/s0-publishing-provider-spike.md — findings note:\n  five questions answered, the early/late timing model, seven\n  empirically-hit hazards with verified mitigations, churn posture\n- .workspec/decisions/aspire-publishing-strategy.yaml — the branch\n  call as a Decision artifact (criteria = the spike questions, both\n  branches scored, outcome: enrichment; fallback documented)\n- .workspec/catalogs/aspire-publishing.yaml — schema-required\n  placeholder catalog (uncosted architectural decision)\n\nBoth artifacts validate via workspec-decisions (2 OK). Full evidence\nrecord: comment on #103. Publisher MVP #106 rescoped to A1.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a876073213161a29370a19d1e5d1b73fba8d00b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/git/trees/a876073213161a29370a19d1e5d1b73fba8d00b3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/git/commits/c89d13c3153b287c19a0e729b42755a42b6151ee","verification":{"payload":"tree a876073213161a29370a19d1e5d1b73fba8d00b3\nparent a4f71e71c524e427b44d24c41bf8804e3a9be0ee\nauthor Brett Smith <brett@fieldstate.io> 1785016613 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785016613 +1200\n\ndocs(topology): S0 publishing-provider spike findings + branch decision (#113)\n\nS0 (#103) answered the v0.1 branch question empirically against Aspire\n13.4.6 with real `aspire publish` runs: cross-package interposition\nworks (a WorkSpec-owned pipeline step''s mutations land in stock\nDocker Compose and Azure Bicep output), and every probed infra-shell\nconcept — SKU, per-resource resource-group placement, alien\nvnet/subnet constructs — survives the stock providers at step time.\nPer the frozen decision procedure: enrichment branch.\n\n- docs/topology/s0-publishing-provider-spike.md — findings note:\n  five questions answered, the early/late timing model, seven\n  empirically-hit hazards with verified mitigations, churn posture\n- .workspec/decisions/aspire-publishing-strategy.yaml — the branch\n  call as a Decision artifact (criteria = the spike questions, both\n  branches scored, outcome: enrichment; fallback documented)\n- .workspec/catalogs/aspire-publishing.yaml — schema-required\n  placeholder catalog (uncosted architectural decision)\n\nBoth artifacts validate via workspec-decisions (2 OK). Full evidence\nrecord: comment on #103. Publisher MVP #106 rescoped to A1.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZTElCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAR7oQAIe/cmaEUM4PCtpL2Uw/nK4b\nTUOUJd+6T340yRx0gjzPt9QufKpWZdPFRIFk/ao0qHV+G3DtK5DfafntXyW+YPRu\nZ6cO90w6a1tmXN+9hIsPuGTW/x/3+r1WctyPqORTVs9FSUEQdltaMKJsGDnw5JyX\nOgzmq2oRFGpUYq7IfvS5VXgHrKOBpHcDVjicAMtW1zBrDvZn+YF7Q0qt+o1w+sHN\nlaHq2cmI/+haYc/yvV+xromPIla2Hhz0fqGLChHEiy9ErQB+a5kqCEp+FJkEQeqv\n47WESnRiVkiZE3vKg/muH7gTh8iSoHcKtc6w1raec6c/u0fsXMz0hjQp+SNg3JxR\nyzFb5dq9ZHJheyhK4ucmQ2cXaVQIm92Tqy0GEhirP/euVyK1rRaNiDorTiYLhGtg\nZ+EXosIJPWChI4WO2W/4ixkFFbY4/JKfeaUyFLyWD4M8zl93Uos4WbY9mrUiDesh\nLhlKHactG62MqB+cTUX/BHV8bSWeMXiRIlGzYWOsowO/kLGJsjeAKpFzrchHfI6/\n/QCorZA0W5RdU6h5iuP56BYMkKG6X1ZDM28WfFPhBpb/jYFCfyzj5DrAkJ7QxQDr\n7Hy8IDwg0P4ZUUtuhw5tINruhJPYJBGzYhp/YIb/4xoINdJ27/4g1fboudRmHzNV\nPNYNdq5VnRNFzj0BHbWd\n=CwqT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-25T21:56:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commit/c89d13c3153b287c19a0e729b42755a42b6151ee","node_id":"C_kwDOTPvB8toAKGM4OWQxM2MzMTUzYjI4N2MxOWEwZTcyOWI0Mjc1NWE0MmI2MTUxZWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commit/a4f71e71c524e427b44d24c41bf8804e3a9be0ee","sha":"a4f71e71c524e427b44d24c41bf8804e3a9be0ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commits/a4f71e71c524e427b44d24c41bf8804e3a9be0ee"}],"sha":"c89d13c3153b287c19a0e729b42755a42b6151ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commits/c89d13c3153b287c19a0e729b42755a42b6151ee"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28607748?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FullStackChef","id":28607748,"login":"FullStackChef","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4NjA3NzQ4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commits/a4f71e71c524e427b44d24c41bf8804e3a9be0ee/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-25T10:54:32Z","email":"brett@fieldstate.io","name":"Brett Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-25T10:54:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(c4): containment layer for createFsSource (CodeQL js/path-injection) (#102)\n\nc4-model was the one package with no path containment: createFsSource\ndid a bare join(rootDir, path), with c4-studio''s isWorkspecPath\npre-check as the documented single line of defence. This ports the\nhouse path-containment.ts (resolveWithinRoot + RefEscapesRootError,\nmirroring decision-/cost-studio) into c4-model''s ./fs subpath and\nbrings c4 up to the two-layer boundary + containment pattern:\n\n- listFiles/readFile/writeFile resolve through resolveWithinRoot and\n  throw RefEscapesRootError before any filesystem call\n- exists() is the deliberate exception: a predicate, not an action —\n  an escaping path reports false without touching the filesystem,\n  matching createMemorySource parity and preserving loadC4Model''s\n  best-effort dangling-link diagnostics for schema-valid content-\n  derived targets like \"~/../escape.md\" (adversarial review caught\n  that throwing here 400''d /api/model on legitimate content)\n- RefEscapesRootError re-exported from @workspec/c4-model/fs and\n  classified in c4-studio''s error mapper + server (client-input, not\n  internal fault), mirroring the other studios\n- stale \"pre-check IS the full defence\" doc comments corrected\n\nAlso: docs/aspire-hosting/mcp-integration.md tool count 34 -> 48 with\ntopology_* namespaces, and a 2-line pnpm-lock.yaml catch-up for\nexamples/topology-web-app (missing since #101; CI runs\n--frozen-lockfile, so this repairs a latent install break on main).\n\nContainment revert-checked (5 tests fail without it, incl. an\nout-of-root write); exists() fix revert-checked (loader-level\nregression test reproduces the availability bug).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a8e9d0a9da04e0382c25f7f1321fb83d09fb1749","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/git/trees/a8e9d0a9da04e0382c25f7f1321fb83d09fb1749"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/git/commits/a4f71e71c524e427b44d24c41bf8804e3a9be0ee","verification":{"payload":"tree a8e9d0a9da04e0382c25f7f1321fb83d09fb1749\nparent 85f30429a143a26c023396c120bd4cdeb90fa652\nauthor Brett Smith <brett@fieldstate.io> 1784976872 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784976872 +1200\n\nfix(c4): containment layer for createFsSource (CodeQL js/path-injection) (#102)\n\nc4-model was the one package with no path containment: createFsSource\ndid a bare join(rootDir, path), with c4-studio''s isWorkspecPath\npre-check as the documented single line of defence. This ports the\nhouse path-containment.ts (resolveWithinRoot + RefEscapesRootError,\nmirroring decision-/cost-studio) into c4-model''s ./fs subpath and\nbrings c4 up to the two-layer boundary + containment pattern:\n\n- listFiles/readFile/writeFile resolve through resolveWithinRoot and\n  throw RefEscapesRootError before any filesystem call\n- exists() is the deliberate exception: a predicate, not an action —\n  an escaping path reports false without touching the filesystem,\n  matching createMemorySource parity and preserving loadC4Model''s\n  best-effort dangling-link diagnostics for schema-valid content-\n  derived targets like \"~/../escape.md\" (adversarial review caught\n  that throwing here 400''d /api/model on legitimate content)\n- RefEscapesRootError re-exported from @workspec/c4-model/fs and\n  classified in c4-studio''s error mapper + server (client-input, not\n  internal fault), mirroring the other studios\n- stale \"pre-check IS the full defence\" doc comments corrected\n\nAlso: docs/aspire-hosting/mcp-integration.md tool count 34 -> 48 with\ntopology_* namespaces, and a 2-line pnpm-lock.yaml catch-up for\nexamples/topology-web-app (missing since #101; CI runs\n--frozen-lockfile, so this repairs a latent install break on main).\n\nContainment revert-checked (5 tests fail without it, incl. an\nout-of-root write); exists() fix revert-checked (loader-level\nregression test reproduces the availability bug).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZJXoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuswQAFua3NA2VsaoEZezdNlvnusu\ntfl+U2mV1e6hX8K3aA6lUWZA4wY+P0YEzmNuxsY704DgtQ04ZJqe45IbCJKoBjZj\nFi3TXiUKcGp+Z8ZyIlHiI+TwgzGRKoIVJtocAnUUHOOl0oqZ6fet4/vAoNOkfQLI\nX7dLPWuNRZKak7dtdYxOGyAphTWclxUM321COfMbJu8UVQP0P3uuj5bfEN3F1fLn\nm6N0IhPeANOX5Z4Lwc6rKx+AuF5RuJ27qlkCwiCqKcErfJ/3tim8/SBOzC5EbrJY\n1sOk+f0Xudp8ETdeRvEBzcPkq2nMWGur2zvnNk7Ji9VJwh//NNVGjI9aiYo6dOXM\npRlYqAxUf2A3B2fiAQ6TRCnEc+gSB4VvrR9OcibmYhOiXuMqATMezjNqDhgJGrYB\n+mLWpyrhC0LuaTWRxuzu10Eyu++hJhF4v9+d8bZuasj78V0IYAfCM6/NN0b4vnil\nqKs9X3DalnjPFmlww9aoGz6HFlgZCMGuUyYQToIWHqPf/1fx08HzViR07V1qno2j\nqrMfQIrXmO3mFdPfq2zFxSnyS4lPlbbOR1OxXCsrfcGTA50uUR14pUhCYkLqaYZs\n6MpV3zm7FdyMbeQJayRZt+mCDbl3rcMY2R6BQpKAWRU+qucuMirG9LFDSDMx17QQ\ntiWxdk90jFyxC6zBYDGX\n=Olpg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-25T10:54:32Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commit/a4f71e71c524e427b44d24c41bf8804e3a9be0ee","node_id":"C_kwDOTPvB8toAKGE0ZjcxZTcxYzUyNGU0MjdiNDRkMjRjNDFiZjg4MDRlM2E5YmUwZWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commit/85f30429a143a26c023396c120bd4cdeb90fa652","sha":"85f30429a143a26c023396c120bd4cdeb90fa652","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commits/85f30429a143a26c023396c120bd4cdeb90fa652"}],"sha":"a4f71e71c524e427b44d24c41bf8804e3a9be0ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commits/a4f71e71c524e427b44d24c41bf8804e3a9be0ee"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28607748?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FullStackChef","id":28607748,"login":"FullStackChef","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4NjA3NzQ4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commits/85f30429a143a26c023396c120bd4cdeb90fa652/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-25T09:47:23Z","email":"brett@fieldstate.io","name":"Brett Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-25T09:47:23Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(topology): topology family — schema, model, adapters, recon, cost, UI, studio + wiring (#101)\n\n* feat(topology): Topology/Resource/Environment artifacts on @workspec/schema-core\n\nNew @workspec/topology-schema: three bare-named artifact kinds (Topology,\nResource, Environment) plus per-lens layout, built on schema-core''s\ndefineArtifact; repository port + memory double; located YAML parse;\ncommitted JSON schemas with a drift guard.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(topology): pure model — resolve(), lens trees, layout-join\n\nNew @workspec/topology-model (browser-safe): loader over a file-source\nport, resolve(topology, env) (prune resources -> auto-prune connections ->\ndeep-merge overrides -> apply naming), network + resource-group lens trees\n(grouping-kind-as-container rule), layout-join, and verify-time diagnostics.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(topology): import adapters terraform/bicep/azure-resource-graph\n\nNew @workspec/topology-adapters: pure functions mapping parsed IaC/cloud\nJSON to derived Resource artifacts (source.kind: derived) via a shared\nvendor->kind catalog. type strings match the authored convention and slug\ncollisions are de-duplicated losslessly with a diagnostic, so reconciliation\nstays a faithful tree-diff.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(topology): reconciliation + drift classification\n\nNew @workspec/topology-recon: maximum-cardinality, order-independent matcher\n(source.from, else the (kind,type,resourceGroup,name) tuple with an\nundefined-resourceGroup wildcard) and phantom/orphan/divergent/miswired\ndrift over a resolved authored topology vs derived actual state. Miswired is\nskipped when connectivity was not observed (connections undefined) rather\nthan reported falsely.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(topology): cost attribution over @workspec/decision-engine\n\nNew @workspec/topology-cost: prices a resolved topology by reusing\ndecision-engine''s lineEnvCost (no reimplemented formula) and rolls cost up\nby resource-group/network and through realizes -> C4 container, with\neven-split-by-default attribution surfaced as unattributed-by-default.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(topology): workbench UI with drift and cost views\n\nNew @workspec/topology-ui: the Topology Workbench (canvas, network<->rg lens\nswitch, env switch, side panel) plus the drift view (colourblind-safe\nphantom/orphan/miswired/divergent badges) and cost view (per-node pills,\ncommitted/schedulable split, container attribution). Dual build (tsup lib +\nmodule-federation remote); tokens sourced only from @workspec/design.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(topology): CLI + server + MCP studio\n\nNew @workspec/topology-studio: the workspec-topology CLI (serve, validate,\nimport, reconcile [CI exit 1 on drift], cost, render, mcp), an Express server\nwith path-contained routes, an FsRepository, and a 14-tool MCP provider\n(namespace topology). Derived-state loading reads an observed topology file\nwhen present so wiring is assessed only when actually captured.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(topology): wire into mcp-host aggregator, mf-host, and Aspire\n\nRegister the topology MCP provider in the workspec-mcp aggregator (48 tools\ntotal; topology namespace = 14), add the topology-ui remote at\n/remote-topology/ in mf-host, and add an aspire-hosting-topology project\n(AddWorkspecTopology) to the solution.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(topology): seeded drifted web-app demo\n\nNew examples/topology-web-app: a full authored .workspec/ topology tree (3\nenvironments, prod-only Front Door, per-lens layout, azure-nz catalog) with a\ncommitted deliberately-drifted actual snapshot. Verified end-to-end:\nreconcile --env prod reports 5 drifts (incl. a precise miswired bypass) and\nexits 1; --env dev is clean and exits 0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(topology): slug-validate env at every boundary (CodeQL js/path-injection)\n\nThe env argument reached posix.join(''.topology-actual'', envSlug) shape-\nunchecked from the MCP tools and the CLI (the HTTP server already\nvalidated via envFrom). Containment via FsRepository.resolve() always\nbackstopped traversal, but the boundaries now reject ill-shaped slugs\nup front:\n\n- mcp-core: new readSlugArg/InvalidSlugError mirroring readRefArg\n  (local predicate; mcp-core stays zod-free), mapped to a client-safe\n  isError by mapErrorToResult\n- topology-studio MCP tools (reconcile/resolve/cost/import): readSlugArg\n  plus pattern/maxLength in their input schemas from schema-core''s\n  SLUG_PATTERN/MAX_SLUG_LENGTH\n- CLI import/reconcile/cost/render: --env shape check, exit 2\n- derivedDirFor: throws InvalidEnvSlugError before the join as a\n  never-fires invariant behind the boundary checks\n\nBoundary tests throughout; revert-checked to be load-bearing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f1a117157e25fc41ab2387a6b96edd71f68966fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/git/trees/f1a117157e25fc41ab2387a6b96edd71f68966fa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/git/commits/85f30429a143a26c023396c120bd4cdeb90fa652","verification":{"payload":"tree f1a117157e25fc41ab2387a6b96edd71f68966fa\nparent 6cbff54efcaf7987c6522e5998294e44768d3098\nauthor Brett Smith <brett@fieldstate.io> 1784972843 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784972843 +1200\n\nfeat(topology): topology family — schema, model, adapters, recon, cost, UI, studio + wiring (#101)\n\n* feat(topology): Topology/Resource/Environment artifacts on @workspec/schema-core\n\nNew @workspec/topology-schema: three bare-named artifact kinds (Topology,\nResource, Environment) plus per-lens layout, built on schema-core''s\ndefineArtifact; repository port + memory double; located YAML parse;\ncommitted JSON schemas with a drift guard.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(topology): pure model — resolve(), lens trees, layout-join\n\nNew @workspec/topology-model (browser-safe): loader over a file-source\nport, resolve(topology, env) (prune resources -> auto-prune connections ->\ndeep-merge overrides -> apply naming), network + resource-group lens trees\n(grouping-kind-as-container rule), layout-join, and verify-time diagnostics.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(topology): import adapters terraform/bicep/azure-resource-graph\n\nNew @workspec/topology-adapters: pure functions mapping parsed IaC/cloud\nJSON to derived Resource artifacts (source.kind: derived) via a shared\nvendor->kind catalog. type strings match the authored convention and slug\ncollisions are de-duplicated losslessly with a diagnostic, so reconciliation\nstays a faithful tree-diff.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(topology): reconciliation + drift classification\n\nNew @workspec/topology-recon: maximum-cardinality, order-independent matcher\n(source.from, else the (kind,type,resourceGroup,name) tuple with an\nundefined-resourceGroup wildcard) and phantom/orphan/divergent/miswired\ndrift over a resolved authored topology vs derived actual state. Miswired is\nskipped when connectivity was not observed (connections undefined) rather\nthan reported falsely.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(topology): cost attribution over @workspec/decision-engine\n\nNew @workspec/topology-cost: prices a resolved topology by reusing\ndecision-engine''s lineEnvCost (no reimplemented formula) and rolls cost up\nby resource-group/network and through realizes -> C4 container, with\neven-split-by-default attribution surfaced as unattributed-by-default.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(topology): workbench UI with drift and cost views\n\nNew @workspec/topology-ui: the Topology Workbench (canvas, network<->rg lens\nswitch, env switch, side panel) plus the drift view (colourblind-safe\nphantom/orphan/miswired/divergent badges) and cost view (per-node pills,\ncommitted/schedulable split, container attribution). Dual build (tsup lib +\nmodule-federation remote); tokens sourced only from @workspec/design.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(topology): CLI + server + MCP studio\n\nNew @workspec/topology-studio: the workspec-topology CLI (serve, validate,\nimport, reconcile [CI exit 1 on drift], cost, render, mcp), an Express server\nwith path-contained routes, an FsRepository, and a 14-tool MCP provider\n(namespace topology). Derived-state loading reads an observed topology file\nwhen present so wiring is assessed only when actually captured.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(topology): wire into mcp-host aggregator, mf-host, and Aspire\n\nRegister the topology MCP provider in the workspec-mcp aggregator (48 tools\ntotal; topology namespace = 14), add the topology-ui remote at\n/remote-topology/ in mf-host, and add an aspire-hosting-topology project\n(AddWorkspecTopology) to the solution.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(topology): seeded drifted web-app demo\n\nNew examples/topology-web-app: a full authored .workspec/ topology tree (3\nenvironments, prod-only Front Door, per-lens layout, azure-nz catalog) with a\ncommitted deliberately-drifted actual snapshot. Verified end-to-end:\nreconcile --env prod reports 5 drifts (incl. a precise miswired bypass) and\nexits 1; --env dev is clean and exits 0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(topology): slug-validate env at every boundary (CodeQL js/path-injection)\n\nThe env argument reached posix.join(''.topology-actual'', envSlug) shape-\nunchecked from the MCP tools and the CLI (the HTTP server already\nvalidated via envFrom). Containment via FsRepository.resolve() always\nbackstopped traversal, but the boundaries now reject ill-shaped slugs\nup front:\n\n- mcp-core: new readSlugArg/InvalidSlugError mirroring readRefArg\n  (local predicate; mcp-core stays zod-free), mapped to a client-safe\n  isError by mapErrorToResult\n- topology-studio MCP tools (reconcile/resolve/cost/import): readSlugArg\n  plus pattern/maxLength in their input schemas from schema-core''s\n  SLUG_PATTERN/MAX_SLUG_LENGTH\n- CLI import/reconcile/cost/render: --env shape check, exit 2\n- derivedDirFor: throws InvalidEnvSlugError before the join as a\n  never-fires invariant behind the boundary checks\n\nBoundary tests throughout; revert-checked to be load-bearing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZIYsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvcAQAHG8B3wK/oSx8nlMYKYfgeiL\nlygAdGmGU95acOhMf9vLX+PEB9zSH3FEJRasw3thrXeS6qV7T/3qNjT8jqLV+spw\nR7bdsGaISt+jpze8616yzil7baDPB3A+t4HCF2U+HDbehqmeSVg21HiRDdwa340g\ndNJfAW01mChtmkK0exIbYMYf2XWhT+Xwu/PGj+aHKDNxZACpxUK20xtNjTxwcSqv\n65yBk7bka93egO/1ySVOdXsnjMFtBlG0qxeySlOYYtHglP/rAhqSoj1FnHqYI29Y\nAdlu6J0L37GO7AeEr092qjTibun4qMxcOCjMZvITtmC5moksX3v2runbggOOQwnJ\ntrIhYLO9z9WntGDfnfGl9GU4XnSPpKr5OTfPCuKS0XNfFEdbd1q2N7Uy+aH7E1KB\nvfoMqMMs5v+oTmZPx3lpRHlW249NWVzZLe5KshZu82OnlbI3Mnn7kMp7xfnhSa2M\n6T1jg29YBIlacjDnS4md4lopUu9xCSq1IwM/H/zwViXyIDJLYYQTW603EXPc53fn\nttKvuHa/VvyIsVNsjD9/YrOsF1aV6xxkSrqQGE2GRBho+j3St4HwY0Q3fmNVpZFP\nK4noy/zrUHzGCBJ0zCTlqv7As5V+EyCq2CTfdKsKRqOQzGEtodw7FlxdIhQRNWWd\nWHGD/ybDY7wXbpYdt9wU\n=cB/T\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-25T09:47:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commit/85f30429a143a26c023396c120bd4cdeb90fa652","node_id":"C_kwDOTPvB8toAKDg1ZjMwNDI5YTE0M2EyNmMwMjMzOTZjMTIwYmQ0Y2RlYjkwZmE2NTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commit/6cbff54efcaf7987c6522e5998294e44768d3098","sha":"6cbff54efcaf7987c6522e5998294e44768d3098","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commits/6cbff54efcaf7987c6522e5998294e44768d3098"}],"sha":"85f30429a143a26c023396c120bd4cdeb90fa652","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commits/85f30429a143a26c023396c120bd4cdeb90fa652"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28607748?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FullStackChef","id":28607748,"login":"FullStackChef","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4NjA3NzQ4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commits/6cbff54efcaf7987c6522e5998294e44768d3098/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-23T01:52:41Z","email":"brett@fieldstate.io","name":"Brett Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-23T01:52:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(mcp): local MCP across all studios + workspec-mcp aggregator + Aspire proxying + zod v4 (#100)\n\n* feat(mcp): shared MCP layer + decision provider (stdio + HTTP)\n\nAdd @workspec/mcp-core — a domain-agnostic contract for exposing studio\nmodule operations as MCP tools, so an AI agent can drive the working tree\n(e.g. fill a decision catalog). Each module contributes an McpToolProvider\n(namespace + JSON-Schema-advertising, self-validating tools); assembleMcpServer\naggregates providers onto one low-level Server with namespaced wire names\n(`decisions_*`), and mountMcpHttp / runMcpStdio expose it over Streamable HTTP\nand stdio. This is the seam a future federated single-app reuses to host ONE\nMCP server across all modules.\n\nWire it up for the decision module (Stage 1 of 3):\n- packages/mcp-core: contract, server assembly (fail-loud dup/bad-name),\n  stateless HTTP mount with a serialized request queue, and a localhost\n  Host + Origin allowlist (hostname-only, port-tolerant, IPv6/trailing-dot/\n  case-aware; missing Origin allowed for non-browser clients, present-but-\n  empty or cross-origin denied) as the DNS-rebinding / cross-origin backstop.\n- decision-studio: createDecisionMcpProvider over the existing FsRepository +\n  engine (list/read/write catalogs & decisions, validate, render_adr), reusing\n  decision-schema''s zod safeParse for authoritative validation and its JSON\n  Schema for tool input advertising. `serve --mcp` mounts /mcp on the studio\n  port; a new `mcp` subcommand runs stdio. Extracted collectDiagnostics so the\n  validate tool and CLI share one implementation; shared isSafeRelativeRef so\n  REST and MCP ref-shape guards can''t drift.\n\nInvariants verified under adversarial review + live probes: path containment\nholds, invalid writes never touch disk, no server-root path/stack leaks to the\nclient, guards fail closed. Tests: mcp-core 28, decision-studio 72 (48 prior).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(decision-schema)!: migrate to zod v4, drop zod-to-json-schema\n\ndecision-schema was the repo''s last zod v3 holdout (house rule: all zod on v4)\nand the only zod-to-json-schema user. Move it to zod ^4.4.3 and regenerate the\ncommitted JSON Schemas via zod 4''s native z.toJSONSchema, matching the pattern\nalready live in schema-core/cost-schema/c4-schema/req-schema.\n\n- json-schema.ts: z.toJSONSchema({ target: ''draft-2020-12'', io: ''input'',\n  reused: ''inline'' }) + local sortJsonKeys for byte-stable output; keeps the\n  self-set $schema/$id/title decoration. io:''input'' keeps .default fields\n  (Lever.enabled) out of `required`, matching safeParse semantics.\n- yaml.ts: deprecated ZodTypeAny -> z.ZodType<T>.\n- decision-studio validate-then-write.ts: widen a structural issue type''s\n  `path` to readonly PropertyKey[] to match zod 4''s $ZodIssue.path.\n- Regenerated json-schema/{catalog,decision}.schema.json. Schema semantics\n  preserved (every required/enum/bound/pattern/description identical); the\n  only shape changes are: additionalProperties:false dropped from plain\n  objects (objects are .strip() at runtime — old schema over-rejected),\n  anyOf->oneOf on the Line discriminated union (mutually exclusive branches,\n  extensionally identical), and an additive type:string on record\n  propertyNames.\n\nBEHAVIOR NOTE: editors/CI validating *.decision.yaml / *.catalog.yaml via the\n$schema directive no longer flag unknown/misspelled keys (runtime already\nignored them). Consistent with every other schema family in the repo.\n\nVerified: decision-schema 48, decision-engine 39, decision-ui 40,\ndecision-studio 72, mcp-core 28 — all green; drift test enforces the committed\nschemas; MCP tools/list smoke intact. Adversarial review: no blocking findings.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(mcp): cost/c4/trace providers + workspec-mcp aggregator (Stage 2+3)\n\nExtend the MCP layer across every studio module and add the aggregator that\nhosts them all on one server — the \"one MCP server, all modules\" end state.\n\nShared helpers: lift the generic provider utilities (ref-shape guard, arg\nreaders, validate-then-write, error-result envelope) out of decision-studio\ninto @workspec/mcp-core so all four providers share one implementation; each\nmodule keeps its own error classifier on the shared envelope. REST refFrom and\nMCP tools now use the same isSafeRelativeRef, so they can''t drift.\n\nProviders (each namespaced, delegating to the module''s own repo/engine and\nvalidating with its own zod before any write):\n- cost (17 tools): list/read/write inventory|spend|attribution|tagplan +\n  validate/report/plan/stocktake/apply; serve --mcp + mcp subcommand.\n- c4 (5 tools): get_model/validate/render/import_aspire/write_layout over\n  C4FileSource + loadC4Model + renderDiagramToSvg; write_layout confined to\n  .layout/, all writes slug-sanitised under .workspec/; serve --mcp + mcp.\n- trace (4 tools): emit/ingest/verify/matrix over the trace repo/CLI cores;\n  mcp subcommand only (trace has no HTTP server).\n\nAggregator @workspec/mcp-host: `workspec-mcp --dir <tree> [--http --port]`\nassembles all four providers onto one Server (stdio default, or mountMcpHttp\nunder --http with the localhost Host+Origin guard). tools/list serves 34 tools\nacross decisions_*/cost_*/c4_*/trace_*, no wire-name collisions.\n\nAdversarial review (independent of the implementer): no blocking findings —\ncontainment holds on every write/path arg (probed), c4 write confinement safe,\nno client-facing error leaks, decision unregressed by the helper lift, and the\naggregator''s namespace isolation + --http Host/Origin enforcement confirmed by\nraw-socket probe. Two fast-follows applied: trace ingest/emit path args now\nshape-checked; an import_aspire confinement regression test locks slugify as\nc4''s containment defense.\n\nTests: mcp-core 56, decision-studio 72, cost-studio 106, c4-studio 127,\ntrace-studio 120, mcp-host 17 — all green; 24-project typecheck clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(aspire): AddWorkspecMcp — proxy the aggregate MCP tools through Aspire\n\nWire the aggregate `workspec-mcp` server into Aspire as a resource and expose\nits tools through Aspire''s built-in MCP server via the experimental\n`WithMcpServer` API. An AI agent connected to Aspire now sees all 34 workspec\ntools (decisions_*/cost_*/c4_*/trace_*) alongside Aspire''s own built-ins, and\nthey''re reachable via `aspire mcp tools` / `aspire mcp call <resource> <tool>`.\n\n- New `aspire-hosting-mcp` project: `AddWorkspecMcp(name, dir)` runs\n  `workspec-mcp --http --dir <dir> --port <port> --host 127.0.0.1` as an\n  executable resource with an HTTP endpoint, a `/health` liveness check, and\n  `WithMcpServer(\"/mcp\", endpointName: \"http\")` so Aspire proxies its tools.\n  `#pragma warning disable ASPIREMCP001` brackets the (experimental) call as a\n  standalone statement — mid-fluent-chain placement does not suppress it, since\n  the diagnostic anchors to the whole chain''s first token.\n- mcp-host: add an unauthenticated `GET /health` to the `--http` app for the\n  Aspire liveness probe.\n- Wire `addWorkspecMcp` into the example TS apphost; add the deps its generated\n  Aspire harness needs to actually run (@types/node, vscode-jsonrpc, tsx) — the\n  example was previously never run for real (its own README said so).\n- Tests: WorkspecMcpExtensionsTests (arg list, http endpoint, ExcludeFromManifest,\n  /health check, and a guard that WithMcpServer attached its public\n  McpServerEndpointAnnotation); wire the test project reference.\n\nVerified LIVE: `aspire run` the example apphost, `aspire mcp tools` lists all 34\nworkspec tools under the `workspec-mcp` resource (clean names — Aspire namespaces\nby resource, no double-prefix). Requires Aspire CLI >= 13.4 (WithMcpServer + the\n`aspire mcp` commands). Solution build 0/0; aspire-hosting-tests 146/146 green\n(under node@22).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(ci): re-trigger checks after Actions billing unlock\n\nNo code change — the prior CI run was blocked by a GitHub Actions billing\nlock (jobs never started); default-setup CodeQL can''t be re-run via the API,\nso this empty commit fires a fresh synchronize event to re-run all checks.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"21fa6fe2afb85f47d3d2aa034b19704e30c223e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/git/trees/21fa6fe2afb85f47d3d2aa034b19704e30c223e6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/git/commits/6cbff54efcaf7987c6522e5998294e44768d3098","verification":{"payload":"tree 21fa6fe2afb85f47d3d2aa034b19704e30c223e6\nparent 9fe3e1587101023def7635324b56b6a08c1764c4\nauthor Brett Smith <brett@fieldstate.io> 1784771561 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784771561 +1200\n\nfeat(mcp): local MCP across all studios + workspec-mcp aggregator + Aspire proxying + zod v4 (#100)\n\n* feat(mcp): shared MCP layer + decision provider (stdio + HTTP)\n\nAdd @workspec/mcp-core — a domain-agnostic contract for exposing studio\nmodule operations as MCP tools, so an AI agent can drive the working tree\n(e.g. fill a decision catalog). Each module contributes an McpToolProvider\n(namespace + JSON-Schema-advertising, self-validating tools); assembleMcpServer\naggregates providers onto one low-level Server with namespaced wire names\n(`decisions_*`), and mountMcpHttp / runMcpStdio expose it over Streamable HTTP\nand stdio. This is the seam a future federated single-app reuses to host ONE\nMCP server across all modules.\n\nWire it up for the decision module (Stage 1 of 3):\n- packages/mcp-core: contract, server assembly (fail-loud dup/bad-name),\n  stateless HTTP mount with a serialized request queue, and a localhost\n  Host + Origin allowlist (hostname-only, port-tolerant, IPv6/trailing-dot/\n  case-aware; missing Origin allowed for non-browser clients, present-but-\n  empty or cross-origin denied) as the DNS-rebinding / cross-origin backstop.\n- decision-studio: createDecisionMcpProvider over the existing FsRepository +\n  engine (list/read/write catalogs & decisions, validate, render_adr), reusing\n  decision-schema''s zod safeParse for authoritative validation and its JSON\n  Schema for tool input advertising. `serve --mcp` mounts /mcp on the studio\n  port; a new `mcp` subcommand runs stdio. Extracted collectDiagnostics so the\n  validate tool and CLI share one implementation; shared isSafeRelativeRef so\n  REST and MCP ref-shape guards can''t drift.\n\nInvariants verified under adversarial review + live probes: path containment\nholds, invalid writes never touch disk, no server-root path/stack leaks to the\nclient, guards fail closed. Tests: mcp-core 28, decision-studio 72 (48 prior).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(decision-schema)!: migrate to zod v4, drop zod-to-json-schema\n\ndecision-schema was the repo''s last zod v3 holdout (house rule: all zod on v4)\nand the only zod-to-json-schema user. Move it to zod ^4.4.3 and regenerate the\ncommitted JSON Schemas via zod 4''s native z.toJSONSchema, matching the pattern\nalready live in schema-core/cost-schema/c4-schema/req-schema.\n\n- json-schema.ts: z.toJSONSchema({ target: ''draft-2020-12'', io: ''input'',\n  reused: ''inline'' }) + local sortJsonKeys for byte-stable output; keeps the\n  self-set $schema/$id/title decoration. io:''input'' keeps .default fields\n  (Lever.enabled) out of `required`, matching safeParse semantics.\n- yaml.ts: deprecated ZodTypeAny -> z.ZodType<T>.\n- decision-studio validate-then-write.ts: widen a structural issue type''s\n  `path` to readonly PropertyKey[] to match zod 4''s $ZodIssue.path.\n- Regenerated json-schema/{catalog,decision}.schema.json. Schema semantics\n  preserved (every required/enum/bound/pattern/description identical); the\n  only shape changes are: additionalProperties:false dropped from plain\n  objects (objects are .strip() at runtime — old schema over-rejected),\n  anyOf->oneOf on the Line discriminated union (mutually exclusive branches,\n  extensionally identical), and an additive type:string on record\n  propertyNames.\n\nBEHAVIOR NOTE: editors/CI validating *.decision.yaml / *.catalog.yaml via the\n$schema directive no longer flag unknown/misspelled keys (runtime already\nignored them). Consistent with every other schema family in the repo.\n\nVerified: decision-schema 48, decision-engine 39, decision-ui 40,\ndecision-studio 72, mcp-core 28 — all green; drift test enforces the committed\nschemas; MCP tools/list smoke intact. Adversarial review: no blocking findings.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(mcp): cost/c4/trace providers + workspec-mcp aggregator (Stage 2+3)\n\nExtend the MCP layer across every studio module and add the aggregator that\nhosts them all on one server — the \"one MCP server, all modules\" end state.\n\nShared helpers: lift the generic provider utilities (ref-shape guard, arg\nreaders, validate-then-write, error-result envelope) out of decision-studio\ninto @workspec/mcp-core so all four providers share one implementation; each\nmodule keeps its own error classifier on the shared envelope. REST refFrom and\nMCP tools now use the same isSafeRelativeRef, so they can''t drift.\n\nProviders (each namespaced, delegating to the module''s own repo/engine and\nvalidating with its own zod before any write):\n- cost (17 tools): list/read/write inventory|spend|attribution|tagplan +\n  validate/report/plan/stocktake/apply; serve --mcp + mcp subcommand.\n- c4 (5 tools): get_model/validate/render/import_aspire/write_layout over\n  C4FileSource + loadC4Model + renderDiagramToSvg; write_layout confined to\n  .layout/, all writes slug-sanitised under .workspec/; serve --mcp + mcp.\n- trace (4 tools): emit/ingest/verify/matrix over the trace repo/CLI cores;\n  mcp subcommand only (trace has no HTTP server).\n\nAggregator @workspec/mcp-host: `workspec-mcp --dir <tree> [--http --port]`\nassembles all four providers onto one Server (stdio default, or mountMcpHttp\nunder --http with the localhost Host+Origin guard). tools/list serves 34 tools\nacross decisions_*/cost_*/c4_*/trace_*, no wire-name collisions.\n\nAdversarial review (independent of the implementer): no blocking findings —\ncontainment holds on every write/path arg (probed), c4 write confinement safe,\nno client-facing error leaks, decision unregressed by the helper lift, and the\naggregator''s namespace isolation + --http Host/Origin enforcement confirmed by\nraw-socket probe. Two fast-follows applied: trace ingest/emit path args now\nshape-checked; an import_aspire confinement regression test locks slugify as\nc4''s containment defense.\n\nTests: mcp-core 56, decision-studio 72, cost-studio 106, c4-studio 127,\ntrace-studio 120, mcp-host 17 — all green; 24-project typecheck clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(aspire): AddWorkspecMcp — proxy the aggregate MCP tools through Aspire\n\nWire the aggregate `workspec-mcp` server into Aspire as a resource and expose\nits tools through Aspire''s built-in MCP server via the experimental\n`WithMcpServer` API. An AI agent connected to Aspire now sees all 34 workspec\ntools (decisions_*/cost_*/c4_*/trace_*) alongside Aspire''s own built-ins, and\nthey''re reachable via `aspire mcp tools` / `aspire mcp call <resource> <tool>`.\n\n- New `aspire-hosting-mcp` project: `AddWorkspecMcp(name, dir)` runs\n  `workspec-mcp --http --dir <dir> --port <port> --host 127.0.0.1` as an\n  executable resource with an HTTP endpoint, a `/health` liveness check, and\n  `WithMcpServer(\"/mcp\", endpointName: \"http\")` so Aspire proxies its tools.\n  `#pragma warning disable ASPIREMCP001` brackets the (experimental) call as a\n  standalone statement — mid-fluent-chain placement does not suppress it, since\n  the diagnostic anchors to the whole chain''s first token.\n- mcp-host: add an unauthenticated `GET /health` to the `--http` app for the\n  Aspire liveness probe.\n- Wire `addWorkspecMcp` into the example TS apphost; add the deps its generated\n  Aspire harness needs to actually run (@types/node, vscode-jsonrpc, tsx) — the\n  example was previously never run for real (its own README said so).\n- Tests: WorkspecMcpExtensionsTests (arg list, http endpoint, ExcludeFromManifest,\n  /health check, and a guard that WithMcpServer attached its public\n  McpServerEndpointAnnotation); wire the test project reference.\n\nVerified LIVE: `aspire run` the example apphost, `aspire mcp tools` lists all 34\nworkspec tools under the `workspec-mcp` resource (clean names — Aspire namespaces\nby resource, no double-prefix). Requires Aspire CLI >= 13.4 (WithMcpServer + the\n`aspire mcp` commands). Solution build 0/0; aspire-hosting-tests 146/146 green\n(under node@22).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(ci): re-trigger checks after Actions billing unlock\n\nNo code change — the prior CI run was blocked by a GitHub Actions billing\nlock (jobs never started); default-setup CodeQL can''t be re-run via the API,\nso this empty commit fires a fresh synchronize event to re-run all checks.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYXPpCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1qoQAEDEtKwAwsQLnqqrnPPYoeal\nYSDsewpqtjwn2D6TLrKvltiUQipu75pg+wXUyJ8OI4ew8SFB5hBKasp3wuRHwa7d\nF9b7UiHhj/4DPmtaJxGjL9FT85V2ASLVJfUCZyUFXlK42ixnqgsZ7S57DBqgsftt\nNYZxv/hhEV6FLc8TiBD7MFJTZzl61QrTbAqFGEmljfN1L+1xnwsUqd0TzfgI+z/9\nGkMo/3d7258jEfOmpXmr7BP7lAmlTWDlxBxbEdfxfhD+5TPGtqbtSOjzDkwGaim9\nsLLtiyvS2BAf378VSFMoO+epbMjj+aS3qe9Eh6g8/E0gRDMuJMCblzU+CBesujRY\n6mafrTZBAmHzP9WS4docFI2xk3t2iQgQyJEG1WAADArtOenMSBXqTyU1VOdkQj/2\npMdpowu9NNsWjxzkIW9Jll14ItUYEt/KsZWeE01kKanqKQrJMYo0vnxX1v1j9K1Y\nJX80HtdMexfDHKxc44fjQlncLUf+6XCaN84diXWqWwiacYsyCClwFJRAWqOHEbYz\nrfWR4s6E9knoZcEMquGMZc4/Y9c2uQ4Bpmtzjb4pRGXtfJmCUesytE4ZHrGiiWtM\nUGVQk0vVMU3KClZT1EWbGH2yZg9QGDAOIswZqVRF21dFaD2ZGUPuGU4JK7Izy+U0\n7Ysu5fo2rDUJP/grsV72\n=qJfK\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-23T01:52:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commit/6cbff54efcaf7987c6522e5998294e44768d3098","node_id":"C_kwDOTPvB8toAKDZjYmZmNTRlZmNhZjc5ODdjNjUyMmU1OTk4Mjk0ZTQ0NzY4ZDMwOTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commit/9fe3e1587101023def7635324b56b6a08c1764c4","sha":"9fe3e1587101023def7635324b56b6a08c1764c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commits/9fe3e1587101023def7635324b56b6a08c1764c4"}],"sha":"6cbff54efcaf7987c6522e5998294e44768d3098","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commits/6cbff54efcaf7987c6522e5998294e44768d3098"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28607748?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FullStackChef","id":28607748,"login":"FullStackChef","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4NjA3NzQ4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commits/9fe3e1587101023def7635324b56b6a08c1764c4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-20T21:30:34Z","email":"brett@fieldstate.io","name":"Brett Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-20T21:30:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(decision)!: migrate the decision family onto @workspec/schema-core + .workspec/ (U2, #84) (#99)\n\nBREAKING: unifies the decision family on the canonical artifact format. Decision\nand Catalog artifacts now live at `.workspec/{decisions,catalogs}/<slug>.yaml`\n(was `*.decision.yaml`/`*.catalog.yaml` suffix files anywhere), the envelope is\nbuilt with schema-core''s `defineArtifact` (`metadata: {slug?}` only), identity is\nthe filename slug, and `metadata.id` is dropped.\n\n- decision-schema: `defineArtifact(''Decision''|''Catalog'', spec)`; ALL rich metadata\n  moved to spec (Decision: title/status/created/deciders/supersedes; Catalog:\n  name/currency/asOf); the cross-field `.superRefine`s chain onto the envelope.\n  `spec.supersedes` is now the target decision''s SLUG; `spec.catalog` is a catalog\n  SLUG (resolved to `.workspec/catalogs/<slug>.yaml`), not a relative path.\n  `TYPE_DIRECTORIES`; base constants + JSON-schema gen from schema-core; suffix/\n  `isDecisionFile` machinery retired. zod 3→4. Internal ids untouched.\n- decision-studio: `fs-repository` rewritten to the `.workspec/` directory-walk\n  (mirroring cost/trace-studio); `resolveCatalogRef` resolves the catalog slug (no\n  relative path-join); comment-preserving serializer kept; CLI write paths +\n  `DecisionRef.slug`.\n- decision-engine: `buildAdrModel(decision, catalog, slug)` — the ADR is keyed on\n  the slug now (metadata.id is gone); metadata reads → spec.\n- decision-ui: metadata reads → spec across card/adr/catalog/compare/workspace/\n  decide; a `decisionSlug(decision, ref)` helper threads identity; the second\n  `resolveCatalogRef` (host.ts) resolves the catalog slug; supersedes-match by slug.\n- Fixtures (examples/hosting-platform, examples/postgres-*, docs/decisions) +\n  mf-host''s decision seed reshaped to the new envelope, with the id→slug remap\n  (e.g. `dec-d1-monorepo-tooling` → `d1-monorepo-build-tooling`). apps/site left on\n  the published pins until republish.\n\nAll four packages → 0.1.0-alpha.6 (lockstep). Whole workspace green — root\ntypecheck/build/test + `dotnet test` (139/139, incl. the real-CLI decision E2E).\nMinimal-churn lockfile (no unrelated jest-dom perturbation).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"491efcf613059d68e3da309a487e39c3607fd2e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/git/trees/491efcf613059d68e3da309a487e39c3607fd2e8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/git/commits/9fe3e1587101023def7635324b56b6a08c1764c4","verification":{"payload":"tree 491efcf613059d68e3da309a487e39c3607fd2e8\nparent cdc1e5b54ad2036ec7f1481cab1a936fa555e30e\nauthor Brett Smith <brett@fieldstate.io> 1784583034 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784583034 +1200\n\nfeat(decision)!: migrate the decision family onto @workspec/schema-core + .workspec/ (U2, #84) (#99)\n\nBREAKING: unifies the decision family on the canonical artifact format. Decision\nand Catalog artifacts now live at `.workspec/{decisions,catalogs}/<slug>.yaml`\n(was `*.decision.yaml`/`*.catalog.yaml` suffix files anywhere), the envelope is\nbuilt with schema-core''s `defineArtifact` (`metadata: {slug?}` only), identity is\nthe filename slug, and `metadata.id` is dropped.\n\n- decision-schema: `defineArtifact(''Decision''|''Catalog'', spec)`; ALL rich metadata\n  moved to spec (Decision: title/status/created/deciders/supersedes; Catalog:\n  name/currency/asOf); the cross-field `.superRefine`s chain onto the envelope.\n  `spec.supersedes` is now the target decision''s SLUG; `spec.catalog` is a catalog\n  SLUG (resolved to `.workspec/catalogs/<slug>.yaml`), not a relative path.\n  `TYPE_DIRECTORIES`; base constants + JSON-schema gen from schema-core; suffix/\n  `isDecisionFile` machinery retired. zod 3→4. Internal ids untouched.\n- decision-studio: `fs-repository` rewritten to the `.workspec/` directory-walk\n  (mirroring cost/trace-studio); `resolveCatalogRef` resolves the catalog slug (no\n  relative path-join); comment-preserving serializer kept; CLI write paths +\n  `DecisionRef.slug`.\n- decision-engine: `buildAdrModel(decision, catalog, slug)` — the ADR is keyed on\n  the slug now (metadata.id is gone); metadata reads → spec.\n- decision-ui: metadata reads → spec across card/adr/catalog/compare/workspace/\n  decide; a `decisionSlug(decision, ref)` helper threads identity; the second\n  `resolveCatalogRef` (host.ts) resolves the catalog slug; supersedes-match by slug.\n- Fixtures (examples/hosting-platform, examples/postgres-*, docs/decisions) +\n  mf-host''s decision seed reshaped to the new envelope, with the id→slug remap\n  (e.g. `dec-d1-monorepo-tooling` → `d1-monorepo-build-tooling`). apps/site left on\n  the published pins until republish.\n\nAll four packages → 0.1.0-alpha.6 (lockstep). Whole workspace green — root\ntypecheck/build/test + `dotnet test` (139/139, incl. the real-CLI decision E2E).\nMinimal-churn lockfile (no unrelated jest-dom perturbation).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqXpN6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAO1EQAB47hqNkwzyPQU5wjGpvRU+n\nad1sjxDa6n3cQCdVt5fF1g1KWSDAd3IbYku384M8pCfaOiNxm+QRBPVb+V5zRaJQ\n9SbGoikusEDwQ+JUq/DHvqDwk62ZNar8YN8nOtJm/aRnmv6AI/1JXZanlzsn3ATJ\nofM4SrJQOMlhQV+e/T/aRL7U04VDZY6Qi3RWma3d+Yl/KM1Cjqygw6OPLPIogEAy\nzQ1Ens6+ZRG6OtekilvTpBaK1bOLQg2iowiogJPIEQlZvy8kj9LoLG/jctRyRtmC\nzKhOkmDeIApRQeYxGD4KWXn81W84ZiVNtxw6yB/JLiQzsp6L1rdPo9fzFBGvvkE3\nkIpTsJSS5lDNz66zB27IEdBtv0HdjLcY1Krl2wsEbhYos6qQrIc4nKp