nts_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FullStackChef","id":28607748,"login":"FullStackChef","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4NjA3NzQ4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commits/08b82773de447cd10e184051bb209979682335a3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-19T09:45:41Z","email":"brett@fieldstate.io","name":"Brett Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-19T09:45:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(traceability): junit emitter + format-agnostic ingest (T7, #75) (#96)\n\nAdds `junit` as a second provider on the emitter seam — proving the seam\ngeneralizes (adding a framework = adding an emitter, the shared round-trip\nconformance harness admitted junit with ZERO changes) — and makes the CLI''s\ningest format-agnostic so `--emitter junit` works end-to-end.\n\n- `junitEmitter` — `emit(rules)` → JUnit XML (one `<testsuite>` per Rule, one\n  `<testcase name=\"<scenario-slug>\">` per scenario — the scenario slug IS the\n  binding; title in a companion property), `ingest(xml)` → TestRun keyed on the\n  scenario slug. Four declared conventions. Deterministic, XML-escaped output.\n- `ingest` parses XML defensively (never throws): `<failure>`/`<error>` → fail,\n  `<skipped>` → skip, else pass; outline rows fold `fail > skip > pass`. The\n  hand-rolled scanner guards against cross-testcase bleed — an unterminated\n  `<testcase>` is marked malformed (lenient skip) without swallowing the next\n  testcase''s evidence.\n- Shared `verdict.ts` (`foldVerdict`) extracted so both emitters use one fold;\n  `xml-escape.ts` shared by render + ingest.\n- **Format-agnostic ingest:** `Emitter.ingest` now receives the raw report and\n  each emitter parses its own format. `cucumberEmitter.ingest` accepts a JSON\n  string (parsed internally, defensively) as well as a pre-parsed array; the CLI\n  `runIngest` reads the results file as text and hands it straight to the\n  emitter — no more `JSON.parse` in the CLI (which broke XML). Unreadable file →\n  exit 1; a report the emitter can''t parse → an empty (still valid) TestRun.\n\nEmitters 93 tests, studio 102. Smoke-tested end-to-end: emit+ingest for both\ncucumber (JSON) and junit (XML), verify passing on a junit-ingested run.\nAdversarially reviewed; the malformed-XML cross-testcase-bleed finding was fixed.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c9948179648fbd91f6e9ea3ca93f26eb9dfbf4d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/git/trees/c9948179648fbd91f6e9ea3ca93f26eb9dfbf4d0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/git/commits/08b82773de447cd10e184051bb209979682335a3","verification":{"payload":"tree c9948179648fbd91f6e9ea3ca93f26eb9dfbf4d0\nparent df24355efb8009fc3d80557d2e722800e5936817\nauthor Brett Smith <brett@fieldstate.io> 1784454341 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784454341 +1200\n\nfeat(traceability): junit emitter + format-agnostic ingest (T7, #75) (#96)\n\nAdds `junit` as a second provider on the emitter seam — proving the seam\ngeneralizes (adding a framework = adding an emitter, the shared round-trip\nconformance harness admitted junit with ZERO changes) — and makes the CLI''s\ningest format-agnostic so `--emitter junit` works end-to-end.\n\n- `junitEmitter` — `emit(rules)` → JUnit XML (one `<testsuite>` per Rule, one\n  `<testcase name=\"<scenario-slug>\">` per scenario — the scenario slug IS the\n  binding; title in a companion property), `ingest(xml)` → TestRun keyed on the\n  scenario slug. Four declared conventions. Deterministic, XML-escaped output.\n- `ingest` parses XML defensively (never throws): `<failure>`/`<error>` → fail,\n  `<skipped>` → skip, else pass; outline rows fold `fail > skip > pass`. The\n  hand-rolled scanner guards against cross-testcase bleed — an unterminated\n  `<testcase>` is marked malformed (lenient skip) without swallowing the next\n  testcase''s evidence.\n- Shared `verdict.ts` (`foldVerdict`) extracted so both emitters use one fold;\n  `xml-escape.ts` shared by render + ingest.\n- **Format-agnostic ingest:** `Emitter.ingest` now receives the raw report and\n  each emitter parses its own format. `cucumberEmitter.ingest` accepts a JSON\n  string (parsed internally, defensively) as well as a pre-parsed array; the CLI\n  `runIngest` reads the results file as text and hands it straight to the\n  emitter — no more `JSON.parse` in the CLI (which broke XML). Unreadable file →\n  exit 1; a report the emitter can''t parse → an empty (still valid) TestRun.\n\nEmitters 93 tests, studio 102. Smoke-tested end-to-end: emit+ingest for both\ncucumber (JSON) and junit (XML), verify passing on a junit-ingested run.\nAdversarially reviewed; the malformed-XML cross-testcase-bleed finding was fixed.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqXJzFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0e4QAJf3v8ypvZLfdfUEMDcLMVxJ\n3SlYiAE1CAB74XhDRPTsEjW4STNvOIf+2PHoDpCFt//RlXXLam5YNchSQGo+bHzN\nwSdnRNR1rsyjWNP0DutwPKkZgf17+YXPlUGq3yCfsT5G5vXtB/6egkGOY1k0ftzM\nDqm93jcYGNH4h+PBtgSqWa3s9dekLsJOP9tVyniM5Ot0w+dWg7F7U9rf7sT3EZUB\n8OC