ha":"08b82773de447cd10e184051bb209979682335a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commits/08b82773de447cd10e184051bb209979682335a3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28607748?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FullStackChef","id":28607748,"login":"FullStackChef","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4NjA3NzQ4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commits/df24355efb8009fc3d80557d2e722800e5936817/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-19T08:53:57Z","email":"brett@fieldstate.io","name":"Brett Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-19T08:53:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(traceability): Matrix view — the RTM in the UI (T6, #74) (#95)\n\nEnables the Matrix tab in the Traceability Workbench and renders the RTM:\nscenario rows grouped by Feature → Rule (system-requirement), each showing its\nlatest-run proof (pass/fail/skip/unproven) as a status cell. Completes #74\nalongside the merged `workspec-trace matrix` export.\n\n- Grouping is a view-layer projection over the derived model (`model.features`\n  → `sysreqsOf` → `scenariosOf`) — never re-derives the meters (MetersBar stays\n  sole owner); rollups reuse the shared `format.ts` proof helpers.\n- Expand/collapse per feature and Rule; an untested-only filter that hides\n  proven/failing scenarios but NEVER hides structural diagnostics (an empty Rule,\n  an uncovered feature stay visible — a compliance view must not hide them).\n- Explicit empty states: empty Rule → \"a requirement with no proof\"; feature\n  with no Rules → \"uncovered\"; same wording as Feature detail.\n- Latest-run-only (spec §9.4) — no fabricated per-run history. Export stays the\n  CLI''s job (`workspec-trace matrix`); the toolbar shows a pointer, not a button.\n- Exposed as an MF remote; zero local design tokens (status cells reuse the\n  shared proof color tokens). 72 tests green.\n\nAdversarially reviewed: per-scenario status cells, the filter-keeps-diagnostics\nrule, grouping via trace-model lookups, render-not-rederive, and latest-only all\nconfirmed. A pre-existing dangling-ref visibility gap (shared with Feature detail)\nis tracked as a follow-up.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7cfc8266ae46a2a6f4e7a5628375a997a19bb9a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/git/trees/7cfc8266ae46a2a6f4e7a5628375a997a19bb9a7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/git/commits/df24355efb8009fc3d80557d2e722800e5936817","verification":{"payload":"tree 7cfc8266ae46a2a6f4e7a5628375a997a19bb9a7\nparent 2f7ebb57fb96d6043f0517b502260d58439a04fd\nauthor Brett Smith <brett@fieldstate.io> 1784451237 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784451237 +1200\n\nfeat(traceability): Matrix view — the RTM in the UI (T6, #74) (#95)\n\nEnables the Matrix tab in the Traceability Workbench and renders the RTM:\nscenario rows grouped by Feature → Rule (system-requirement), each showing its\nlatest-run proof (pass/fail/skip/unproven) as a status cell. Completes #74\nalongside the merged `workspec-trace matrix` export.\n\n- Grouping is a view-layer projection over the derived model (`model.features`\n  → `sysreqsOf` → `scenariosOf`) — never re-derives the meters (MetersBar stays\n  sole owner); rollups reuse the shared `format.ts` proof helpers.\n- Expand/collapse per feature and Rule; an untested-only filter that hides\n  proven/failing scenarios but NEVER hides structural diagnostics (an empty Rule,\n  an uncovered feature stay visible — a compliance view must not hide them).\n- Explicit empty states: empty Rule → \"a requirement with no proof\"; feature\n  with no Rules → \"uncovered\"; same wording as Feature detail.\n- Latest-run-only (spec §9.4) — no fabricated per-run history. Export stays the\n  CLI''s job (`workspec-trace matrix`); the toolbar shows a pointer, not a button.\n- Exposed as an MF remote; zero local design tokens (status cells reuse the\n  shared proof color tokens). 72 tests green.\n\nAdversarially reviewed: per-scenario status cells, the filter-keeps-diagnostics\nrule, grouping via trace-model lookups, render-not-rederive, and latest-only all\nconfirmed. A pre-existing dangling-ref visibility gap (shared with Feature detail)\nis tracked as a follow-up.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqXJClCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQVYQAHOVTwvEz/VxhqZg6n9/qIDU\ncCYFMeLf60SX80Vsdqz0QEbaVCspw8gl6vn0ITul1y74bNQ2RI3/QvPXAVfxywZ0\nh1oDpY0zgK1ilhzaJc+UW8mceIDgtvVatMGoDFVEPA4Nb8qUld+kpLYwvvXajFH4\nRlX6C7XuLTk9L2ZAp2XFNwO5l8ewbXLvPLjm7clZnzL7VPPZ/7MuaGNOrmHwEm5r\nNMRVxW2yrNqpFH+8DVcUzjHPm/ZlOm3hCdCkg+k9OQFCz1MprNjx5xiYZ1nsjR4a\nW2w1xXTlybssLb+Nw4l2zEx8zBW4IIu11eSG71NJE9yhtGHOrzFRNX8rZ8c9+6lL\nyusjrm2j+GMk+L6y8VcN3dt7QGmbn4hls5n5FlSTDmDZ4ng0T4ezoYo5hLmaweD8\nWAOmWN3ySREGpzFHMu9wcpZ8dAdW5YoJfruOgP2ISNLKBnKY1KXP/XpHmbTKPPyt\nwYUUze3l2jhBIkPtAZH0OAt5/Yx6UTVymJBtxod/FraE1R410sXSTdDoPDFHItve\n+LpwUkxOnobUp0IhP7hT2IdAAZpy3QujVmB4lsl76F2iQaqTOKHjtgC7aXWB2voH\nZloh+Qza6UiJa2YpFC/2zLFQvFsHkSngsw3XDuHjH+tY+E6IPUxt7PhWm7dyvQwi\nm7Dgc68s9uhdEyFOYIJy\n=F72x\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-19T08:53:58Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commit/df24355efb8009fc3d80557d2e722800e5936817","node_id":"C_kwDOTPvB8toAKGRmMjQzNTVlZmI4MDA5ZmMzZDgwNTU3ZDJlNzIyODAwZTU5MzY4MTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commit/2f7ebb57fb96d6043f0517b502260d58439a04fd","sha":"2f7ebb57fb96d6043f0517b502260d58439a04fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commits/2f7ebb57fb96d6043f0517b502260d58439a04fd"}],"sha":"df24355efb8009fc3d80557d2e722800e5936817","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commits/df24355efb8009fc3d80557d2e722800e5936817"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28607748?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FullStackChef","id":28607748,"login":"FullStackChef","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4NjA3NzQ4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commits/2f7ebb57fb96d6043f0517b502260d58439a04fd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-19T08:16:00Z","email":"brett@fieldstate.io","name":"Brett Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-19T08:16:00Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(traceability): matrix export — the RTM compliance artifact (T6, #74) (#94)\n\n`workspec-trace matrix [--out <file>] [--format md|csv|html]` — generates the\nrequirements traceability matrix as a deterministic, byte-stable artifact (the\ncompliance payload). Format inferred from the `--out` extension (.md/.csv/.html)\nor forced with `--format`; stdout when no `--out`. Exit 2 on unknown format,\n1 on write failure; loader issues warn but don''t abort (the RTM renders anyway).\n\n- One row per **scenario** — the full trace: Feature · Rule · Scenario ·\n  Verifies (the Rule''s userReqs) · Status (latest-run proof) · Run · SHA. An\n  **empty Rule** still appears (a placeholder row — a requirement with no proof\n  must not be invisible in an audit doc); dangling refs render the raw ref\n  as-authored, nothing dropped.\n- Pure, IO-free serializers with correct escaping — RFC 4180 CSV (quote+double),\n  Markdown (backslash-then-pipe, newline→`<br>`), self-contained HTML (entity\n  escaping, no external refs) — column order defined once so the three renderers\n  can''t drift. Rows sorted by feature→rule→scenario for byte-stability.\n- Exposes `buildMatrixRows`/`renderMatrix` from the package for a future Matrix\n  export button in the UI.\n\nGolden-snapshot determinism tests per format + escaping edge cases + exit-code /\nformat-inference coverage. 101 tests green. Adversarially reviewed: escaping\nround-tripped through real parsers, determinism confirmed under reversed input,\ncompleteness + dangling + exit codes verified against the built binary.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1ad77a7822e220674a4f2c5d7c5db0c38942ebab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/git/trees/1ad77a7822e220674a4f2c5d7c5db0c38942ebab"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/git/commits/2f7ebb57fb96d6043f0517b502260d58439a04fd","verification":{"payload":"tree 1ad77a7822e220674a4f2c5d7c5db0c38942ebab\nparent 128db93050daaf7c86c45b1a3e3dd3d565267f42\nauthor Brett Smith <brett@fieldstate.io> 1784448960 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784448960 +1200\n\nfeat(traceability): matrix export — the RTM compliance artifact (T6, #74) (#94)\n\n`workspec-trace matrix [--out <file>] [--format md|csv|html]` — generates the\nrequirements traceability matrix as a deterministic, byte-stable artifact (the\ncompliance payload). Format inferred from the `--out` extension (.md/.csv/.html)\nor forced with `--format`; stdout when no `--out`. Exit 2 on unknown format,\n1 on write failure; loader issues warn but don''t abort (the RTM renders anyway).\n\n- One row per **scenario** — the full trace: Feature · Rule · Scenario ·\n  Verifies (the Rule''s userReqs) · Status (latest-run proof) · Run · SHA. An\n  **empty Rule** still appears (a placeholder row — a requirement with no proof\n  must not be invisible in an audit doc); dangling refs render the raw ref\n  as-authored, nothing dropped.\n- Pure, IO-free serializers with correct escaping — RFC 4180 CSV (quote+double),\n  Markdown (backslash-then-pipe, newline→`<br>`), self-contained HTML (entity\n  escaping, no external refs) — column order defined once so the three renderers\n  can''t drift. Rows sorted by feature→rule→scenario for byte-stability.\n- Exposes `buildMatrixRows`/`renderMatrix` from the package for a future Matrix\n  export button in the UI.\n\nGolden-snapshot determinism tests per format + escaping edge cases + exit-code /\nformat-inference coverage. 101 tests green. Adversarially reviewed: escaping\nround-tripped through real parsers, determinism confirmed under reversed input,\ncompleteness + dangling + exit codes verified against the built binary.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqXIfACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArM8QAGbhUFhpxEb9i1EiIPo0Q7mj\n5br8xotCMQlGXLHy3nNrVoVAG2hbAQRea26LfUNoWuPRp/UY0x8ErPgvD3D56OAU\nraMSCpHoIe4sGGJZ1l2NJ4NbYmx+DVkQmN0j1VFaEZILo5wOKe+xAFlQ1OxBv+sa\nv753Uh7xpOi/CGyn+VVXGIJe7XTSYsSXCzopsvymvQ87rGtsCTvTF7BZ212UFgih\ncS1x24hMlEAmDVnKR7jHHjLYLMqDxRgBC60nUK1OUSnn8V+6EtOnyG9iFYFNc1Vt\nHvntqQprw+MZ4hgidwd00W8BN+OF3AV+3OTB3hKlbpeDMOMgqP93HT5D1F+OyyEr\nBT2+Yx3DJlmwRcv1fPjYehPUKGD7fFmrxXhULlBm1SS2mkkObA8vPd7yhX3GIpPs\n+O9KGDhAVgI9LIi8EYIxZb3zrtZWU05MIlbidNGGQGhuylw2nYNV5MvG1lvQ2f2L\ndZJNmM/87ghUV/Mkh+Yv//OyXotIoR2raKLyMXJW3S2hIdnPr9dq44MuBNC2AXYc\nhhNnTIjcCVnIddelb/X8WGWRtbap7Nap4HZJn0/x+DnXI05Upxug1JEwACCOSU1K\nto2cfW8vkabXRoNOaSgCOzyGyljS+KGgyNBbQfwb/oyrVgekJTYNLG3eEhkIwSr5\nPJmFoJav09W14mGHKxf6\n=qjpe\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-19T08:16:00Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commit/2f7ebb57fb96d6043f0517b502260d58439a04fd","node_id":"C_kwDOTPvB8toAKDJmN2ViYjU3ZmI5NmQ2MDQzZjA1MTdiNTAyMjYwZDU4NDM5YTA0ZmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commit/128db93050daaf7c86c45b1a3e3dd3d565267f42","sha":"128db93050daaf7c86c45b1a3e3dd3d565267f42","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commits/128db93050daaf7c86c45b1a3e3dd3d565267f42"}],"sha":"2f7ebb57fb96d6043f0517b502260d58439a04fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commits/2f7ebb57fb96d6043f0517b502260d58439a04fd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28607748?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FullStackChef","id":28607748,"login":"FullStackChef","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4NjA3NzQ4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commits/128db93050daaf7c86c45b1a3e3dd3d565267f42/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-19T07:41:57Z","email":"brett@fieldstate.io","name":"Brett Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-19T07:41:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(traceability): trace-ui — Requirements + Feature detail + meters bar (T5, #73) (#93)\n\n`@workspec/trace-ui`: the Traceability Workbench UI, mirroring the cost-ui\narchitecture (React 18, Tailwind v4, module-federation remote, themed via a\n`theme` prop, host-agnostic). Consumes `@workspec/design` with ZERO local design\ntokens (enforced by a test). Renders an already-derived `TraceModel` — never\nre-derives.\n\n- **MetersBar** — the three meters side by side, never collapsed (spec §5):\n  Scenario coverage, UserReq coverage, Pass rate, each `{numerator, denominator,\n  ratio}` straight from the model, plus a pass/fail/skip/unproven summary.\n- **RequirementsExplorer** — filterable rows (All / User reqs / Rules /\n  Diagnostics / Has untested); click a row for its chain (userReq → verifying\n  Rules → scenarios → proof) via trace-model lookups. Diagnostics surfaces every\n  `model.findings` entry, including orphan-feature findings that name no row.\n- **FeatureDetail** — feature → userReqs → Rules → scenarios with proof; the\n  empty-rule and no-sysreq cases render as explicit labelled states.\n- **TraceApp** shell + `TraceStudioHost`/`TraceRepositoryPort` (`readModel()`)\n  host contract; MF remotes (`MetersBar`/`RequirementsExplorer`/`FeatureDetail`/\n  `TraceApp`) with react/react-dom/react-query as shared singletons. Matrix and\n  Run-review tabs are present but disabled (T6/T7).\n- A dev story (`pnpm --filter @workspec/trace-ui dev`) over a seeded fixture.\n\nAdapted from the design: added the third meter (UserReq coverage) per spec §5;\nscenario identity is the scenario''s own slug (5-kind model). Verified in a\nbrowser in both themes. 61 tests green. Adversarially reviewed; the Diagnostics\nundercount and a themed-root double-wrap were fixed.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"03c552be513d0034ad9fe9d97ddc6e5d98ad5504","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/git/trees/03c552be513d0034ad9fe9d97ddc6e5d98ad5504"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/git/commits/128db93050daaf7c86c45b1a3e3dd3d565267f42","verification":{"payload":"tree 03c552be513d0034ad9fe9d97ddc6e5d98ad5504\nparent 3032862ec37e25f64bbcc7bd18059a1c663eb5e9\nauthor Brett Smith <brett@fieldstate.io> 1784446917 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784446917 +1200\n\nfeat(traceability): trace-ui — Requirements + Feature detail + meters bar (T5, #73) (#93)\n\n`@workspec/trace-ui`: the Traceability Workbench UI, mirroring the cost-ui\narchitecture (React 18, Tailwind v4, module-federation remote, themed via a\n`theme` prop, host-agnostic). Consumes `@workspec/design` with ZERO local design\ntokens (enforced by a test). Renders an already-derived `TraceModel` — never\nre-derives.\n\n- **MetersBar** — the three meters side by side, never collapsed (spec §5):\n  Scenario coverage, UserReq coverage, Pass rate, each `{numerator, denominator,\n  ratio}` straight from the model, plus a pass/fail/skip/unproven summary.\n- **RequirementsExplorer** — filterable rows (All / User reqs / Rules /\n  Diagnostics / Has untested); click a row for its chain (userReq → verifying\n  Rules → scenarios → proof) via trace-model lookups. Diagnostics surfaces every\n  `model.findings` entry, including orphan-feature findings that name no row.\n- **FeatureDetail** — feature → userReqs → Rules → scenarios with proof; the\n  empty-rule and no-sysreq cases render as explicit labelled states.\n- **TraceApp** shell + `TraceStudioHost`/`TraceRepositoryPort` (`readModel()`)\n  host contract; MF remotes (`MetersBar`/`RequirementsExplorer`/`FeatureDetail`/\n  `TraceApp`) with react/react-dom/react-query as shared singletons. Matrix and\n  Run-review tabs are present but disabled (T6/T7).\n- A dev story (`pnpm --filter @workspec/trace-ui dev`) over a seeded fixture.\n\nAdapted from the design: added the third meter (UserReq coverage) per spec §5;\nscenario identity is the scenario''s own slug (5-kind model). Verified in a\nbrowser in both themes. 61 tests green. Adversarially reviewed; the Diagnostics\nundercount and a themed-root double-wrap were fixed.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqXH/FCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6IMQADCm4MUOHV7P9Ap2jSK46tqD\nIHhYfqHBOKUOyDh2hWiu/W2os1fANjdoQzKc9Z0Oq1U09YCy0nye5MMiAHYUp5OM\niYuPO+Dlh7As2orhgcT/sFatGnIp7VXF6npL3zOeZa4nrQenuy9X0TO4tk+wc4AZ\n5Fh16GrWhIrkkT2KeVmNbdBvzSIr/eFpfdJkd4XymTc1Zz1FDqUr7jIQtWsQRL2s\noqwY1l6kpEp5MyEI/QXncxn5hvClGgjJRm63VFnhIJbx2FnOFEQYK2e46F4rFcFr\nfS05Z0WjxrGxhpRgOxLSrfRWwLRNQyn/wEqAoBPGqIzWK08Msc9Ai70N33xkoFiU\nlPJ5ahCWhQtsak8ps3GwVCEiCT0qbmLyp7ANAzSBd3OgSK6cRMiZNVVbJqFw0Bm/\n7GVCH7VGp47ypKWZU3zWc1ZShC/KdDi8yFsy+PgQdl6ojoxotALiJ107dIfkZjbE\n79TNd/dXbcjPXzzFyPJ4bAc2nCaQvi6eNTWigwvHFqhJ8fDMt/fnnF5/wsFxFk8x\nPtBy4Xo2fbyRLfeCHKEFolpaR5lkiw8TCmaR7HyEuXj5//K2BQKJGIQVywVFWjzQ\na6Gc2VRXL5hKyD/F2n87QXflal9v18hSXa9DdiIEHuvEkXcARFdfASC374NvtkJo\ngKinksRXIGyRnnov8+3s\n=ahqm\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-19T07:41:58Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commit/128db93050daaf7c86c45b1a3e3dd3d565267f42","node_id":"C_kwDOTPvB8toAKDEyOGRiOTMwNTBkYWFmN2M4NmM0NWIxYTNlM2RkM2Q1NjUyNjdmNDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commit/3032862ec37e25f64bbcc7bd18059a1c663eb5e9","sha":"3032862ec37e25f64bbcc7bd18059a1c663eb5e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commits/3032862ec37e25f64bbcc7bd18059a1c663eb5e9"}],"sha":"128db93050daaf7c86c45b1a3e3dd3d565267f42","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commits/128db93050daaf7c86c45b1a3e3dd3d565267f42"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28607748?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FullStackChef","id":28607748,"login":"FullStackChef","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4NjA3NzQ4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commits/3032862ec37e25f64bbcc7bd18059a1c663eb5e9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-19T06:18:59Z","email":"brett@fieldstate.io","name":"Brett Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-19T06:18:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(traceability): model rework — SystemRequirement=Rule + Scenario 5th kind (#92)\n\n* docs(traceability): revise spec to the 5-kind Rule model (Scenario is its own kind)\n\nRestores the Gherkin Rule as a layer between feature and scenario, per Brett''s\ncorrection: a SystemRequirement IS a Gherkin Rule (groups scenarios, no steps of\nits own), and Scenario becomes the fifth file-native kind (references its parent\nRule; carries given/when/then/examples). Evidence keys on the scenario slug.\nThree meters: scenario coverage, userReq coverage, pass rate. Adds the empty-rule\nfinding. Supersedes the earlier \"file IS the scenario\" cut (§9.1 resolved).\n\nReworks req-schema/trace-model/trace-emitters/trace-studio to follow.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(traceability): rework req-schema to the 5-kind Rule model (#69)\n\nFollows the spec revision on this branch. SystemRequirement is now a Gherkin\nRule and Scenario becomes the fifth file-native kind.\n\n- SystemRequirement (Rule) — `{ title, feature, userReqs[], links? }`; drops\n  `given`/`when`/`then`/`examples` (a Rule groups scenarios, it has no steps).\n- Scenario (NEW) — `{ title, systemRequirement (→ requirements/system/*),\n  given?, when?, then, examples? }` at `.workspec/scenarios/<slug>.yaml`. The\n  exact step shape SystemRequirement used to carry, plus the parent-Rule ref.\n- TYPE_DIRECTORIES: `Scenario → ''scenarios''`; ARTIFACT_KINDS gains Scenario.\n- JSON schemas: `system-requirement.schema.json` regenerated to the Rule shape,\n  new `scenario.schema.json`; four req-schema schemas at the flat v1alpha1 base,\n  drift byte-clean.\n- Fixtures: the §4 examples (the `inline-create` Rule + its two Scenarios) plus\n  invalid `scenario-missing-then` / `scenario-bad-sysreq-ref` /\n  `system-requirement-missing-feature`. Removed the two now-meaningless invalid\n  sysreq fixtures (a Rule has no `then`); the stray-key-stripping they proved is\n  re-covered by a unit test.\n\nEvidence (`TestRun.results`) now keys on the SCENARIO slug — semantic, no schema\nchange. Reuses schema-core primitives; wiring (tsc -b, references, exports\nsubpath) intact. 75 tests green. Opus-reviewed: no defects.\n\nDownstream (trace-model / trace-emitters / trace-studio) still reference the old\nSystemRequirement steps and are reworked in the following PRs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(traceability): rework trace-model to the 5-kind Rule model (#70)\n\nMoves the evidence join down a layer — from system-requirement to scenario —\nand adds the Rule derivation on top, per the revised spec §4.6/§4.7.\n\n- Input `TraceTree` gains `scenarios`; `ScenarioNode` carries the per-scenario\n  proof/evidence (keyed on the scenario slug; absent from the latest run →\n  `unproven`).\n- `SysReqNode` is now a Rule: `{ ..., scenarios[], ruleProven, empty }` — no\n  proof of its own. `ruleProven` = has ≥1 scenario AND every scenario passes;\n  `empty` = no scenarios.\n- `UserReqNode` gains `provenBy` (the ruleProven verifiers); `covered` = ≥1\n  ruleProven verifier.\n- THREE meters, never collapsed: `scenarioCoverage` (scenarios with a result ÷\n  all), `userReqCoverage` (userReqs with ≥1 ruleProven verifier ÷ all),\n  `passRate` (passing ÷ evidenced scenarios).\n- Findings gain `empty-rule`; `dangling-ref` now checks `scenario.systemRequirement`;\n  `duplicate-slug` covers all five kinds.\n- `build-model.ts` split into single-purpose derivation modules (per the house\n  layout). Golden worked-example reworked to five kinds. 39 tests green.\n\nOpus-reviewed: all three meters hand-recomputed (6/7, 1/4, 4/6), ruleProven''s\nunproven-scenario case correct, no defects.\n\nAlso fixes the now-stale TSDoc on req-schema''s `TestRun` (evidence keys on the\nscenario slug, not the sysreq).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(traceability): rework trace-emitters to the 5-kind Rule model (#71)\n\n`emit` now takes Rules with their scenarios and writes one `.feature` file per\nRule, nested `Feature:` › `Rule:` › `Scenario:` (spec §3). Each scenario carries\nits own scenario slug as the `@<scenario-slug>` tag — the round-trip binding.\n\n- New contract: `RuleWithScenarios = { sysreq, scenarios[] }`; `emit(rules)`.\n  `SysReqInput` → `RuleInput`/`ScenarioInput`. Conventions updated to\n  `feature-file-per-rule` / `rule-groups-scenarios` / `req-tag-on-scenario` /\n  `outline-from-examples`.\n- `ingest` mechanism byte-identical (it always keyed on whatever `@tag` held);\n  the recovered slug is now a SCENARIO slug, so `TestRun.results` keys on\n  scenarios. Defensive parsing + outline-row fold preserved.\n- `mockCucumberRun` + round-trip conformance are scenario-level: emit → mock run\n  → ingest → `buildModel` → assert every scenario''s `proof === ''pass''`, plus a\n  new check that a failing scenario flips its Rule''s `ruleProven` and the\n  userReq''s `covered` to false. 41 tests green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(traceability): rework workspec-trace CLI to the 5-kind Rule model (#72)\n\nMigrates the CLI to the Rule + Scenario model and closes the two review nits.\n\n- Loader (`fs-repository.ts`) walks the new `.workspec/scenarios/` kind, validates\n  `ScenarioArtifact`, and populates `TraceTree.scenarios`; SystemRequirement\n  validates against the reshaped Rule.\n- `emit` groups scenarios by their parent Rule and writes one `.feature` per\n  Rule; `--feature` filters Rules before grouping. It now **warns** on a scenario\n  whose `systemRequirement` names a non-existent Rule (previously dropped\n  silently) — verify already flags it as a dangling-ref, but a bare emit gave no\n  feedback.\n- `verify` renders THREE meters (scenario coverage · userReq coverage · pass\n  rate), never collapsed; gate fails on loader issues, error findings, or a meter\n  below its floor. Three opt-in threshold flags replace the old two. The\n  `empty-rule` finding surfaces as a warning. Exit codes 0/1/2 unchanged.\n- The tree→Rules-with-scenarios grouping is extracted to a single shared helper\n  `groupScenariosByRule` in `@workspec/trace-emitters` (new `grouping.ts`),\n  consumed by both the emitter''s conformance harness and the CLI — no more\n  duplicated grouping logic across packages.\n\n5-kind CLI fixtures; round-trip emit→ingest→verify + exit-code + loader tests.\nWhole workspace green (root typecheck, `pnpm -r build`, all suites). Reviewed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3e5d0f19afe92dbddf267bf5397892c37f73e569","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/git/trees/3e5d0f19afe92dbddf267bf5397892c37f73e569"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/git/commits/3032862ec37e25f64bbcc7bd18059a1c663eb5e9","verification":{"payload":"tree 3e5d0f19afe92dbddf267bf5397892c37f73e569\nparent 64b106e030481b760ee640139268f7d500d11c8b\nauthor Brett Smith <brett@fieldstate.io> 1784441939 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784441939 +1200\n\nfeat(traceability): model r