) now keys on the SCENARIO slug — semantic, no schema\nchange. Reuses schema-core primitives; wiring (tsc -b, references, exports\nsubpath) intact. 75 tests green. Opus-reviewed: no defects.\n\nDownstream (trace-model / trace-emitters / trace-studio) still reference the old\nSystemRequirement steps and are reworked in the following PRs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(traceability): rework trace-model to the 5-kind Rule model (#70)\n\nMoves the evidence join down a layer — from system-requirement to scenario —\nand adds the Rule derivation on top, per the revised spec §4.6/§4.7.\n\n- Input `TraceTree` gains `scenarios`; `ScenarioNode` carries the per-scenario\n  proof/evidence (keyed on the scenario slug; absent from the latest run →\n  `unproven`).\n- `SysReqNode` is now a Rule: `{ ..., scenarios[], ruleProven, empty }` — no\n  proof of its own. `ruleProven` = has ≥1 scenario AND every scenario passes;\n  `empty` = no scenarios.\n- `UserReqNode` gains `provenBy` (the ruleProven verifiers); `covered` = ≥1\n  ruleProven verifier.\n- THREE meters, never collapsed: `scenarioCoverage` (scenarios with a result ÷\n  all), `userReqCoverage` (userReqs with ≥1 ruleProven verifier ÷ all),\n  `passRate` (passing ÷ evidenced scenarios).\n- Findings gain `empty-rule`; `dangling-ref` now checks `scenario.systemRequirement`;\n  `duplicate-slug` covers all five kinds.\n- `build-model.ts` split into single-purpose derivation modules (per the house\n  layout). Golden worked-example reworked to five kinds. 39 tests green.\n\nOpus-reviewed: all three meters hand-recomputed (6/7, 1/4, 4/6), ruleProven''s\nunproven-scenario case correct, no defects.\n\nAlso fixes the now-stale TSDoc on req-schema''s `TestRun` (evidence keys on the\nscenario slug, not the sysreq).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(traceability): rework trace-emitters to the 5-kind Rule model (#71)\n\n`emit` now takes Rules with their scenarios and writes one `.feature` file per\nRule, nested `Feature:` › `Rule:` › `Scenario:` (spec §3). Each scenario carries\nits own scenario slug as the `@<scenario-slug>` tag — the round-trip binding.\n\n- New contract: `RuleWithScenarios = { sysreq, scenarios[] }`; `emit(rules)`.\n  `SysReqInput` → `RuleInput`/`ScenarioInput`. Conventions updated to\n  `feature-file-per-rule` / `rule-groups-scenarios` / `req-tag-on-scenario` /\n  `outline-from-examples`.\n- `ingest` mechanism byte-identical (it always keyed on whatever `@tag` held);\n  the recovered slug is now a SCENARIO slug, so `TestRun.results` keys on\n  scenarios. Defensive parsing + outline-row fold preserved.\n- `mockCucumberRun` + round-trip conformance are scenario-level: emit → mock run\n  → ingest → `buildModel` → assert every scenario''s `proof === ''pass''`, plus a\n  new check that a failing scenario flips its Rule''s `ruleProven` and the\n  userReq''s `covered` to false. 41 tests green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(traceability): rework workspec-trace CLI to the 5-kind Rule model (#72)\n\nMigrates the CLI to the Rule + Scenario model and closes the two review nits.\n\n- Loader (`fs-repository.ts`) walks the new `.workspec/scenarios/` kind, validates\n  `ScenarioArtifact`, and populates `TraceTree.scenarios`; SystemRequirement\n  validates against the reshaped Rule.\n- `emit` groups scenarios by their parent Rule and writes one `.feature` per\n  Rule; `--feature` filters Rules before grouping. It now **warns** on a scenario\n  whose `systemRequirement` names a non-existent Rule (previously dropped\n  silently) — verify already flags it as a dangling-ref, but a bare emit gave no\n  feedback.\n- `verify` renders THREE meters (scenario coverage · userReq coverage · pass\n  rate), never collapsed; gate fails on loader issues, error findings, or a meter\n  below its floor. Three opt-in threshold flags replace the old two. The\n  `empty-rule` finding surfaces as a warning. Exit codes 0/1/2 unchanged.\n- The tree→Rules-with-scenarios grouping is extracted to a single shared helper\n  `groupScenariosByRule` in `@workspec/trace-emitters` (new `grouping.ts`),\n  consumed by both the emitter''s conformance harness and the CLI — no more\n  duplicated grouping logic across packages.\n\n5-kind CLI fixtures; round-trip emit→ingest→verify + exit-code + loader tests.\nWhole workspace green (root typecheck, `pnpm -r build`, all suites). Reviewed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqXGxTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAajcQALDq5wuEt7gNqi16YEvT4gI1\nbnC3ZzC0KtrwXNNu9o2g3oTB+cyXU7MPE3kAOyw/sBIKEKE+QAgVBhjITcpMDZbA\nWrREdCbtuJAsmrkXciCmWhcf4QJj7Zh8Cvlzp8wAKguRaBrIcoT7fAU5+m1ssAr4\nWpx9hBS76WNDZwaXiiytXUFF2Om68OKnejGvMWRpD14E9wIrjbnwyJliCZAu3RJ9\nQn55zY7CujzCQ0TDlz3euuY8j9Dzj/DfRL/FMu9jYl9+TnVnQYZFIeeL+HO28WoM\n+k/u6bYX3qNBGnUp/B1QwKhpcu0guY8VOJRB/C0EpuI7tlo1nmEdw4HNU5VhCO3a\nWtk0VMe0Wnc1AUS5u7u6wonhUaptxKq9N15AvzGC2JV6zoDkUzHcp6qyhOFtps2D\nI9JEcC4g8rOAWgqzD1yxmjRIkmo6kXqyCfGTeJyUpfUNTsgE39hoXuZC6p6iqQrw\nlJHE8PgMNVRgHXAbcGTh13hO7gVUf3SxHV628IvSBswzaWlPKeW51Cy8/bxkmml0\nnm72SEwZA+R7g3cogqsV3Eo+RnS9zyPFMTeCzyoIc3IvYNBU3ZAQ2RTRt8pLCJ63\nxvD2unsfXvV4ejFR9Wp1eYKkde44CghIOVQ3Le35tFVB7LUBtfj2dTicnW+kiJXp\ncuU+niaHguGU65ELzftn\n=jzdV\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-19T06:19:00Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commit/3032862ec37e25f64bbcc7bd18059a1c663eb5e9","node_id":"C_kwDOTPvB8toAKDMwMzI4NjJlYzM3ZTI1ZjY0YmJjYzdiZDE4MDU5YTFjNjYzZWI1ZTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commit/64b106e030481b760ee640139268f7d500d11c8b","sha":"64b106e030481b760ee640139268f7d500d11c8b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commits/64b106e030481b760ee640139268f7d500d11c8b"}],"sha":"3032862ec37e25f64bbcc7bd18059a1c663eb5e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commits/3032862ec37e25f64bbcc7bd18059a1c663eb5e9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28607748?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FullStackChef","id":28607748,"login":"FullStackChef","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4NjA3NzQ4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commits/64b106e030481b760ee640139268f7d500d11c8b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-19T03:37:14Z","email":"brett@fieldstate.io","name":"Brett Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-19T03:37:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(traceability): workspec-trace CLI — emit/ingest/verify (T4, #72) (#91)\n\n`@workspec/trace-studio`: the standalone `workspec-trace` CLI — spec §8''s\nshippable value with zero frontend. Ties the loader + req-schema validation +\ntrace-model derivation + the cucumber seam into three verbs. `run(argv, io,\ndeps)` is the testable entry point (injectable IO + repository + clock);\n`bin.ts` is the only thing touching `process`.\n\n- **FsRepository** (the fs boundary trace-model deliberately lacks) — walks the\n  `.workspec/` tree (actors/, features/, requirements/{user,system}/), parses\n  YAML, validates each file against its req-schema Zod artifact via a STRUCTURAL\n  validator (no direct zod dep, like cost-studio), derives the slug from the\n  FILENAME (the file is the identity), and attaches the repo-relative source.\n  Validation failures are collected as `LoadIssue[]` and returned, never thrown;\n  every read is path-contained to the root.\n- **emit** `--emitter cucumber [--feature <slug>] [--out <dir>]` — sysreqs →\n  `.feature` files written under `--out` (default `features/`).\n- **ingest** `<results> --emitter cucumber [--id --sha --ci --runs-dir]` —\n  cucumber JSON → `TestRun`, written to `.workspec/.runs/<id>.json` (spec §4.5;\n  gitignore-able per §9.3). id/ts default to the injectable clock (the CLI is the\n  impure boundary; the emitter stays pure).\n- **verify** `[--min-coverage --min-pass-rate] [--json]` — the CI gate: loads\n  the tree + runs, derives the model, and FAILS (exit 1) on any loader issue, any\n  error finding (dangling intra-tree ref / duplicate slug, spec §4.7), or a meter\n  below its floor. Both meters shown side by side, never collapsed (§5).\n  Thresholds opt-in (default 0); error findings always gate. Exit codes: 0 pass,\n  1 gate fail, 2 usage.\n\nConsumes req-schema + schema-core + trace-model + trace-emitters via TS project\nreferences (typecheck `tsc -b`). CLI round-trip + exit-code + loader tests\n(39 green); bin.js carries the `#!/usr/bin/env node` shebang.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"55c74978f27ae589f379c91ddf7a0242e1d7174b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/git/trees/55c74978f27ae589f379c91ddf7a0242e1d7174b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/git/commits/64b106e030481b760ee640139268f7d500d11c8b","verification":{"payload":"tree 55c74978f27ae589f379c91ddf7a0242e1d7174b\nparent c4cd09c21f5afc22ab6f0e0f373579bd04713f92\nauthor Brett Smith <brett@fieldstate.io> 1784432234 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784432234 +1200\n\nfeat(traceability): workspec-trace CLI — emit/ingest/verify (T4, #72) (#91)\n\n`@workspec/trace-studio`: the standalone `workspec-trace` CLI — spec §8''s\nshippable value with zero frontend. Ties the loader + req-schema validation +\ntrace-model derivation + the cucumber seam into three verbs. `run(argv, io,\ndeps)` is the testable entry point (injectable IO + repository + clock);\n`bin.ts` is the only thing touching `process`.\n\n- **FsRepository** (the fs boundary trace-model deliberately lacks) — walks the\n  `.workspec/` tree (actors/, features/, requirements/{user,system}/), parses\n  YAML, validates each file against its req-schema Zod artifact via a STRUCTURAL\n  validator (no direct zod dep, like cost-studio), derives the slug from the\n  FILENAME (the file is the identity), and attaches the repo-relative source.\n  Validation failures are collected as `LoadIssue[]` and returned, never thrown;\n  every read is path-contained to the root.\n- **emit** `--emitter cucumber [--feature <slug>] [--out <dir>]` — sysreqs →\n  `.feature` files written under `--out` (default `features/`).\n- **ingest** `<results> --emitter cucumber [--id --sha --ci --runs-dir]` —\n  cucumber JSON → `TestRun`, written to `.workspec/.runs/<id>.json` (spec §4.5;\n  gitignore-able per §9.3). id/ts default to the injectable clock (the CLI is the\n  impure boundary; the emitter stays pure).\n- **verify** `[--min-coverage --min-pass-rate] [--json]` — the CI gate: loads\n  the tree + runs, derives the model, and FAILS (exit 1) on any loader issue, any\n  error finding (dangling intra-tree ref / duplicate slug, spec §4.7), or a meter\n  below its floor. Both meters shown side by side, never collapsed (§5).\n  Thresholds opt-in (default 0); error findings always gate. Exit codes: 0 pass,\n  1 gate fail, 2 usage.\n\nConsumes req-schema + schema-core + trace-model + trace-emitters via TS project\nreferences (typecheck `tsc -b`). CLI round-trip + exit-code + loader tests\n(39 green); bin.js carries the `#!/usr/bin/env node` shebang.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqXEZqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPDcQACF0RiEcFVATg/aQTWPBYQP4\nTOEFrq3ZQ0LoUB9lga3rUhnBJa2POc2+dJlUMvlsXaBUFUS0m8Xz0LOhm2rOpSAJ\nFn4xpTKTGLWjWsU5dXPinwSls3Nr9RudrIMJgtMTGp4/oSGl77tgxhGMQj/t06OH\nLG+xctPgP/C5+DeowTQfacL1hFcCx3bYuWUsw59kDPjpx1+8NkNgJ6mWUNU7TaH5\nULr2H3DPfVxWW7JOZRnV4p41hhxamQp8dHMXVsorhjaifjcCfsqC2Tw9pJuX+5/+\nAcykOgMTgevA62NvfrNMnBd3XMh8b95q54virAIlQrr+IakZ5Jw/5T9c2JL9BR8r\n/44az0YO2NgGXaEsfLoEaiiXnK62l/4hiB2xLqur32lxKlP/30XWVB3p5BknXfqT\nMefvrociRpq3cppgtAdO9EK6mqgnRc0HlQrBnKy2TBidEfgEK3d+Df4DAMI24IL4\nOhhOOsEKjTblrzqNqE5uSqH7oRm4Nj4SPfgQNQUZvMjVuveaCq4gi5ShS+mNTh6Q\n6fIBOuIeGi9ShJvlHpRoSR+s0yKM73jLYsDelrwmFjgn2oISqzOHGSzoKHqe0dc0\nBMzKqQLmt5hJ1hrUroSDSNyMOy2oW/jjuBr3Bi83HwXL/FDrqCSFfzGULoluqCqu\nsP0+j0I6011RWLibHXCk\n=dzr6\n-----END