.github.com/users/FullStackChef/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FullStackChef","id":28607748,"login":"FullStackChef","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4NjA3NzQ4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commits/c4cd09c21f5afc22ab6f0e0f373579bd04713f92/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-19T00:56:21Z","email":"brett@fieldstate.io","name":"Brett Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-19T00:56:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(traceability): trace-emitters — cucumber emit+ingest seam (T3, #71) (#90)\n\n`@workspec/trace-emitters`: the provider seam binding SysReq artifacts to a test\ntoolchain in both directions, with `cucumber` as the first concrete emitter.\nPure functions — no IO, no clock, never throws.\n\n- `Emitter` contract — `{ name, conventions, emit(sysreqs)→EmittedFile[],\n  ingest(raw, meta)→TestRun }`. Adding a framework = adding an emitter, nothing\n  else. `emit` takes `{slug, sysreq}` (the loader-derived slug is authoritative —\n  metadata.slug is optional in schema-core), returns file descriptors (the T4 CLI\n  writes them); `ingest` is clock-free (RunMeta supplies id/ts/sha/ci).\n- cucumber `emit` — one `.feature` per sysreq (`feature-file-per-sysreq`), the\n  `@<slug>` tag (`req-tag-on-scenario`, the load-bearing binding), and Scenario\n  Outline + Examples for a sysreq with an `examples` table (`outline-from-examples`).\n  Continuation steps map to `And` with a redundant leading \"and\"/\"but\" stripped.\n  Byte-stable output (sorted, snapshot-tested).\n- cucumber `ingest` — parses Cucumber JSON defensively (never throws on garbage),\n  recovers the slug from the `@tag`, aggregates steps to one verdict (any fail →\n  fail; all passed → pass; else skip), folds outline rows (fail > skip > pass),\n  and produces a `TestRun` keyed on the sysreq slug alone (spec §4.5).\n- Round-trip conformance (the acceptance bar) — reusable, emitter-agnostic\n  `roundTrip`/`assertRoundTrip`: emit → mock run → ingest → `buildModel`, asserting\n  each sysreq''s derived `proof === ''pass''`. \"Proven\" is semantic (the same\n  judgement the meters/UI make), not a string match. Negative cases covered\n  (a failing/skipped scenario → fail/skip → unproven). trace-model is a runtime\n  dependency because the harness is exported for future emitters to self-test.\n\nConsumes req-schema + trace-model via TS project references (typecheck `tsc -b`).\n38/38 tests green (incl. emit snapshots, ingest edge cases, round-trip).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2d1bd87718f492a220017f414a3c1b92281195b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/git/trees/2d1bd87718f492a220017f414a3c1b92281195b4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/git/commits/c4cd09c21f5afc22ab6f0e0f373579bd04713f92","verification":{"payload":"tree 2d1bd87718f492a220017f414a3c1b92281195b4\nparent d0bd8ee6f9b606a187001528b0a0ebf147dac853\nauthor Brett Smith <brett@fieldstate.io> 1784422581 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784422581 +1200\n\nfeat(traceability): trace-emitters — cucumber emit+ingest seam (T3, #71) (#90)\n\n`@workspec/trace-emitters`: the provider seam binding SysReq artifacts to a test\ntoolchain in both directions, with `cucumber` as the first concrete emitter.\nPure functions — no IO, no clock, never throws.\n\n- `Emitter` contract — `{ name, conventions, emit(sysreqs)→EmittedFile[],\n  ingest(raw, meta)→TestRun }`. Adding a framework = adding an emitter, nothing\n  else. `emit` takes `{slug, sysreq}` (the loader-derived slug is authoritative —\n  metadata.slug is optional in schema-core), returns file descriptors (the T4 CLI\n  writes them); `ingest` is clock-free (RunMeta supplies id/ts/sha/ci).\n- cucumber `emit` — one `.feature` per sysreq (`feature-file-per-sysreq`), the\n  `@<slug>` tag (`req-tag-on-scenario`, the load-bearing binding), and Scenario\n  Outline + Examples for a sysreq with an `examples` table (`outline-from-examples`).\n  Continuation steps map to `And` with a redundant leading \"and\"/\"but\" stripped.\n  Byte-stable output (sorted, snapshot-tested).\n- cucumber `ingest` — parses Cucumber JSON defensively (never throws on garbage),\n  recovers the slug from the `@tag`, aggregates steps to one verdict (any fail →\n  fail; all passed → pass; else skip), folds outline rows (fail > skip > pass),\n  and produces a `TestRun` keyed on the sysreq slug alone (spec §4.5).\n- Round-trip conformance (the acceptance bar) — reusable, emitter-agnostic\n  `roundTrip`/`assertRoundTrip`: emit → mock run → ingest → `buildModel`, asserting\n  each sysreq''s derived `proof === ''pass''`. \"Proven\" is semantic (the same\n  judgement the meters/UI make), not a string match. Negative cases covered\n  (a failing/skipped scenario → fail/skip → unproven). trace-model is a runtime\n  dependency because the harness is exported for future emitters to self-test.\n\nConsumes req-schema + trace-model via TS project references (typecheck `tsc -b`).\n38/38 tests green (incl. emit snapshots, ingest edge cases, round-trip).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqXCC1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArZsQAIWAqlpEcACz1/0O+KSlliZi\nYG9uQ563zyd40XM9IfO+qnNV9xKopqROOfBlDm/KKrFtEMXXqcDSUJ65IieyE03I\nUszDu4OAOw8ObPVfPLoVWEUrx7I5L8Xa0ADSFd/Bc7zKrH2vkUjelqkAWO4frTIk\niFZfMqM