-studio/commits/d0bd8ee6f9b606a187001528b0a0ebf147dac853"}],"sha":"c4cd09c21f5afc22ab6f0e0f373579bd04713f92","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commits/c4cd09c21f5afc22ab6f0e0f373579bd04713f92"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28607748?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FullStackChef","id":28607748,"login":"FullStackChef","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4NjA3NzQ4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commits/d0bd8ee6f9b606a187001528b0a0ebf147dac853/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-19T00:30:58Z","email":"brett@fieldstate.io","name":"Brett Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-19T00:30:58Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(traceability): trace-model — pure derivation engine (T2, #70) (#89)\n\n`@workspec/trace-model`: `buildModel(tree, runs) → TraceModel` — the pure,\ndeterministic, normative derivation of the traceability graph per spec §4.6.\nNo IO/DOM/React, never throws (every problem is a structured Finding), every\narray deterministically sorted so the golden snapshot is byte-stable.\n\nDerives (never stores):\n- evidence join — each SystemRequirement → its latest-run verdict keyed on the\n  sysreq slug alone (§4.5); pass/fail/skip/absence distinct, absence → unproven.\n- `verifies` edges; per-userReq `verifiedBy` / `passingSysReqs` / `covered`.\n- Coverage meter (userReq-centric, spec §4.6): userReqs with ≥1 PASSING verifying\n  sysreq ÷ all userReqs — this is what makes orphan-userReq the headline finding.\n  (Supersedes issue #70''s pre-validation sysreq-centric coverage.)\n- Pass-rate meter (sysreq-centric): passing ÷ sysreqs with evidence in the latest\n  run. Two separate meters, never collapsed (§5). Each exposes numerator/\n  denominator/ratio.\n- Findings (data, never thrown): orphan-user-requirement (headline),\n  orphan-feature, dangling-ref (intra-tree bare-slug refs only — cross-layer\n  `links` are inert, §4.7), duplicate-slug.\n\nPure by construction: input is located artifacts ({slug, artifact, source}) the\nT4 loader supplies; the engine never reads the filesystem. v0 is latest-run-only\n(§9.4) and single-tree (§9.5). Golden-fixture snapshot + unit tests (30 green).\n\nConsumes `@workspec/req-schema` via a TS project reference (typecheck is `tsc -b`,\nresolving req-schema→schema-core from source — no pre-built dist needed).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e9253598f25a042373a2f895bed340c683bd6100","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/git/trees/e9253598f25a042373a2f895bed340c683bd6100"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/git/commits/d0bd8ee6f9b606a187001528b0a0ebf147dac853","verification":{"payload":"tree e9253598f25a042373a2f895bed340c683bd6100\nparent 6b0171bbc5e3f64e777597c67d02c404ac541f4d\nauthor Brett Smith <brett@fieldstate.io> 1784421058 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784421058 +1200\n\nfeat(traceability): trace-model — pure derivation engine (T2, #70) (#89)\n\n`@workspec/trace-model`: `buildModel(tree, runs) → TraceModel` — the pure,\ndeterministic, normative derivation of the traceability graph per spec §4.6.\nNo IO/DOM/React, never throws (every problem is a structured Finding), every\narray deterministically sorted so the golden snapshot is byte-stable.\n\nDerives (never stores):\n- evidence join — each SystemRequirement → its latest-run verdict keyed on the\n  sysreq slug alone (§4.5); pass/fail/skip/absence distinct, absence → unproven.\n- `verifies` edges; per-userReq `verifiedBy` / `passingSysReqs` / `covered`.\n- Coverage meter (userReq-centric, spec §4.6): userReqs with ≥1 PASSING verifying\n  sysreq ÷ all userReqs — this is what makes orphan-userReq the headline finding.\n  (Supersedes issue #70''s pre-validation sysreq-centric coverage.)\n- Pass-rate meter (sysreq-centric): passing ÷ sysreqs with evidence in the latest\n  run. Two separate meters, never collapsed (§5). Each exposes numerator/\n  denominator/ratio.\n- Findings (data, never thrown): orphan-user-requirement (headline),\n  orphan-feature, dangling-ref (intra-tree bare-slug refs only — cross-layer\n  `links` are inert, §4.7), duplicate-slug.\n\nPure by construction: input is located artifacts ({slug, artifact, source}) the\nT4 loader supplies; the engine never reads the filesystem. v0 is latest-run-only\n(§9.4) and single-tree (§9.5). Golden-fixture snapshot + unit tests (30 green).\n\nConsumes `@workspec/req-schema` via a TS project reference (typecheck is `tsc -b`,\nresolving req-schema→schema-core from source — no pre-built dist needed).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqXBrCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5bsQAFLtuORdUgDgO7SdVUmXVp1m\nk4nbYujW4GcZB1WEioAow7VHj+FOvsaVcpUDND1v8w7komEIstg66LaaA/q3pP46\np/GDuaS3NGOpYEvpDv/3TCmAI86GfFOxyY+Low9tqR5Fhc2hMStVw7HI52Qavn4y\nppde1ARKC70D3YfxsTKUhzC1UbaL20d4qR8ILUR+Alq8+xdVkqiJ418wvObGQUBu\n2iOsZWADMLBfLZ/A57hbwXWOV+MS2VjKKZ9tcoJcFkFc7Av9rYQ25R5f7peSzOcI\ncgiOkKVNhLm/MWKrZho0IUaFDO9KHLWi1Z9Aev6Gc50YxkcZZFI