mmits/d0bd8ee6f9b606a187001528b0a0ebf147dac853"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28607748?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FullStackChef","id":28607748,"login":"FullStackChef","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4NjA3NzQ4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commits/6b0171bbc5e3f64e777597c67d02c404ac541f4d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-19T00:06:47Z","email":"brett@fieldstate.io","name":"Brett Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-19T00:06:47Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(traceability): req-schema — four artifact kinds, the schema freeze (T1, #69) (#88)\n\n* feat(traceability): req-schema — four artifact kinds, the schema freeze (T1, #69)\n\nFreezes the WorkSpec Traceability Workbench artifact model per the validated\nspec (docs/traceability/spec.md §4). Option B — four file-native kinds, each a\nK8s-style envelope (apiVersion/kind/metadata/spec) built on @workspec/schema-core''s\n`defineArtifact`, `.workspec/<dir>/<slug>.yaml`, slug = identity.\n\nKinds:\n- Actor — re-exported from schema-core (the shared kind); its dir + schema stay\n  owned by schema-core.\n- Feature (`features/`) — { name, product? }.\n- UserRequirement (`requirements/user/`) — the artifact the RTM traces:\n  { title, actor, as, want, so, features[], status: draft|agreed|implemented|\n  verified, links? }.\n- SystemRequirement (`requirements/system/`) — THE FILE IS THE SCENARIO: one\n  Gherkin scenario per file, { title, feature, userReqs[], given?, when?, then,\n  examples? }. No nested `scenarios[]`, no scenario id (spec §9.1 correction) —\n  a stray `scenarios[]` is stripped and the file fails on absent `then`.\n\nRefs (§4.7): intra-tree single-kind fields (actor/feature/features/userReqs) are\nbare slugs; cross-layer `links` reuse schema-core''s shared `linksField` (pathRef).\nThe spec''s illustrative `need:<slug>` kind-qualified shorthand is deferred, not\nfrozen — it depends on Enterprise''s parent-kind chain (flagged unconfirmed in\nspec §9.2). Documented on the `links` field.\n\nAlso: `TestRun` evidence type (§4.5, flat — machine-ingested, keys on the sysreq\nslug, pass|fail|skip|absence distinct); JSON-Schema gen for the three req-schema\nkinds at the flat `https://schema.workspec.io/v1alpha1/` base with a byte-exact\ndrift test; valid fixtures reproducing the §4 examples + invalid fixtures failing\nper-kind on their intended field. Reuses schema-core''s `buildJsonSchema`/`Slug`/\n`linksField`/`MetadataSchema` — zero duplicated primitives. 60/60 tests green.\n\nAdds the generated `json-schema/` subpath to `exports` (was in `files` only) and\nto `.prettierignore`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(traceability): wire req-schema→schema-core TS project reference (T1, #69)\n\nCI runs typecheck BEFORE build, so no `dist/` exists when req-schema\ntype-checks — `tsc --noEmit` then can''t resolve `@workspec/schema-core`''s\ndeclarations. Match the established dependent-package pattern (packages/c4-model):\nuse `tsc -b` and add a TS project `references` entry to\n`../schema-core/tsconfig.build.json` in both tsconfig.json and\ntsconfig.build.json, so typecheck builds schema-core''s declarations on demand\nfrom source and never has to run after build.\n\nVerified from a clean (no-dist) tree: `pnpm run typecheck`, `pnpm run build`,\nand req-schema''s 60 tests all green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7480d7f96f73b5907bb51b1e5706920462605447","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/git/trees/7480d7f96f73b5907bb51b1e5706920462605447"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/git/commits/6b0171bbc5e3f64e777597c67d02c404ac541f4d","verification":{"payload":"tree 7480d7f96f73b5907bb51b1e5706920462605447\nparent f7e567a4c6c4331af648514ed3af24bb1c5e68da\nauthor Brett Smith <brett@fieldstate.io> 1784419607 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784419607 +1200\n\nfeat(traceability): req-schema — four artifact kinds, the schema freeze (T1, #69) (#88)\n\n* feat(traceability): req-schema — four artifact kinds, the schema freeze (T1, #69)\n\nFreezes the WorkSpec Traceability Workbench artifact model per the validated\nspec (docs/traceability/spec.md §4). Option B — four file-native kinds, each a\nK8s-style envelope (apiVersion/kind/metadata/spec) built on @workspec/schema-core''s\n`defineArtifact`, `.workspec/<dir>/<slug>.yaml`, slug = identity.\n\nKinds:\n- Actor — re-exported from schema-core (the shared kind); its dir + schema stay\n  owned by schema-core.\n- Feature (`features/`) — { name, product? }.\n- UserRequirement (`requirements/user/`) — the artifact the RTM traces:\n  { title, actor, as, want, so, features[], status: draft|agreed|implemented|\n  verified, links? }.\n- SystemRequirement (`requirements/system/`) — THE FILE IS THE SCENARIO: one\n  Gherkin scenario per file, { title, feature, userReqs[], given?, when?, then,\n  examples? }. No nested `scenarios[]`, no scenario id (spec §9.1 correction) —\n  a stray `scenarios[]` is stripped and the file fails on absent `then`.\n\nRefs (§4.7): intra-tree single-kind fields (actor/feature/features/userReqs) are\nbare slugs; cross-layer `links` reuse schema-core''s shared `linksField` (pathRef).\nThe spec''s illustrative `need:<slug>` kind-qualified shorthand is deferred, not\nfrozen — it depends on Enterprise''s parent-kind chain (flagged unconfirmed in\nspec §9.2). Documented on the `links` field.\n\nAlso: `TestRun` evidence type (§4.5, flat — machine-ingested, keys on the sysreq\nslug, pass|fail|skip|absence distinct); JSON-Schema gen for the three req-schema\nkinds at the flat `https://schema.workspec.io/v1alpha1/` base with a byte-exact\ndrift test; valid fixtures reproducing the §4 examples + invalid fixtures failing\nper-kind on their intended field. Reuses schema-core''s `buildJsonSchema`/`Slug`/\n`linksField`/`MetadataSchema` — zero duplicated primitives. 60/60 tests green.\n\nAdds the generated `json-schema/` subpath to `exports` (was in `files` only) and\nto `.prettierignore`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(traceability): wire req-schema→schema-core TS project reference (T1, #69)\n\nCI runs typecheck BEFORE build, so no `dist/` exists when req-schema\ntype-checks — `tsc --noEmit` then can''t resolve `@workspec/schema-core`''s\ndeclarations. Match the established dependent-package pattern (packages/c4-model):\nuse `tsc -b` and add a TS project `references` entry to\n`../schema-core/tsconfig.build.json` in both tsconfig.json and\ntsconfig.build.json, so typecheck builds schema-core''s declarations on demand\nfrom source and never has to run after build.\n\nVerified from a clean (no-dist) tree: `pnpm run typecheck`, `pnpm run build`,\nand req-schema''s 60 tests all green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQB