s","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FullStackChef","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commits/09e022e49702541b276cf1c3950a0f2f795c7d25/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-14T21:13:11Z","email":"brett@fieldstate.io","name":"Brett Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-14T21:13:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(release): unify all packages at 0.1.0-alpha.5 (#64)\n\nBump every publishable package to a single 0.1.0-alpha.5 for one unified\nrelease: the 15 npm packages (decision alpha.1, c4 alpha.2, cost alpha.1 → all\nalpha.5) and the four Aspire NuGet packages (Directory.Build.props alpha.0 →\nalpha.5). Internal deps use the workspace: protocol, so pnpm pack rewrites them\nto 0.1.0-alpha.5 in the tarballs (verified; no workspace: leaks); the external\n@workspec/design pin stays alpha.1.\n\napps/site pins are left on the currently-published decision alpha.1 / c4 alpha.2\n(they resolve from the registry until alpha.5 is live); a post-publish follow-up\nbumps them to alpha.5. NuGet still requires the one-time nuget.org setup to\nactually publish (see docs/decisions/RELEASING.md).\n\nTo ship: tag v0.1.0-alpha.5 and push — CI republishes all npm packages at\nalpha.5 (fresh build), including a clean cost family over the broken alpha.0.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c8ad7c64f51d83e41e33bfa4782aed252c74d3e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/git/trees/c8ad7c64f51d83e41e33bfa4782aed252c74d3e0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/git/commits/09e022e49702541b276cf1c3950a0f2f795c7d25","verification":{"payload":"tree c8ad7c64f51d83e41e33bfa4782aed252c74d3e0\npar