/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commit/f0b86888a7d6a4b48583aa7657f18a9e95789c19","node_id":"C_kwDOTPvB8toAKGYwYjg2ODg4YTdkNmE0YjQ4NTgzYWE3NjU3ZjE4YTllOTU3ODljMTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commit/9a9bd828ef2361681653a1341abfc5a174e4cc76","sha":"9a9bd828ef2361681653a1341abfc5a174e4cc76","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commits/9a9bd828ef2361681653a1341abfc5a174e4cc76"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commit/a1769067017c5b7712daef840c849c13df3c528e","sha":"a1769067017c5b7712daef840c849c13df3c528e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commits/a1769067017c5b7712daef840c849c13df3c528e"}],"sha":"f0b86888a7d6a4b48583aa7657f18a9e95789c19","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commits/f0b86888a7d6a4b48583aa7657f18a9e95789c19"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commits/a1769067017c5b7712daef840c849c13df3c528e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-13T22:43:02Z","email":"brett@pukekos.co.nz","name":"Brett Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-13T22:43:02Z","email":"brett@pukekos.co.nz","name":"Brett Smith"},"message":"fix(decision-studio): make server tests hermetic under parallel suite runs\n\nDiagnosis: the reported 404-vs-200 flake in server.test.ts was investigated\nagainst a literal port-collision / shared-tempdir-race theory. Mechanistic\ninspection (supertest@7.2.2''s Test#serverAddress calls `app.listen(0)` per\nrequest and closes the ephemeral server immediately in `end()`) shows neither\ndecision-studio''s nor c4-studio''s server.test.ts ever binds a fixed port —\nthe only fixed-port `.listen()` calls live in each package''s serve.ts\n`runServe`, which is exercised only by the CLI/E2E paths, never by any\nvitest-matched *.test.ts. mkdtemp-based temp dirs are also inherently\ncollision-free. ~30 stress runs (15 sequential + 12-way simultaneous\ndecision-studio/c4-studio vitest pairs, 5 full root `pnpm run test` runs)\nproduced zero repro, consistent with that mechanistic finding — stated\nplainly per the task''s fallback allowance.\n\nThe one real hermeticity gap found: server.test.ts''s first describe block\nbuilt its Express app once against the shared, repo-committed\nexamples/hosting-platform directory instead of a per-test mkdtemp copy —\nunlike this file''s own write round-trip block and unlike c4-studio''s\nserver.test.ts, which already mkdtemps for every test (the \"healthier\"\nexisting pattern). Currently nothing writes there (the one PUT test is\nrejected by Zod validation before reaching disk), but examples/hosting-platform\nis read by many other suites across the monorepo (decision-schema,\ndecision-engine, cli.test.ts, decide-roundtrip.test.ts, fs-repository.test.ts),\nso sharing it live via the Express server was the one landmine waiting for a\nfuture edit (e.g. a fixed-up PUT payload) to turn a passing test into one that\ncorrupts a checked-in fixture for every other package''s tests.\n\nFix: give the read-API describe block its own mkdtemp''d copy (ds-host-read-)\nper test, mirroring the write-round-trip block (renamed ds-host-write- for\nclarity) and c4-studio''s pattern. No server-side changes were needed —\nsupertest''s ephemeral binding already satisfies port isolation on both sides.\nc4-studio''s server.test.ts already followed the healthier pattern throughout,\nso it needed no changes.\n\nVerification: root lint, typecheck, and `pnpm run test` all green; 5x\nconcurrent decision-studio + c4-studio vitest runs post-fix, zero failures.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f0518288a8c55888af3b0ef5958cbe9f2b00f0c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/git/trees/f0518288a8c55888af3b0ef5958cbe9f2b00f0c4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/git/commits/a1769067017c5b7712daef840c849c13df3c528e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commit/a1769067017c5b7712daef840c849c13df3c528e","node_id":"C_kwDOTPvB8toAKGExNzY5MDY3MDE3YzViNzcxMmRhZWY4NDBjODQ5YzEzZGYzYzUyOGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commit/9a9bd828ef2361681653a1341abfc5a174e4cc76","sha":"9a9bd828ef2361681653a1341abfc5a174e4cc76","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commits/9a9bd828ef2361681653a1341abfc5a174e4cc76"}],"sha":"a1769067017c5b7712daef840c849c13df3c528e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commits/a1769067017c5b7712daef840c849c13df3c528e"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-studio/commits/9a9bd828ef2361681653a1341abfc5a174e4cc76/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-13T22:23:46Z","email":"brett@pukekos.co.nz","name":"Brett Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-13T22:23:46Z","emai