"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/farxC/open-training/commits/d885378872660055aa75738c14fe1fb64963dbed/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-05T01:17:27Z","email":"rafaelflamengo07@outlook.com","name":"farxC"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-05T01:17:27Z","email":"rafaelflamengo07@outlook.com","name":"farxC"},"message":"Merge branch ''feat/exercise-page-recomposition''\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1809181b0400980bac4e0ba9169818c5541bb524","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/farxC/open-training/git/trees/1809181b0400980bac4e0ba9169818c5541bb524"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/farxC/open-training/git/commits/d885378872660055aa75738c14fe1fb64963dbed","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83882306?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/farxC","id":83882306,"login":"farxC","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODgyMzA2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/farxC/open-training/commit/d885378872660055aa75738c14fe1fb64963dbed","node_id":"C_kwDOTP0lv9oAKGQ4ODUzNzg4NzI2NjAwNTVhYTc1NzM4YzE0ZmUxZmI2NDk2M2RiZWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/farxC/open-training/commit/29a6e090fa50715260e6cfa6eda419b342c79374","sha":"29a6e090fa50715260e6cfa6eda419b342c79374","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/farxC/open-training/commits/29a6e090fa50715260e6cfa6eda419b342c79374"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/farxC/open-training/commit/01e8512134af7aa2cd188732f7e72043a27c1869","sha":"01e8512134af7aa2cd188732f7e72043a27c1869","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/farxC/open-training/commits/01e8512134af7aa2cd188732f7e72043a27c1869"}],"sha":"d885378872660055aa75738c14fe1fb64963dbed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/farxC/open-training/commits/d885378872660055aa75738c14fe1fb64963dbed"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83882306?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/farxC","id":83882306,"login":"farxC","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODgyMzA2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/farxC/open-training/commits/01e8512134af7aa2cd188732f7e72043a27c1869/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-05T01:16:53Z","email":"rafaelflamengo07@outlook.com","name":"farxC"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-05T01:17:01Z","email":"rafaelflamengo07@outlook.com","name":"farxC"},"message":"feat(exercises): rebuild the exercise page around its sets\n\nThe screen opened with metadata and a chart and dumped every set at the\nbottom as undated rows, which is backwards: the sets are the only thing on\nthe page that was actually done. Everything else exists to explain them.\n\nThe sets now come first, as a ledger. One line per session, written the way\nit gets written by hand (80x12  85x10  100x6), with the month in a recessed\nstrip above its first session and the top set in full ink. RPE, failure and\nper-set intensity against the all-time best live one tap deeper, in a drawer\nthat opens recessed under its line — that''s the kind of thing you look up\nabout one session rather than scan across ten. It opens on the last two\nmonths *trained* (an untrained month doesn''t spend a slot, so a layoff can''t\nleave the plate blank), reaching back two months at a time or all at once.\n\nThe progression chart gets a cursor. Bars that can''t be identified are a\ntexture, not a chart: one column is always selected — the most recent by\ndefault — and the readout above names it in full, with the scale''s ceiling\nmarked so a tall bar means a number rather than \"the tallest one here\".\n\nThe config becomes a spec plate: a 2xN grid where anything left at its\ndefault recedes, so what stays in ink is what distinguishes this movement.\nThe resistance curve is drawn as a thumbnail of plain Views instead of a\n160px Skia chart pretending to be a value.\n\nThe editor behind it (shared with the live session''s snapshot editor) groups\nits nine chip rows into the questions they answer — execution, load, grip,\nbench — each with a line saying what the dimension means, over a live\nsummary in the same words the spec plate will use. Its save action is pinned\nrather than buried under the last chip group, and the sheet it lives in now\nscrolls: in a plain View its last sections were simply cut off.\n\nThe edit affordance moves into the header as a proper button; it used to be\nbare text floating beside the metadata line. Equipment and type finally get\npt-BR labels instead of rendering their raw column values.\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1809181b0400980bac4e0ba9169818c5541bb524","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/farxC/open-training/git/trees/1809181b0400980bac4e0ba9169818c5541bb524"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/farxC/open-training/git/commits/01e8512134af7aa2cd188732f7e72043a27c1869","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83882306?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/farxC","id":83882306,"login":"farxC","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODgyMzA2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/farxC/open-training/commit/01e8512134af7aa2cd188732f7e72043a27c1869","node_id":"C_kwDOTP0lv9oAKDAxZTg1MTIxMzRhZjdhYTJjZDE4ODczMmY3ZTcyMDQzYTI3YzE4Njk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/farxC/open-training/commit/29a6e090fa50715260e6cfa6eda419b342c79374","sha":"29a6e090fa50715260e6cfa6eda419b342c79374","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/farxC/open-training/commits/29a6e090fa50715260e6cfa6eda419b342c79374"}],"sha":"01e8512134af7aa2cd188732f7e72043a27c1869","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/farxC/open-training/commits/01e8512134af7aa2cd188732f7e72043a27c1869"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83882306?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/farxC","id":83882306,"login":"farxC","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODgyMzA2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/farxC/open-training/commits/29a6e090fa50715260e6cfa6eda419b342c79374/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-05T00:42:34Z","email":"rafaelflamengo07@outlook.com","name":"farxC"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-05T00:42:34Z","email":"rafaelflamengo07@outlook.com","name":"farxC"},"message":"Merge branch ''feat/muscle-group-exercise-drilldown''\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"39497201030dc2ea272ddaa7cd426a5b40a29ed9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/farxC/open-training/git/trees/39497201030dc2ea272ddaa7cd426a5b40a29ed9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/farxC/open-training/git/commits/29a6e090fa50715260e6cfa6eda419b342c79374","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83882306?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/farxC","id":83882306,"login":"farxC","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODgyMzA2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/farxC/open-training/commit/29a6e090fa50715260e6cfa6eda419b342c79374","node_id":"C_kwDOTP0lv9oAKDI5YTZlMDkwZmE1MDcxNTI2MGU2Y2ZhNmVkYTQxOWIzNDJjNzkzNzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/farxC/open-training/commit/f694d1165b3f8bcf81ea9effe84967effcdfc355","sha":"f694d1165b3f8bcf81ea9effe84967effcdfc355","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/farxC/open-training/commits/f694d1165b3f8bcf81ea9effe84967effcdfc355"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/farxC/open-training/commit/e85e68efc53a8564d3d3cb241da184475b6ece10","sha":"e85e68efc53a8564d3d3cb241da184475b6ece10","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/farxC/open-training/commits/e85e68efc53a8564d3d3cb241da184475b6ece10"}],"sha":"29a6e090fa50715260e6cfa6eda419b342c79374","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/farxC/open-training/commits/29a6e090fa50715260e6cfa6eda419b342c79374"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83882306?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/farxC","id":83882306,"login":"farxC","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODgyMzA2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/farxC/open-training/commits/e85e68efc53a8564d3d3cb241da184475b6ece10/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-05T00:42:07Z","email":"rafaelflamengo07@outlook.com","name":"farxC"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-05T00:42:07Z","email":"rafaelflamengo07@outlook.com","name":"farxC"},"message":"feat(analytics): open a muscle group to see which exercises built its load\n\nThe panel said how much each group got and how often, but never where the\nload came from — 18 séries/week of chest concentrated in one press is a\ndifferent training week from 18 spread over three movements, and finding\nthat out meant opening sessions one by one in the feed.\n\nTapping a group row now pulls out a drawer listing its exercises, ranked by\nweighted series, each with its share of the group and the sessions it\nappeared in. One group open at a time: the panel runs to ten rows and the\nranking is only readable while it stays short.\n\ngetMuscleExerciseSeriesInRange is the same snapshot rollup the group rows\nuse, grouped by exercise as well. One query over the whole window, divided\nby the same week count — analysisWeeks() tiles the range exactly, so the\nchildren sum to the parent in every window, which is the guarantee the whole\nscreen rests on. It also selects an unweighted set count, the only thing\nthat separates six sets at ½× from three at 1×, which is what the ½× badge\nreads.\n\nTwo things only showed up running it against real data on a device:\n\n- Frequency per exercise is a count, not a per-week average. A movement\n  trained eight times across a 26-week window averages 0.3×/week, which\n  reads as nothing, with the pips showing a single empty ring. \"em 8\n  sessões\" is legible in every window, and nothing here needs to sum to the\n  parent the way series does.\n\n- The tail is folded at six. One group had 21 exercises in a half-year\n  window — three screens of scrolling whose second half repeated \"0.5, 5%\".\n  splitExerciseRows keeps the six largest and carries the rest''s series into\n  a summary line, so a folded drawer never appears to contradict the number\n  on the row that opened it. Tapping that line unfolds the full list.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"39497201030dc2ea272ddaa7cd426a5b40a29ed9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/farxC/open-training/git/trees/39497201030dc2ea272ddaa7cd426a5b40a29ed9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/farxC/open-training/git/commits/e85e68efc53a8564d3d3cb241da184475b6ece10","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83882306?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/farxC","id":83882306,"login":"farxC","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODgyMzA2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/farxC/open-training/commit/e85e68efc53a8564d3d3cb241da184475b6ece10","node_id":"C_kwDOTP0lv9oAKGU4NWU2OGVmYzUzYTg1NjRkM2QzY2IyNDFkYTE4NDQ3NWI2ZWNlMTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/farxC/open-training/commit/f694d1165b3f8bcf81ea9effe84967effcdfc355","sha":"f694d1165b3f8bcf81ea9effe84967effcdfc355","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/farxC/open-training/commits/f694d1165b3f8bcf81ea9effe84967effcdfc355"}],"sha":"e85e68efc53a8564d3d3cb241da184475b6ece10","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/farxC/open-training/commits/e85e68efc53a8564d3d3cb241da184475b6ece10"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83882306?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/farxC","id":83882306,"login":"farxC","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODgyMzA2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/farxC","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/farxC/open-training/commits/f694d1165b3f8bcf81ea9effe84967effcdfc355/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-05T00:08:18Z","email":"rafaelflamengo07@outlook.com","name":"farxC"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-05T00:08:18Z","email":"rafaelflamengo07@outlook.com","name":"farxC"},"message":"fix(analytics): stop NativeWind from eating the chips'' styles on Android\n\nOn a phone the MODALIDADE selector rendered as loose icons and labels: no\npill, no fill, no border, all four endurance options crammed into one row —\nand the FORÇA group looked empty, because its chip is the active one and an\nactive chip paints its icon and label white, which on the white card is\ninvisible.\n\nThe cause is `style={({ pressed, hovered }) => …}`. NativeWind''s JSX\ntransform swaps every Pressable for the react-native-css-interop wrapper, and\non native that wrapper treats the inline `style` prop as a style rule: it\nspreads the value — `{ ...fn }` is `{}` — and writes the result back over the\nprop. So a function style is silently discarded on device while working fine\nin the browser, whose interop path never touches `style`. Verified against\nthe interop''s own primitives: a function comes out `{}`, an object comes out\nintact.\n\nInteraction state now lives in useInteractionState and the style props are\nplain objects. Same hex values, paddings, flex sizing and active shadow as\nbefore — no visual change intended. The ORDENAR chips in the muscle load\npanel and the desktop PeriodChips had the same defect and got the same\ntreatment.\n\nA source scan guards the pattern instead of a render test: wrap-jsx skips\nregistering the interop components when NODE_ENV is \"test\", so the bug cannot\nreproduce under jest.\n\nVerified on a Galaxy S23 (Android 15): FORÇA fills with ink and reads white\non it, ENDURANCE lays out 2x2 with cream keys, and tapping moves the fill.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"cac399ae2a049701a461db7cdbd92da05851a3a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/farxC/open-training/git/trees/cac399ae2a049701a461db7cdbd92da05851a3a5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repo