accf99904"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3331339?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevesioli/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevesioli/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevesioli/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevesioli/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/stevesioli","id":3331339,"login":"stevesioli","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMzEzMzk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevesioli/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevesioli/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevesioli/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevesioli/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevesioli/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevesioli","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stevesioli/portfolio/commits/4cdc095ead92f4550ba9f237412dd9b7ea0a6df7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-22T13:29:31Z","email":"steve.m@sioli.com","name":"Steve Sioli"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-22T13:29:31Z","email":"steve.m@sioli.com","name":"Steve Sioli"},"message":"fix(shell): apply sticky overflow gate synchronously to fix intermittent scroll skip\n\nuseIsStuck toggled a section''s overflow-y-auto via React state feeding\na className ternary. On a fast scroll gesture, several native scroll\nevents can fire in the window between a state update and React\nactually committing the new className — each one gets scroll-chained\nby the browser based on whatever overflow value is *currently\npainted*, so a stale overflow-hidden during that gap let wheel input\nleak straight through to the page instead of being captured by the\nsection. This is what caused Experience to sometimes get skipped\nbefore Skills scrolled into view — a fast/committed scroll gesture\ncould outrun the re-render.\n\nuseIsStuck now mutates element.style.overflowY directly inside the\nscroll handler instead of returning state for a className toggle,\nclosing that gap. Section and the shell''s inline hero section updated\nto match — className now has a static overflow-hidden default (the\nhook flips it before first paint via useLayoutEffect regardless).\n\nAlso added @mf-types/.mf to the shared eslint config''s ignores,\nmatching their existing .gitignore entry — Module Federation''s\ngenerated type stubs were tripping no-explicit-any and\nconsistent-type-imports on every local `pnpm lint` run. Harmless in CI\n(they''re never committed) but noisy locally; noticed while verifying\nthis fix.\n\nVerified: tsc -b and eslint --max-warnings 0 both pass clean across\nshell, mfe-hero, mfe-experience, and packages/ui in this environment.","tree":{"sha":"d368b113f0a9f2d7a0b382a0b8c6071a3ea77b84","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stevesioli/portfolio/git/trees/d368b113f0a9f2d7a0b382a0b8c6071a3ea77b84"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stevesioli/portfolio/git/commits/4cdc095ead92f4550ba9f237412dd9b7ea0a6df7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3331339?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevesioli/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevesioli/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevesioli/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevesioli/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/stevesioli","id":3331339,"login":"stevesioli","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMzEzMzk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevesioli/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevesioli/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevesioli/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevesioli/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevesioli/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevesioli","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/stevesioli/portfolio/commit/4cdc095ead92f4550ba9f237412dd9b7ea0a6df7","node_id":"C_kwDOTQCvC9oAKDRjZGMwOTVlYWQ5MmY0NTUwYmE5ZjIzNzQxMmRkOWI3ZWEwYTZkZjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/stevesioli/portfolio/commit/76884e1995c56ea98f079a95771080f6105de668","sha":"76884e1995c56ea98f079a95771080f6105de668","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stevesioli/portfolio/commits/76884e1995c56ea98f079a95771080f6105de668"}],"sha":"4cdc095ead92f4550ba9f237412dd9b7ea0a6df7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stevesioli/portfolio/commits/4cdc095ead92f4550ba9f237412dd9b7ea0a6df7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3331339?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevesioli/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevesioli/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevesioli/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevesioli/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/stevesioli","id":3331339,"login":"stevesioli","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMzEzMzk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevesioli/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevesioli/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevesioli/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevesioli/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevesioli/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevesioli","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stevesioli/portfolio/commits/76884e1995c56ea98f079a95771080f6105de668/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-12T20:53:17Z","email":"steve.m@sioli.com","name":"Steve Sioli"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-12T20:54:27Z","email":"steve.m@sioli.com","name":"Steve Sioli"},"message":"refactor(mfe-hero): finalize hybrid hero layout, remove comparison variants\n\nDecision made: the hybrid layout (chips'' text-only left column + a\npull-quote right column with the avatar floated into it) is the final\nhero design. Folds HeroHybrid''s JSX directly into HeroSection.tsx —\nthe comparison-harness variant switch and its VARIANT constant are\ngone, since there''s nothing left to switch between.\n\nRemoved the three unused variant files (HeroPhotoChips, HeroPhotoPanel,\nHeroInline). Also dropped mfe-hero''s now-unused direct \"motion\"\ndependency (and its pnpm-lock.yaml entry) — only HeroPhotoChips used\n`motion/react` directly; @resume/ui''s Reveal/StaggerGroup still pull\nmotion in as their own dependency, so nothing else in this app needs\nit. Updated content.ts''s PULL_QUOTE doc comment, which referenced the\nnow-deleted \"inline\" variant by name.\n\nVerified: `tsc -b` and `eslint . --max-warnings 0` both pass clean for\nmfe-hero against this environment''s node_modules.","tree":{"sha":"1993ef284a5b4497b56c907a0cf1d6762d0ec3b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stevesioli/portfolio/git/trees/1993ef284a5b4497b56c907a0cf1d6762d0ec3b7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stevesioli/portfolio/git/commits/76884e1995c56ea98f079a95771080f6105de668","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3331339?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevesioli/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevesioli/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevesioli/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevesioli/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/stevesioli","id":3331339,"login":"