com","name":"Utkrisht Verma"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T01:04:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Merge pull request #24 from utility-crm/fix/reader-entitlement-and-session\n\nfix: premium pages stay locked for paying readers","tree":{"sha":"86b16b9adfdaac354460eb3406934ed749aecafd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/git/trees/86b16b9adfdaac354460eb3406934ed749aecafd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/git/commits/cf0421a522c8ff757ef11436f2bc69a8021e041b","verification":{"payload":"tree 86b16b9adfdaac354460eb3406934ed749aecafd\nparent f166d2cfa781f44190beeb7c6b0e49b2ed0b15d5\nparent b9a5c50b4019339c2d3b8ce706f8d55b37858ad8\nauthor Utkrisht Verma <utk.rs.verma@gmail.com> 1787101497 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787101497 +0530\n\nMerge pull request #24 from utility-crm/fix/reader-entitlement-and-session\n\nfix: premium pages stay locked for paying readers","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhQE5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAANM8QAFsaZmOG/GRklZ9HTvmwPoNj\nuaw/2qhE0eaNyl7NxUtJhyAGb6QahzjaPNJQFrelS4oJPHHd9axwHRp9Edc5OCPT\neJNiaEfBxX61HXeLKn42DUuK6WbVo5d8+4OdxaHuNcjPvACUIw+QuIH3SzXw5D4W\newqNCpFWWCEaj2Ru5JUB1nZA0YbTzs0nq8znTdEZyCMMVpKR/UY0vIYSmfAJ0bIn\nKvTbidSSfMx2oe1nhfZRUCjLrwYrcKgwZg1iP20PMmxuZD3Nf7o9eg2uNJleYK+c\n3RS2einbaaTIf0wtwsStsxLgoIBDvHJ2gN37Y6aFc7wD8rKNtIol5vLv/OQoMfol\nMX0QQK6Z7eoahbok9bcLcHTnnEUx5cKq8ofEIR7znQ2kJCgDZDMSHM37BxlfKe+K\niy7j021+Pu5vQ89SYH0DD/8GGkEZs3hTAuw/BPzTf5+q5rmHO3WLzh5BKCUJ8VDd\nNu2Bwh75FXTg4oinE1B7k5akrQyF/c2TpTex3eqsY4cWzSiyZX84Yre4QATvdjcW\nd8XW8OyPkMsTjAuJrEoBtqj5bNT2eyuH6JwoxA4s3mR6Z9ptjOEuWJta2QD8Cu8J\nco3WN8vvgouaS6MKU06Pbw4CpO6EldJA+SZODVHqtCHz6rOvBnWwRo+82vcxDDfW\n9grl20R/wTlrdEKQ1/K0\n=KnH9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-19T01:04:58Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commit/cf0421a522c8ff757ef11436f2bc69a8021e041b","node_id":"C_kwDOTQKyJdoAKGNmMDQyMWE1MjJjOGZmNzU3ZWYxMTQzNmYyYmM2OWE4MDIxZTA0MWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commit/f166d2cfa781f44190beeb7c6b0e49b2ed0b15d5","sha":"f166d2cfa781f44190beeb7c6b0e49b2ed0b15d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commits/f166d2cfa781f44190beeb7c6b0e49b2ed0b15d5"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commit/b9a5c50b4019339c2d3b8ce706f8d55b37858ad8","sha":"b9a5c50b4019339c2d3b8ce706f8d55b37858ad8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commits/b9a5c50b4019339c2d3b8ce706f8d55b37858ad8"}],"sha":"cf0421a522c8ff757ef11436f2bc69a8021e041b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commits/cf0421a522c8ff757ef11436f2bc69a8021e041b"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commits/b9a5c50b4019339c2d3b8ce706f8d55b37858ad8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T01:04:17Z","email":"usk.rs.verma@gmail.com","name":"vincenzo-verma"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T01:04:17Z","email":"usk.rs.verma@gmail.com","name":"vincenzo-verma"},"message":"fix(billing): key webhook idempotency on the Razorpay event header\n\nTwo faults on the reader webhook, both about applying one event exactly once.\n\nrazorpay_event_id was `event.id || event.account_id || crypto.randomUUID()`.\nRazorpay''s webhook body has no top-level `id`, so that resolved to account_id —\none value for every event a merchant ever sends. With razorpay_event_id UNIQUE\nand INSERT OR IGNORE, the first event logged for a tenant claimed that id and\nevery later event was silently discarded, leaving the billing event log with a\nsingle row per tenant. billing-platform already hit this and documents it; the\nreal key is the x-razorpay-event-id header.\n\nIt is now required rather than defaulted. A random fallback would defeat the\nguard below, and an event we cannot deduplicate is one we cannot safely apply,\nso a body without the header is refused with a 400 and logged.\n\nThe subscription update also ran before the event was logged, so every\nredelivery of one subscription.charged reset current_end to now + interval,\nquietly extending access — Razorpay retries deliveries, and they can be replayed\nby hand.\n\nThe mutation and the event log now go in one db.batch(), which D1 runs as a\nsingle sequential transaction. The mutation is guarded on the event id not being\nlogged yet and runs first, so inside the transaction it still sees the pre-insert\nstate: first delivery mutates and logs, a redelivery no-ops on both and still\nanswers 2xx. Ordering it this way rather than logging first is deliberate — a\ncrash mid-batch rolls back both and the retry re-applies, where log-then-mutate\nwould record the event and lose the state change permanently.","tree":{"sha":"86b16b9adfdaac354460eb3406934ed749aecafd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/git/trees/86b16b9adfdaac354460eb3406934ed749aecafd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/git/commits/b9a5c50b4019339c2d3b8ce706f8d55b37858ad8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commit/b9a5c50b4019339c2d3b8ce706f8d55b37858ad8","node_id":"C_kwDOTQKyJdoAKGI5YTVjNTBiNDAxOTMzOWMyZDNiOGNlNzA2ZjhkNTViMzc4NThhZDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commit/944afb8adecd10ed975db26417baec0c6cccc18c","sha":"944afb8adecd10ed975db26417baec0c6cccc18c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commits/944afb8adecd10ed975db26417baec0c6cccc18c"}],"sha":"b9a5c50b4019339c2d3b8ce706f8d55b37858ad8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commits/b9a5c50b4019339c2d3b8ce706f8d55b37858ad8"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commits/944afb8adecd10ed975db26417baec0c6cccc18c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T17:19:57Z","email":"usk.rs.verma@gmail.com","name":"vincenzo-verma"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T17:19:57Z","email":"usk.rs.verma@gmail.com","name":"vincenzo-verma"},"message":"fix(auth): stop a phone login clearing a reader''s verified-email flag\n\nThe existing-reader UPDATE in verify-firebase COALESCEd email and phone_number\n(backfill only, never overwrite) but rebound email_verified from the incoming\ntoken every time. A phone/OTP token carries no email claim, so that value is\nalways 0: a reader who had verified their email and later signed in with OTP\nsilently lost the flag, and with it a gate they had already passed.\n\nemail_verified is now write-once-up. It is raised only when the token proves this\nrow''s address — linkEmail is non-null only for a Firebase-verified email, and the\nCASE reads the pre-UPDATE email, so a NULL one means we are backfilling linkEmail\nitself. A verified token for a different address leaves the flag alone rather than\nmarking the stored address verified. Nothing clears it.","tree":{"sha":"ee0f5e766d6a71fafa6f0d24034646376d0cde16","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/git/trees/ee0f5e766d6a71fafa6f0d24034646376d0cde16"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/git/commits/944afb8adecd10ed975db26417baec0c6cccc18c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commit/944afb8adecd10ed975db26417baec0c6cccc18c","node_id":"C_kwDOTQKyJdoAKDk0NGFmYjhhZGVjZDEwZWQ5NzVkYjI2NDE3YmFlYzBjNmNjY2MxOGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commit/670bbc8a7d616f004aa8d2735689f56ea8dfd29d","sha":"670bbc8a7d616f004aa8d2735689f56ea8dfd29d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commits/670bbc8a7d616f004aa8d2735689f56ea8dfd29d"}],"sha":"944afb8adecd10ed975db26417baec0c6cccc18c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commits/944afb8adecd10ed975db26417baec0c6cccc18c"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commits/670bbc8a7d616f004aa8d2735689f56ea8dfd29d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T17:19:34Z","email":"usk.rs.verma@gmail.com","name":"vincenzo-verma"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T17:19:34Z","email":"usk.rs.verma@gmail.com","name":"vincenzo-verma"},"message":"fix(billing): let the webhook create the entitlement the browser never wrote\n\nreader_subscriptions rows are the only thing that unlocks premium pages, and\nPOST /reader/verify was the only code that ever wrote one. It runs from Razorpay\nCheckout''s browser `handler` callback, which is not guaranteed to run: a closed\ntab, a dropped connection or a crash after the debit left the reader charged with\nnothing unlocked and no way back.\n\nThe webhook could not fix that. It looked the subscription up by razorpay_sub_id\nand nested every branch inside `if (row)`, so an unmatched event did nothing and\nstill answered 2xx; subscription.activated was not handled at all. The data was\nalready in the payload and being discarded — createSubscription sends\nnotes: { plan_id, tier_id, reader_id } and Razorpay echoes them back.\n\nThe webhook now creates the row from those notes on subscription.charged and\nsubscription.activated. notes only decide which reader and which plan: tier_id\nand the interval come from the local plans row, because tier_id is what actually\nunlocks content and a webhook body is external input that must not name its own\ntier. reader_id has no FK, so the reader is confirmed to exist before insert.\nSame INSERT ... ON CONFLICT(razorpay_sub_id) as /reader/verify, so a webhook and\na browser callback racing on one subscription converge. Recovery failures are\nswallowed and fall through to the existing unmatched 2xx — a broken recovery must\nnot turn a delivered webhook into a retry storm. Recovered rows now also get\ntheir event logged, which the NOT NULL FK previously skipped.\n\nsubscription.authenticated stays unhandled on purpose: the mandate exists but no\nmoney has moved, and an active entitlement for an unpaid mandate is free access.\n\nThe term math moves to reader-sub-row.ts alongside the notes->row mapping so both\nwriters agree on \"one paid term\" and the mapping is checkable under plain node\n(reader-sub-row.selfcheck.mjs; the repo has no test runner and index.ts is not\nimportable outside a bundler). It asserts that a notes-supplied tier_id is\nignored in favour of the local plan, that non-paying events mint nothing, and the\nper-interval term math.\n\nMigration 0014 finally declares reader_subscriptions.last_payment_id, which\nuntil now existed only because ensureBillingColumns ALTERs it in at runtime and\nswallows the duplicate-column error — a freshly provisioned tenant had the column\nonly if some billing request happened to run that patch first. SQLite has no\nADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS, so scripts/baseline/tenant.sql carries the matching\nschema-verified ledger entry; without it the plain ALTER would abort\nmigrate-all-tenants.sh on the first already-patched tenant, which is every live\ntenant.","tree":{"sha":"a7d5145d692fe7946476542cf7062e22519a3d85","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/git/trees/a7d5145d692fe7946476542cf7062e22519a3d85"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/git/commits/670bbc8a7d616f004aa8d2735689f56ea8dfd29d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commit/670bbc8a7d616f004aa8d2735689f56ea8dfd29d","node_id":"C_kwDOTQKyJdoAKDY3MGJiYzhhN2Q2MTZmMDA0YWE4ZDI3MzU2ODlmNTZlYThkZmQyOWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commit/e912920cd6b7fafd956647feb3e1a8c6fa5987af","sha":"e912920cd6b7fafd956647feb3e1a8c6fa5987af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commits/e912920cd6b7fafd956647feb3e1a8c6fa5987af"}],"sha":"670bbc8a7d616f004aa8d2735689f56ea8dfd29d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commits/670bbc8a7d616f004aa8d2735689f56ea8dfd29d"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commits/e912920cd6b7fafd956647feb3e1a8c6fa5987af/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T17:19:03Z","email":"usk.rs.verma@gmail.com","name":"vincenzo-verma"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T17:19:03Z","email":"usk.rs.verma@gmail.com","name":"vincenzo-verma"},"message":"fix(reader): recover a rejected session instead of selling a second subscription\n\nA reader with an active subscription was shown the paywall, with a \"Sign in to\ncontinue\" button and plan buttons, because their browser held no usable reader\nsession — so no Authorization header reached the server and every premium page\ncame back locked. The client never looked at the `signed_in` / `unlocked` fields\nthe server already returns, so a lost session was indistinguishable from \"not\nsubscribed\" and the reader was invited to buy what they were already paying for.\n\n- PaperViewer: when the paper payload reports signed_in === false while we still\n  hold a session, that token was rejected (expired, or minted under a rotated\n  secret). Drop it, re-prompt, and switch the locked-page copy to \"Your session\n  expired / Sign in again\" with the plan buttons hidden. Checked inside loadPaper\n  so the verdict is always paired with the token that produced it; the anonymous\n  refetch after sign-out (signed_in false, no session) matches neither branch, so\n  it neither loops nor clears the notice.\n- ReaderApp: owns the recovery (signOut + open the login dialog) and passes it as\n  a useCallback, since PaperViewer holds it in a fetch dependency list.\n- useReaderSession: parse localStorage defensively. It runs during render, so a\n  corrupt entry — or a bare JWT written by an older client — threw and took the\n  whole reader app down. Anything that is not the shape signIn writes is dropped.\n- FirebaseAuthActionPage stored the raw JWT under the session key, which is the\n  bare-JWT case above: every later load of the reader app crashed for anyone who\n  used the email-link lane. Store { token, reader }, as signIn does.\n- Razorpay checkout: the handler callback is the only thing that records the\n  subscription, so a dismissed modal or a failed payment left a possibly-charged\n  reader with no access and no message. Report both. Prefill only a non-empty\n  email — phone-only readers have none, and an empty string just renders a blank\n  invalid field.","tree":{"sha":"8d43c21598aafb3afe76044643f7d9f812bdaf08","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/git/trees/8d43c21598aafb3afe76044643f7d9f812bdaf08"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/git/commits/e912920cd6b7fafd956647feb3e1a8c6fa5987af","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commit/e912920cd6b7fafd956647feb3e1a8c6fa5987af","node_id":"C_kwDOTQKyJdoAKGU5MTI5MjBjZDZiN2ZhZmQ5NTY2NDdmZWIzZTFhOGM2ZmE1OTg3YWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commit/db94a52d1ae3bd2e09cc46d78395f4a1524188e9","sha":"db94a52d1ae3bd2e09cc46d78395f4a1524188e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commits/db94a52d1ae3bd2e09cc46d78395f4a1524188e9"}],"sha":"e912920cd6b7fafd956647feb3e1a8c6fa5987af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commits/e912920cd6b7fafd956647feb3e1a8c6fa5987af"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commits/db94a52d1ae3bd2e09cc46d78395f4a1524188e9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T17:18:29Z","email":"usk.rs.verma@gmail.com","name":"vincenzo-verma"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T17:18:29Z","email":"usk.rs.verma@gmail.com","name":"vincenzo-verma"},"message":"fix(content): unlock manual grants, and ship plan tax to the paywall\n\nhasActiveSub compared the edition''s tier_id against reader_subscriptions.tier_id,\nwhich manual staff grants write as NULL (admin-grants.ts) because staff grant\n\"access\", not one tier. `NULL = ''tier-uuid''` is NULL, never true, so an active\nmanual grant unlocked nothing at all — confirmed in production, where a reader\nwith an active manual grant still saw every premium page locked.\n\nA NULL tier on a manual grant now satisfies any tier. Scoped to\ngrant_type = ''manual'' deliberately: a bare `tier_id IS NULL` would also hand\nevery tier to a razorpay row whose tier failed to record.\n\nAlso add p.tax_percentage to GET /:slug/plans. The paywall quotes a\ntax-inclusive price from that field and billing charges tax-inclusive, so\nomitting it left the field undefined client-side — treated as 0, quoting the\nreader less than the mandate actually debits.","tree":{"sha":"2e29d9b4ebb52400be6f88aa60338d377bd07d7e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/git/trees/2e29d9b4ebb52400be6f88aa60338d377bd07d7e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/git/commits/db94a52d1ae3bd2e09cc46d78395f4a1524188e9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commit/db94a52d1ae3bd2e09cc46d78395f4a1524188e9","node_id":"C_kwDOTQKyJdoAKGRiOTRhNTJkMWFlM2JkMmUwOWNjNDZkNzgzOTVmNGExNTI0MTg4ZTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commit/f166d2cfa781f44190beeb7c6b0e49b2ed0b15d5","sha":"f166d2cfa781f44190beeb7c6b0e49b2ed0b15d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commits/f166d2cfa781f44190beeb7c6b0e49b2ed0b15d5"}],"sha":"db94a52d1ae3bd2e09cc46d78395f4a1524188e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commits/db94a52d1ae3bd2e09cc46d78395f4a1524188e9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/107689613?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vincenzo-Verma/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vincenzo-Verma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vincenzo-Verma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vincenzo-Verma/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Vincenzo-Verma","id":107689613,"login":"Vincenzo-Verma","node_id":"U_kgDOBms2jQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vincenzo-Verma/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vincenzo-Verma/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vincenzo-Verma/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vincenzo-Verma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vincenzo-Verma/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vincenzo-Verma","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commits/f166d2cfa781f44190beeb7c6b0e49b2ed0b15d5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-02T11:00:21Z","email":"utk.rs.verma@gmail.com","name":"Utkrisht Verma"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-02T11:00:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Merge pull request #23 from utility-crm/feat/manual-email-verify\n\nfeat(crm): let superadmins manually verify a publisher email","tree":{"sha":"042f10d4220c84012ef0b8801d3a687d15d617ec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/git/trees/042f10d4220c84012ef0b8801d3a687d15d617ec"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/git/commits/f166d2cfa781f44190beeb7c6b0e49b2ed0b15d5","verification":{"payload":"tree 042f10d4220c84012ef0b8801d3a687d15d617ec\nparent 3b439b593bfb7c7bdbda4b6538ea5690a05c6d16\nparent d56bc11e1ad9aeda58f7b353b8923ce2767327e5\nauthor Utkrisht Verma <utk.rs.verma@gmail.com> 1785668421 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785668421 +0530\n\nMerge pull request #23 from utility-crm/feat/manual-email-verify\n\nfeat(crm): let superadmins manually verify a publisher email","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqbyNFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZBAQAAit1fEUT/ACAzeVnev4SUHt\nDHJemLmXqQqB7yy62qZmmFS9dl0CNoGwL2TA++FQwfosKLruVPwC8RBLnzDD632P\nZkLwVhOU9Ee2I+dyDEfAtW8wtlk4A0XqpClDFFopBqkgo0BZF7f92NCLBCVAswEU\nza/YLpzoNz9g8zwNf6C7Ate2Iin7XT0yxsfjkqRJhS6fS9XSuiYgVXfoTmo7g8l6\nyaVJYVQNfe2RoafkLVpnXfE/hapxhPpcsMfKn6/8ahFdWcniEDl1FJVOByQBrQ+H\nsZ3W0m57SyQfG2jq7Zxcl6IS2byDvQW4vbH32yB6QmA1MfTAdhRGKpTGqSpCQP5J\n7gnvOwKYwurcL7W1m+Y7RoLTOIpo3azoMzfGUahuOOXa0UGZaNVK3J2NZUepaOCx\nh2j2KzR9s1wvqcoQLyH6qFmsrvMWRGaayMX91Xoe7WKm/0yTTZcw6PpXDJSarHPy\nHZPDWSOkVASBQV+bYKNmKqD+qup+y5x/dveiyYueOGToF8YP/6hRMiYrjp17CQ2J\nqhGa/INIUBljYhOAjo8xfwKDHINIFtcEaPKpQA0rJBMqUKGPdwNTkriSutdJpnvZ\nBTWtjX8vLMaixkdD6KNyiA6HKuVWze294hPRxe+EeSp7DB+Gx1Ko6FAXMym+s+6y\nfS/nlVAgulC4Kv/URT7w\n=FSyO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-02T11:00:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commit/f166d2cfa781f44190beeb7c6b0e49b2ed0b15d5","node_id":"C_kwDOTQKyJdoAKGYxNjZkMmNmYTc4MWY0NDE5MGJlZWI3YzZiMGU0OWIyZWQwYjE1ZDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commit/3b439b593bfb7c7bdbda4b6538ea5690a05c6d16","sha":"3b439b593bfb7c7bdbda4b6538ea5690a05c6d16","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commits/3b439b593bfb7c7bdbda4b6538ea5690a05c6d16"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commit/d56bc11e1ad9aeda58f7b353b8923ce2767327e5","sha":"d56bc11e1ad9aeda58f7b353b8923ce2767327e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commits/d56bc11e1ad9aeda58f7b353b8923ce2767327e5"}],"sha":"f166d2cfa781f44190beeb7c6b0e49b2ed0b15d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commits/f166d2cfa781f44190beeb7c6b0e49b2ed0b15d5"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commits/d56bc11e1ad9aeda58f7b353b8923ce2767327e5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-02T10:56:27Z","email":"usk.rs.verma@gmail.com","name":"vincenzo-verma"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-02T10:56:27Z","email":"usk.rs.verma@gmail.com","name":"vincenzo-verma"},"message":"fix: gate content /internal/* routes and make provisioning trigger atomic\n\nTwo review findings on the manual email-verify PR.\n\n1. Concurrent POSTs to /api/tenants/:slug/verify-email could both read the\n   tenant as ''pending'' and both dispatch PROVISION_WORKER, running the\n   workflow twice for one slug. Claim the tenant with a conditional\n   UPDATE ... WHERE id = ? AND status = ''pending'' and only dispatch when\n   that update changed a row, so the write serializes the trigger. This\n   also moves the tenant off ''pending'' on the success path, which the\n   handler previously never did (unlike /internal/:slug/reprovision), so\n   the portal no longer shows a stale status. The failure rollback now\n   matches on status = ''provisioning'' since the claim moves it first.\n\n2. The content worker''s /internal/* routes were unauthenticated. Its\n   wrangler.jsonc sets no `routes` and does not disable workers_dev, so\n   the routes answer on the public workers.dev hostname even though they\n   escape the gateway''s /api/* forwarding. Ungated, set-email-verified let\n   any caller clear the content write gate for any address, and the\n   pre-existing migrate-owner route let any caller upsert a password_hash\n   into org_users. Add a shared-secret guard (X-Internal-Secret, compared\n   without early exit) on all three routes; it fails closed with 503 when\n   INTERNAL_SECRET is unset rather than serving unauthenticated.\n\n   The admin worker sends the header from its own INTERNAL_SECRET. The\n   migrate-owner call site is wrapped so a missing secret follows the\n   existing non-fatal path instead of 500-ing tenant activation.","tree":{"sha":"042f10d4220c84012ef0b8801d3a687d15d617ec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/git/trees/042f10d4220c84012ef0b8801d3a687d15d617ec"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/git/commits/d56bc11e1ad9aeda58f7b353b8923ce2767327e5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commit/d56bc11e1ad9aeda58f7b353b8923ce2767327e5","node_id":"C_kwDOTQKyJdoAKGQ1NmJjMTFlMWFkOWFlZGE1OGY3YjM1M2I4OTIzY2UyNzY3MzI3ZTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commit/272401ed7b7c25e3d5d2d077b06a978bede5a215","sha":"272401ed7b7c25e3d5d2d077b06a978bede5a215","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commits/272401ed7b7c25e3d5d2d077b06a978bede5a215"}],"sha":"d56bc11e1ad9aeda58f7b353b8923ce2767327e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commits/d56bc11e1ad9aeda58f7b353b8923ce2767327e5"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commits/272401ed7b7c25e3d5d2d077b06a978bede5a215/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-02T10:01:56Z","email":"usk.rs.verma@gmail.com","name":"vincenzo-verma"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-02T10:14:02Z","email":"usk.rs.verma@gmail.com","name":"vincenzo-verma"},"message":"feat(crm): let superadmins manually verify a publisher email\n\nThe content worker refuses writes from a publisher whose address is\nunverified (requireVerifiedEmail), and the verification mail is normally\nthe only way to clear that gate. When delivery is broken — bounced\ndomain, Resend outage, an address only reachable out of band — the\npublisher cannot publish and has nothing to retry, since resending just\nmails the same dead address again.\n\nAdds a superadmin-only endpoint that flips email_verified directly,\nsending no mail, plus a banner on the tenant detail page that surfaces\nthe unverified state and a confirm modal before the write.\n\nThe flag lives in one of two stores and tenant status is not a reliable\npointer to which: activation does not always migrate the owner row out of\npending_owners, so active tenants are seen with the row still there.\nBoth stores are therefore written and success is \"at least one row\nchanged\", mirroring the existing writeOwner in verify-email.ts. The\norg_users write goes through a new content-worker internal endpoint\nbecause the admin worker holds CONTROL_DB and service bindings but no\nper-tenant D1.\n\nReads match on LOWER(email) on both sides, consistent with\nverify-email.ts: rows predating the lowercase-on-write rule are stored\nmixed-case and an exact match misses them.","tree":{"sha":"b30fdc68241723ff7c3d68dff048c1cc1465beaf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/git/trees/b30fdc68241723ff7c3d68dff048c1cc1465beaf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/git/commits/272401ed7b7c25e3d5d2d077b06a978bede5a215","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commit/272401ed7b7c25e3d5d2d077b06a978bede5a215","node_id":"C_kwDOTQKyJdoAKDI3MjQwMWVkN2I3YzI1ZTNkNWQyZDA3N2IwNmE5NzhiZWRlNWEyMTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commit/3b439b593bfb7c7bdbda4b6538ea5690a05c6d16","sha":"3b439b593bfb7c7bdbda4b6538ea5690a05c6d16","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commits/3b439b593bfb7c7bdbda4b6538ea5690a05c6d16"}],"sha":"272401ed7b7c25e3d5d2d077b06a978bede5a215","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commits/272401ed7b7c25e3d5d2d077b06a978bede5a215"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/107689613?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vincenzo-Verma/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://ap