yNzkwZTJlYTcwYjUzNjFhMmFmMDc0N2VjMzc0MzBiMGFhNzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commit/254784c9e3151ea65ac82b76df91817e372108a0","sha":"254784c9e3151ea65ac82b76df91817e372108a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commits/254784c9e3151ea65ac82b76df91817e372108a0"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commit/64354c3da2d2bd47c5f1a6b9fff00f4e98970a9a","sha":"64354c3da2d2bd47c5f1a6b9fff00f4e98970a9a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commits/64354c3da2d2bd47c5f1a6b9fff00f4e98970a9a"}],"sha":"87472790e2ea70b5361a2af0747ec37430b0aa78","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commits/87472790e2ea70b5361a2af0747ec37430b0aa78"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commits/254784c9e3151ea65ac82b76df91817e372108a0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-01T15:31:36Z","email":"usk.rs.verma@gmail.com","name":"vincenzo-verma"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-01T15:31:36Z","email":"usk.rs.verma@gmail.com","name":"vincenzo-verma"},"message":"fix(auth): prevent password value exposure in DOM and improve form security","tree":{"sha":"36fd33ebabb62b5329daa02d90fcbda683b22a39","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/git/trees/36fd33ebabb62b5329daa02d90fcbda683b22a39"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/git/commits/254784c9e3151ea65ac82b76df91817e372108a0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commit/254784c9e3151ea65ac82b76df91817e372108a0","node_id":"C_kwDOTQKyJdoAKDI1NDc4NGM5ZTMxNTFlYTY1YWM4MmI3NmRmOTE4MTdlMzcyMTA4YTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commit/05c314abeddd0e828ea7478a800849d6574fed8f","sha":"05c314abeddd0e828ea7478a800849d6574fed8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commits/05c314abeddd0e828ea7478a800849d6574fed8f"}],"sha":"254784c9e3151ea65ac82b76df91817e372108a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commits/254784c9e3151ea65ac82b76df91817e372108a0"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commits/05c314abeddd0e828ea7478a800849d6574fed8f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-01T08:39:33Z","email":"usk.rs.verma@gmail.com","name":"vincenzo-verma"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-01T08:39:33Z","email":"usk.rs.verma@gmail.com","name":"vincenzo-verma"},"message":"feat: verified-email gate, manual grant visibility, plan-change mail\n\nPublisher email verification becomes a real precondition rather than a\nflag nobody read, and manually granted plans become visible to the\npublisher.\n\nManual grants (a)\n- billing-platform status now reads manual_since/manual_until and returns\n  subscription_source (''razorpay'' | ''manual'' | ''none''). has_subscription is\n  unchanged for back-compat.\n- PlatformBillingPage picks the current tier from that discriminator instead\n  of the has_subscription approximation, which highlighted Free for every\n  granted plan. Cancel/refund stays Razorpay-only: a grant has nothing to\n  refund.\n\nPlan-change mail (b, c)\n- New internal /internal/billing/platform/:slug/plan-change, called from the\n  admin worker on grant, extend, deactivate and the expiry sweep. Each call\n  is catch-guarded: the grant is the operation of record, the mail is not.\n- Senders canonicalised: noreply@payments.epaperspace.com system to\n  publisher, noreply-<slug>@payments.epaperspace.com publisher to reader.\n\nVerification, diagnosis and repair (d)\n- readOwner/writeOwner and profile''s loadOwner no longer trust tenants.status\n  to say where the owner row lives. Live data disagreed in both directions:\n  an active tenant with an empty org_users but a verified pending_owners row,\n  and an active tenant whose D1 had no binding in any worker. Both made the\n  lookup report \"no account\", which swallowed the mail silently.\n- writeOwner now checks meta.changes. A zero-row UPDATE used to answer 200\n  while leaving email_verified = 0, so confirming a link appeared to work and\n  left the publisher blocked with nothing to retry.\n- validate-bindings.js gained --live: it only ever compared the three workers\n  to each other, so a tenant missing from all three passed. It immediately\n  found epaper-test2-ffdd bound nowhere.\n- inject-binding.js splices text instead of round-tripping JSON, which was\n  deleting every comment in the .jsonc files on each provision.\n\nResend and status in the portal (e, f, h)\n- Authenticated POST /api/auth/verify-email/resend. Unlike the public send\n  route it may report what happened (409 verified, 429 throttled, 500 failed)\n  because the caller is known. The public route keeps its generic body.\n- VerifyEmailBanner renders on Papers and Settings, resends the link, and adds\n  an address when the account has none.\n\nWrite gate (g)\n- requireVerifiedEmail on the six content write routes. Reads org_users per\n  request, never a JWT claim, so verifying in one tab unblocks an upload in\n  the other without re-login. Fails open on a missing row, absent binding or\n  D1 error and closed only on an address that is present and unverified;\n  phone-only accounts are never blocked.\n- ensureOrgUser now binds email_verified explicitly. It defaulted to 0 from\n  inside a route the fail-open guard had just allowed, locking the account out\n  of every later write, permanently on the synthetic-address path.\n\nAdd-and-verify an address (i)\n- POST /api/auth/add-email for Google/OTP accounts that arrive without one.\n  Always stores email_verified = 0 whatever the caller claims, 409s on a\n  tenant-level or org_users clash, and mails the link.\n\nVerify before provisioning\n- A password signup holds at ''pending'' and provisions only once the link is\n  opened, so no D1 or R2 is created for an unconfirmed address. Google and\n  phone identities are already verified and provision immediately.\n- /provision-status reports awaiting_verification so the portal can show the\n  confirm-your-email step, and /reprovision refuses to be the way around it.","tree":{"sha":"a0d9335b8e301fed5fc6486d35871619c2e81cfb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/git/trees/a0d9335b8e301fed5fc6486d35871619c2e81cfb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/git/commits/05c314abeddd0e828ea7478a800849d6574fed8f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commit/05c314abeddd0e828ea7478a800849d6574fed8f","node_id":"C_kwDOTQKyJdoAKDA1YzMxNGFiZWRkZDBlODI4ZWE3NDc4YTgwMDg0OWQ2NTc0ZmVkOGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commit/ba70acbccc7ea57dc765385c99444911c28aba21","sha":"ba70acbccc7ea57dc765385c99444911c28aba21","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commits/ba70acbccc7ea57dc765385c99444911c28aba21"}],"sha":"05c314abeddd0e828ea7478a800849d6574fed8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commits/05c314abeddd0e828ea7478a800849d6574fed8f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","id":41898282,"login":"github-actions[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com