api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commits/d6785befa6a0bdb45c85df9c5a73902e7df7d530"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commits/782f2ed3503ae5dcbd8662c11bcb113ef107e6f2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-31T12:32:28Z","email":"usk.rs.verma@gmail.com","name":"vincenzo-verma"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-31T12:35:13Z","email":"usk.rs.verma@gmail.com","name":"vincenzo-verma"},"message":"fix: stop runtime DDL colliding with migration 0013, cache grant ALTERs\n\nensurePlatformConfig''s CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS declared sms_daily_cap and\nsms_disabled, the same two columns migration 0013 adds via ALTER TABLE ADD\nCOLUMN. On a fresh control DB where the admin worker is hit before migrations\napply, the runtime path creates the table with those columns and 0013''s ADD\nCOLUMN then throws, failing the migration. One owner per column: drop them\nfrom the runtime CREATE so either path can run first and the other no-ops.\n\nensureGrantColumns ran four throw-and-ignore ALTERs on every grant request.\nGuard it with a WeakSet keyed on the D1 binding so it runs once per binding\nper isolate.","tree":{"sha":"c3eb7e70194cb41b6c264f3319798d9892b6a3ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/git/trees/c3eb7e70194cb41b6c264f3319798d9892b6a3ea"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/git/commits/782f2ed3503ae5dcbd8662c11bcb113ef107e6f2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commit/782f2ed3503ae5dcbd8662c11bcb113ef107e6f2","node_id":"C_kwDOTQKyJdoAKDc4MmYyZWQzNTAzYWU1ZGNiZDg2NjJjMTFiY2IxMTNlZjEwN2U2ZjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commit/b640051ddef9426d96a770399af523cce6b869bb","sha":"b640051ddef9426d96a770399af523cce6b869bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/com