age":"fix: address review feedback on grants UI, SMS cap and ABAC fallbacks\n\nCo-authored-by: Codesmith <codesmith-bot@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"4ccf53c5645117504015d5c1e8049c757f425842","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/git/trees/4ccf53c5645117504015d5c1e8049c757f425842"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/git/commits/059ccd45ad643a0837e9c5ff8cca93074ca90d75","verification":{"payload":"tree 4ccf53c5645117504015d5c1e8049c757f425842\nparent 2414892caffcfe9310a2fb0ba08ae29e61d07c73\nauthor esoteric-dev <utk.rs.verma01@gmail.com> 1785497082 +0000\ncommitter Codesmith <codesmith-bot@users.noreply.github.com> 1785497082 +0000\n\nfix: address review feedback on grants UI, SMS cap and ABAC fallbacks\n\nCo-authored-by: Codesmith <codesmith-bot@users.noreply.github.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgfqe1ojOsTxGRWUfWHotYsmAlli\nP8UTpUhcX/Er5IiNQAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQB93xils6nlMjnT0HCBIA3gNSL0d426NMo2et00uvxRUF/5Hrgq1ZoCasHKHKs1k/y\nkhqra7ZovW2mGrNWZAogM=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-31T11:24:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/267743959?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codesmith-bot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codesmith-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codesmith-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codesmith-bot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/codesmith-bot","id":267743959,"login":"codesmith-bot","node_id":"U_kgDOD_Vy1w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codesmith-bot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codesmith-bot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codesmith-bot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codesmith-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codesmith-bot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/codesmith-bot","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commit/059ccd45ad643a0837e9c5ff8cca93074ca90d75","node_id":"C_kwDOTQKyJdoAKDA1OWNjZDQ1YWQ2NDNhMDgzN2U5YzVmZjhjY2E5MzA3NGNhOTBkNzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commit/2414892caffcfe9310a2fb0ba08ae29e61d07c73","sha":"2414892caffcfe9310a2fb0ba08ae29e61d07c73","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commits/2414892caffcfe9310a2fb0ba08ae29e61d07c73"}],"sha":"059ccd45ad643a0837e9c5ff8cca93074ca90d75","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commits/059ccd45ad643a0837e9c5ff8cca93074ca90d75"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/utility-crm/epaper-crm/commits/2414892caffcfe9310a2fb0ba08ae29e61d07c73/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-31T07:12:20Z","email":"usk.rs.verma@gmail.com","name":"vincenzo-verma"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-31T11:05:24Z","email":"usk.rs.verma@gmail.com","name":"vincenzo-verma"},"message":"feat: manual subscription grants, renewal mail, SMS cap, ABAC\n\nFixes the reported bug where signing up with email + password sent no\nverification mail, plus the eight follow-on asks tracked in the plan.\n\nVerification mail (root cause): sendAuthMail returned false on a missing\nRESEND_API_KEY or a non-2xx from Resend, and every caller discarded the\nboolean, so the failure died silently through waitUntil. It now throws, so\nall callers log a real error. /verify-email/send and /password-reset/request\nstill return the generic GENERIC_SEND body on failure -- leaking send\nsuccess would enumerate accounts. The resend gate no longer requires\npassword_hash, which Firebase-created publishers do not have.\n\nManual grants: reader_subscriptions gains grant_type, granted_by,\ngrant_note and renewal_notified_at. Superadmin (via a service binding from\nthe admin worker) and publisher staff (via their portal JWT) both route\nthrough admin-grants.ts, so a grant made in either console is the same row\nand shows up in the other. Razorpay-lane rows stay read-only in both UIs\nbecause the mandate owns those dates. Manual rows carry a synthetic\nmanual:<uuid> in razorpay_sub_id, which is UNIQUE NOT NULL and cannot be\nrelaxed without rebuilding the table in every tenant DB.\n\nExpiry and renewal: a half-hourly cron expires whatever is past\ncurrent_end in both lanes and mails a warning three days out.\nrenewal_notified_at is the per-term idempotency guard and is only stamped\non a successful send, so a transient Resend failure retries next tick.\nRenewal notices come from noreply@payments.epaperspace.com.\n\nDatetimes are UTC end to end. datetime-local carries no zone, so the worker\npins a bare value to UTC rather than guessing, and both UIs label the\nfields accordingly. Comparisons use datetime(substr(current_end,1,19)),\nwhich trims to ''YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS''. SQLite 3.42.0+ parses the Z suffix\ndirectly, so that is portability for older builds rather than a fix; it is\nsafe only because every writer uses toISOString().\n\nSMS abuse control: a platform-wide kill switch and a per-tenant daily cap,\nboth enforced before the billable audit row is written. tenant_id is now\nresolved from CONTROL_DB by slug instead of taken from the request body,\nwhere a caller could pick whose budget it spent.\n\nABAC: an optional permissions array on org_users, spread into the portal\nJWT. An explicit array is authoritative; without one the check falls back\nto role, so existing owners and admins keep what they had. The client-side\ncheck only hides buttons -- the worker still decides.\n\nDeactivating a grant stops new page tokens at once, but already-issued HMAC\npage tokens stay valid for up to their 6h TTL. Surfaced as operator-facing\ncopy in both c