d_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chan-c-gt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chan-c-gt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/chan-c-gt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oscar-melendez77/PharmaWatch/commits/8a67be2ea421412850cd20e82970b066fe95a0cc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-08T01:17:20Z","email":"ojosue.morantes@gmail.com","name":"Oscar Melendez"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-08T01:17:20Z","email":"ojosue.morantes@gmail.com","name":"Oscar Melendez"},"message":"Redesign dashboard: Swiss Grid (cool, no brown)\n\nReplace the warm-paper dossier with a cool International/Swiss-typographic\nsystem: white background, near-black ink, a single red accent, Archivo grotesque\n+ IBM Plex Mono, a strict asymmetric grid (numbered 01-08 sections with a left\nnumber rail), huge tabular display numerals, hairline rules and generous\nwhitespace. Data-forward hero (giant top-risk %), key-figures as big-number\ngrid, monochrome+red charts with black outlines. Zero brown anywhere.\n\nCarries forward every fix from the prior review: WCAG-safe text, no emoji (red\n■ marks), friendly SHAP labels, honest sample framing, correct drug vocabulary,\nrisk colour key + colour-blind scatter outline, all-ink AUC, value labels on all\nbar figures, .table-wrap mobile scroll, scroll-padding for the sticky nav.","tree":{"sha":"2206f67edc4b8ff131ae518ba084f1aad9dafd16","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oscar-melendez77/PharmaWatch/git/trees/2206f67edc4b8ff131ae518ba084f1aad9dafd16"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oscar-melendez77/PharmaWatch/git/commits/8a67be2ea421412850cd20e82970b066fe95a0cc","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/293155173?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chan-c-gt/events{/privacy}","fol