/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-14T16:53:38Z","email":"shivsingh6371913458@gmail.com","name":"sumitsingh4411"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-14T16:53:38Z","email":"shivsingh6371913458@gmail.com","name":"sumitsingh4411"},"message":"Topic deep dives: 105 more across 7 sections + engine fix\n\nRolls the deep-dive treatment out across Fundamentals, Browser, JavaScript,\nTypeScript, CSS, React and Next.js. 113 of 383 topic rows now have a staff-level\ndeep dive; the section tables link to them and the sidebar reveals them.\n\nWritten in parallel by subagents against a shared authoring brief (same 7-part\nanatomy, staff-engineer quality bar, original prose only). The run was cut short by\nan account session limit, but every file on disk is complete and correctly slugged\n(validated: 7/7 required headings, TL;DR, Go-deeper, no orphans). Remaining 270\ntopics follow after the limit resets.\n\nEngine fix: the deep-dive ''Primary source'' card assumed the table''s Best Resources\nlink was always external. Some rows point at a repo-relative page (e.g. React''s\n''Virtualization'' row -> the build-a-virtualized-list flagship); those now resolve to\ntheir on-site route instead of rendering a dead .md link. Falls back to the GitHub\nblob URL when a repo path has no published route.\n\nTests: pilot/search/sidebar assertions made robust (no hardcoded pilot counts) so\nthey survive the corpus growing. 25 unit, 77 e2e green. 0 dead links, 0 orphans.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"82e611cec1d9b011e8ada6d7d6357813d54e6af9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sumitsingh4411/frontend-interview-questions/git/trees/82e611cec1d9b011e8ada6d7d6357813d54e6af9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sumitsingh4411/frontend-interview-questions/git/commits/1b2dbed96b671345242cda6b42b1772da805a609","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_u